      `a statement in lieu of prospectus has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a statement in lieu of prospectus has been lodged with the Registrar?
      `the statement in lieu of prospectus complies with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement in lieu of prospectus complies with the requirements of this Act?
      `the day the statement in lieu of prospectus was lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the statement in lieu of prospectus lodged?
      `the day of the first allotment of either shares or debentures` IS A DATE @desc On what day was, or will be, the first allotment of either shares or debentures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 59(1), is the company barred from allotting shares or debentures` IS
    `s 59(1) the company is barred from allotting shares or debentures` `the company is a public company` `the company has a share capital` `the company issued a prospectus on or with reference to its formation` `a statement in lieu of prospectus has been lodged with the Registrar` `the statement in lieu of prospectus complies with the requirements of this Act` `the day the statement in lieu of prospectus was lodged` `the day of the first allotment of either shares or debentures`

@export Under section 59(2), am I guilty of the offence of default?
