§ `Section 60: the statement in lieu of prospectus`

-- Asked by a director who signs, or an expert or other person who deals with, a statement in lieu of prospectus.

@export Under section 60(1), does the statement in lieu of prospectus meet the three requirements of the subsection?
GIVEN `the number of persons named in the statement as a director or a proposed director` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons are named in the statement as a director or a proposed director?
      `the number of those persons who have signed the statement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those persons have signed the statement?
      `the number of those persons for whom an agent authorised in writing has signed the statement` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many of those persons has an agent authorised in writing signed the statement?
      `the statement is in the form of Part 1 of the Sixth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement in the form of Part 1 of the Sixth Schedule?
      `the statement states the matters specified in Part 1 of the Sixth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the matters specified in Part 1 of the Sixth Schedule?
      `the statement sets out the reports specified in Part 2 of the Sixth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement set out the reports specified in Part 2 of the Sixth Schedule?
      `the persons making a report specified in Part 2 have made adjustments in it, or have indicated adjustments in it without giving the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the persons making a report specified in Part 2 have made adjustments in it, or have indicated adjustments in it without giving the reasons?
      `a written statement signed by those persons setting out the adjustments and giving the reasons is endorsed on or attached to the statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a written statement signed by those persons setting out the adjustments and giving the reasons is endorsed on or attached to the statement in lieu of prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 60(1), does the statement in lieu of prospectus meet the three requirements of the subsection` IS
    `s 60(1) the statement in lieu of prospectus meets the three requirements of subsection (1)` (`s 60(1)(a) the statement in lieu of prospectus is signed as the paragraph requires` `the number of persons named in the statement as a director or a proposed director` `the number of those persons who have signed the statement` `the number of those persons for whom an agent authorised in writing has signed the statement`) (`s 60(1)(b) the statement in lieu of prospectus is in the form and has the contents the paragraph requires` `the statement is in the form of Part 1 of the Sixth Schedule` `the statement states the matters specified in Part 1 of the Sixth Schedule` `the statement sets out the reports specified in Part 2 of the Sixth Schedule`) (`s 60(1)(c) the statement in lieu of prospectus has the written statement of adjustments the paragraph requires` `the persons making a report specified in Part 2 have made adjustments in it, or have indicated adjustments in it without giving the reasons` `a written statement signed by those persons setting out the adjustments and giving the reasons is endorsed on or attached to the statement in lieu of prospectus`)

@export Under section 60(3), am I, as a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus, guilty of the offence of an untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure in it?
GIVEN `the person is a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus?
      `a statement in the statement in lieu of prospectus is untrue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a statement in the statement in lieu of prospectus is untrue?
      `the statement in question is misleading in the form and context in which it is included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement in question misleading in the form and context in which it is included?
      `the statement in lieu of prospectus contains a wilful non-disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement in lieu of prospectus contain a wilful non-disclosure?
      `the director proves that the untrue statement or non-disclosure was immaterial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you, as the director, prove that the untrue statement or non-disclosure was immaterial?
      `the director proves that the director had reasonable ground to believe that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you, as the director, prove that you had reasonable ground to believe that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial?
      `the director did believe, up to the time of the delivery for registration of the statement in lieu of prospectus, that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, as the director, believe up to the time of the delivery for registration of the statement in lieu of prospectus that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 60(3), am I, as a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus, guilty of the offence of an untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure in it` IS
    `s 60(3) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person is a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus` (`s 60(3) the statement in lieu of prospectus contains an untrue statement` `a statement in the statement in lieu of prospectus is untrue` `the statement in question is misleading in the form and context in which it is included` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the statement in lieu of prospectus contains a wilful non-disclosure` (`s 60(3) the section gives the director a defence on these facts` `the director proves that the untrue statement or non-disclosure was immaterial` `the director proves that the director had reasonable ground to believe that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial` `the director did believe, up to the time of the delivery for registration of the statement in lieu of prospectus, that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

