GIVEN `it is proposed to acquire shares in a corporation which by reason of the acquisition or anything to be done in consequence or in connection with it will become a subsidiary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is proposed to acquire shares in a corporation which by reason of the acquisition or anything to be done in consequence or in connection with it will become a subsidiary of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 Part 2 paragraph 2(1), is a report required on the acquisition of shares in a corporation that becomes a subsidiary` IS
    `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) a report is required` `it is proposed to acquire shares in a corporation which by reason of the acquisition or anything to be done in consequence or in connection with it will become a subsidiary of the company`

@export Under schedule 6 Part 3 paragraph 4, how many financial years must a report deal with?
GIVEN `the business, corporation or limited liability partnership has been carrying on business for less than 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the business, corporation or limited liability partnership has been carrying on business for less than 3 years?
      `the number of years for which its accounts have been made up` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years have its accounts been made up?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 Part 3 paragraph 4, how many financial years must a report deal with` IS
    `sch 6 Part 3 para 4 the number of financial years a report must deal with` `the business, corporation or limited liability partnership has been carrying on business for less than 3 years` `the number of years for which its accounts have been made up`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sga2 (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force from 6 May 2026 to 20 October 2026 -- sections 76 and 76A.
-- THE SEAT LAYER (layer 2). SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- incorporated under the Act, or who deals with one. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's
-- management or ownership. There is never a seat for the Registrar, the Minister, the Authority or the Court: their powers appear only as what they mean to the person.)
--
-- Every question calls one layer-1 rule of sga2-*.l4 and nothing else; no rule is restated here. Each takes plain inputs: yes/no, numbers, dates, a list of public
-- holidays, or the choice of one of the modules' own lists. Each input is named for the fact it states and carries an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- A fact keeps the same name and the same @desc in every question that asks it. The @desc of a yes/no input is generated from its name by a fixed rule
-- (work/desc.py: the first auxiliary verb opens the question) and a few are reworded by hand where the rule reads badly.
-- Every question's name begins "Under section N," with the Act's own numbering, and asks in the direction of the rule it calls: where the rule is a bar ("bars",
-- "barred", "guilty") the question asks whether the bar applies; where the rule is a permission ("does not prohibit", "may") the question asks whether it holds.
-- NOTHING in an answer means the text says nothing on those facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sga2)").
--
-- Shared inputs. `the company is a private company` is the keel's shared seat input: the seat works out "public company" by s 4(1) of the keel (sg-definitions),
-- taking "the body is a company" as TRUE (assumed). `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` is the keel's seam input (PLAN section 4A).
-- PLAN.md section 7 (the seat names every part shares) is missing from this agent's copy of PLAN.md; the two names above are the ones section 4 and section 3 fix.
-- Records the rules expect (the `Solvency statement` of s 7A) are built inside the question, in its WHERE, from the person's answers; no field is left unasked.
-- A DATE that a question needs only for one branch is still asked; the @desc says what to give when the branch does not arise.
-- The public holidays are a list of dates because the Act counts "business days" against them (s 4(1) "business day").

§ `Companies Act 1967 -- sections 76 and 76A: questions of a director, secretary, member or person dealing with a company`

-- Input adapter, not a rule: the person's yes or no for a paragraph of section 76(10) becomes the answer the route function takes.
GIVEN `the requirement is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 76(10), the answer a paragraph gives when the person says whether it is complied with` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is complied with` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE


§§ `Section 76(1) to (4): the prohibition on a company giving financial assistance (public companies and companies with a public holding company)`

@export Under section 76(1), is the company one the subsection binds?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `the holding company of the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding company of the company a public company? (Answer no if it has none.)
      `the ultimate holding company of the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ultimate holding company of the company a public company? (Answer no if it has none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76(1), is the company one the subsection binds` IS
    `s 76(1) the company is one the subsection binds` (`s 4(1) "public company" the company is a public company` TRUE `the company is a private company` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the holding company of the company is a public company` `the ultimate holding company of the company is a public company`

@export Under section 76(1), does subsection (1) bar the company from giving the financial assistance?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `the holding company of the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding company of the company a public company? (Answer no if it has none.)
      `the ultimate holding company of the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ultimate holding company of the company a public company? (Answer no if it has none.)
      `the company gives, or has given, financial assistance, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company gives, or has given, financial assistance, directly or indirectly?
      `the assistance is for the purpose of the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assistance for the purpose of the acquisition?
      `the assistance is in connection with the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assistance in connection with the acquisition?
      `the company is taken by subsection (3) or (4) to have given the assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company taken by subsection (3) or (4) to have given the assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, the acquisition?
      `the acquisition took place before or at the same time as the giving of the financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the acquisition took place before or at the same time as the giving of the financial assistance?
      `the acquisition was proposed when the financial assistance was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the acquisition proposed when the financial assistance was given?
      `the shares or units of shares are shares or units of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares or units of shares shares or units of shares in the company?
      `the shares or units of shares are shares or units of shares in a holding company or ultimate holding company of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares or units of shares shares or units of shares in a holding company or ultimate holding company of the company?
      `an exception expressly provided by this Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an exception expressly provided by the Act apply to what the company did?
      `section 76 does not apply to the act under subsection (17)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act one to which section 76 does not apply under subsection (17) (done under a contract entered into before 15 May 1987 and lawful apart from this Act)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76(1), does subsection (1) bar the company from giving the financial assistance` IS
    `s 76(1) subsection (1) bars the company from giving the financial assistance` (`s 4(1) "public company" the company is a public company` TRUE `the company is a private company` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the holding company of the company is a public company` `the ultimate holding company of the company is a public company` `the company gives, or has given, financial assistance, directly or indirectly` `the assistance is for the purpose of the acquisition` `the assistance is in connection with the acquisition` `the company is taken by subsection (3) or (4) to have given the assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, the acquisition` `the acquisition took place before or at the same time as the giving of the financial assistance` `the acquisition was proposed when the financial assistance was given` `the shares or units of shares are shares or units of shares in the company` `the shares or units of shares are shares or units of shares in a holding company or ultimate holding company of the company` `an exception expressly provided by this Act applies` `section 76 does not apply to the act under subsection (17)`

@export Under section 76(1)(a), is the acquisition one that paragraph (a) names?
GIVEN `the acquisition took place before or at the same time as the giving of the financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the acquisition took place before or at the same time as the giving of the financial assistance?
      `the shares or units of shares are shares or units of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares or units of shares shares or units of shares in the company?
      `the shares or units of shares are shares or units of shares in a holding company or ultimate holding company of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares or units of shares shares or units of shares in a holding company or ultimate holding company of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76(1)(a), is the acquisition one that paragraph (a) names` IS
    `s 76(1)(a) the acquisition is one that paragraph (a) names` `the acquisition took place before or at the same time as the giving of the financial assistance` `the shares or units of shares are shares or units of shares in the company` `the shares or units of shares are shares or units of shares in a holding company or ultimate holding company of the company`

@export Under section 76(1)(b), is the proposed acquisition one that paragraph (b) names?
GIVEN `the acquisition was proposed when the financial assistance was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the acquisition proposed when the financial assistance was given?
      `the shares or units of shares are shares or units of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares or units of shares shares or units of shares in the company?
      `the shares or units of shares are shares or units of shares in a holding company or ultimate holding company of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares or units of shares shares or units of shares in a holding company or ultimate holding company of the company?
