§ `Section 78D: the creditor's right to object`
-- Arises only where the company has passed a special resolution to reduce its share capital under section 78B or 78C.

@export Under section 78D(2), may the creditor apply to the Court for the resolution to be cancelled?
GIVEN `the company has passed a special resolution for reducing share capital under section 78B or 78C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company passed a special resolution for reducing share capital under section 78B or 78C?
      `the creditor, at the date of the creditor's application to the Court, is entitled to a debt or claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the creditor, at the date of the creditor's application to the Court, is entitled to a debt or claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company?
      `the resolution date` IS A DATE @desc What is the resolution date?
      `the date of the creditor's application to the Court` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the creditor's application to the Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78D(2), may the creditor apply to the Court for the resolution to be cancelled` IS
    `s 78D(2) the creditor may apply to the Court for the resolution to be cancelled` `the company has passed a special resolution for reducing share capital under section 78B or 78C` `the creditor, at the date of the creditor's application to the Court, is entitled to a debt or claim which, if that date were the commencement of the winding up of the company, would be admissible in proof against the company` `the resolution date` `the date of the creditor's application to the Court`

