@export Under section 148(1), is an undischarged bankrupt who acts as director of, or takes part in the management of, a corporation without permission guilty of an offence?
GIVEN `the person is an undischarged bankrupt, whether adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an undischarged bankrupt, whether adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy?
      `the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency?
      `the person acts as director of, or directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of, a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acts as director of, or directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of, a corporation?
      `the person has the permission of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has the permission of the Court?
      `the person has the written permission of the Official Assignee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has the written permission of the Official Assignee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 148(1), is an undischarged bankrupt who acts as director of, or takes part in the management of, a corporation without permission guilty of an offence` IS
    `s 148(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person is an undischarged bankrupt, whether adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy` `the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` `the person acts as director of, or directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of, a corporation` `the person has the permission of the Court` `the person has the written permission of the Official Assignee`

@export Under section 148(1), what is the most an undischarged bankrupt may be penalised on conviction for acting as director without permission?
GIVEN `the person is an undischarged bankrupt, whether adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an undischarged bankrupt, whether adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy?
      `the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency?
      `the person acts as director of, or directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of, a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acts as director of, or directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of, a corporation?
      `the person has the permission of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has the permission of the Court?
      `the person has the written permission of the Official Assignee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has the written permission of the Official Assignee?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 148(1) penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 148(1), what is the most an undischarged bankrupt may be penalised on conviction for acting as director without permission` IS
    `s 148(1) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` `the person is an undischarged bankrupt, whether adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy` `the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` `the person acts as director of, or directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of, a corporation` `the person has the permission of the Court` `the person has the written permission of the Official Assignee`

@export Under section 148(2), may the Court or the Official Assignee refuse an undischarged bankrupt's application for permission, or approve it subject to conditions?
GIVEN `the application is by an undischarged bankrupt under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is by an undischarged bankrupt under subsection (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 148(2), may the Court or the Official Assignee refuse an undischarged bankrupt's application for permission, or approve it subject to conditions` IS
    `s 148(2) the Court or the Official Assignee may refuse the application or approve it subject to conditions` `the application is by an undischarged bankrupt under subsection (1)`

