§ `Section 155C: disqualification under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`

@export Under section 155C(1), is a person subject to a disqualification under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 barred from acting as a director or taking part in the management of a company?
GIVEN `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` IS A `s 155C ground` @desc Which applies: the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005?
      `the Court has given the person permission under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has given the person permission under subsection (3)?
      `the date asked is within the period of disqualification or disqualification order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the date asked is within the period of disqualification or disqualification order?
      `the body is a company, or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the body is a company, or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 155C(1), is a person subject to a disqualification under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 barred from acting as a director or taking part in the management of a company` IS
    `s 155C(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` `the Court has given the person permission under subsection (3)` `the date asked is within the period of disqualification or disqualification order` `the body is a company, or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies`

@export Under section 155C(2), is a person who contravenes section 155C(1) guilty of an offence?
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 155C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person contravenes section 155C(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 155C(2), is a person who contravenes section 155C(1) guilty of an offence` IS
    `s 155C(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person contravenes section 155C(1)`

@export Under section 155C(2), what is the most a person may be penalised on conviction for contravening section 155C(1)?
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 155C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person contravenes section 155C(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 155C(2) penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 155C(2), what is the most a person may be penalised on conviction for contravening section 155C(1)` IS
    `s 155C(2) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` `the person contravenes section 155C(1)`

@export Under section 155C(3), may a person subject to such a disqualification apply to the Court for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company?
GIVEN `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` IS A `s 155C ground` @desc Which applies: the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005?
      `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply?
      `the date the person applies to the Court` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the person applies to the Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 155C(3), may a person subject to such a disqualification apply to the Court for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` IS
    `s 155C(3) the person may apply to the Court for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` `the ground on which the person is subject to a disqualification or disqualification order under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` `the date the person applies to the Court`

@export Under section 155C(4), may the Minister be represented at the hearing and oppose the granting of the application?
GIVEN `the hearing is of an application under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the hearing is of an application under subsection (3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 155C(4), may the Minister be represented at the hearing and oppose the granting of the application` IS
    `s 155C(4) the Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application` `the hearing is of an application under subsection (3)`


