-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sgb2 (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 6 May 2026 to 20 October 2026 -- ss 161 to 173I -- THE SEAT LAYER (part sgb2).
-- This is a rendering of the Act's text, not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member of a company incorporated under the Act, or who deals with one: what the Act requires or lets them do, what they must
-- disclose, file or give and by when, what the company or the Registrar must do about them, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. There is never a seat for the Registrar, the Minister,
-- the Authority or the Court: their powers appear only as what they mean to the person.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the part's layer-1 modules as questions that person would ask. Nothing here is new law. Every question's name begins "Under section N,".
-- READING AN ANSWER. A question answers JUST TRUE ("yes, as the question is put"), JUST FALSE ("no: the text itself says no to that case") or NOTHING ("the text does not answer it", never read as no). A question
-- that asks about a bar or an offence ("is the company barred", "is the person guilty") says yes when the bar or the offence applies; a question that asks about a permission or a duty says yes when it is granted or owed.
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Each question takes yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices, one per fact the person can state. The records the modules expect (the section 7 facts) are built inside the question, in its WHERE.
-- What a question leaves out is named at the question or in NOTES.md (Seams).

§ `Companies Act 1967, ss 161 to 173I -- the questions of a director, secretary, member or officer`

§§ `Section 161: approval of the company for the directors to issue shares`

@export Under section 161(1), are the directors barred from exercising the company's power to issue shares?
GIVEN `the company has given its prior approval in general meeting for the directors to exercise the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company, in general meeting, given its prior approval for the directors to exercise its power to issue shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161(1), are the directors barred from exercising the company's power to issue shares` IS
    `s 161(1) the section bars the directors from exercising the power of the company to issue shares` `the company has given its prior approval in general meeting for the directors to exercise the power`

@export Under section 161(3), is the company's approval for the directors to issue shares in force on that day?
GIVEN `the date the approval was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company in general meeting give its approval?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether the approval is in force?
      `the date the next annual general meeting commencing after the approval was given concludes` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the annual general meeting commencing next after the approval was given conclude?
      `the last day of the period within which the next annual general meeting after that date is required by law to be held` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period within which that next annual general meeting is required by law to be held?
      `the company in general meeting revoked the approval before the day asked about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company in general meeting revoke the approval before that day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161(3), is the company's approval for the directors to issue shares in force on that day` IS
    `s 161(3) the approval is in force on the day` `the date the approval was given` `the day asked about` `the date the next annual general meeting commencing after the approval was given concludes` `the last day of the period within which the next annual general meeting after that date is required by law to be held` `the company in general meeting revoked the approval before the day asked about`

@export Under section 161(6), is an issue of shares made in contravention of the section void?
GIVEN `the issue of shares was made by the company in contravention of section 161` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the issue of shares made without the prior approval section 161 requires (that is, in contravention of the section)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161(6), is an issue of shares made in contravention of the section void` IS
    `s 161(6) the issue of shares is void` `the issue of shares was made by the company in contravention of section 161`

@export Under section 161(7), is the director liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued?
GIVEN `the director knowingly contravened section 161 with respect to the issue of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly contravene section 161 in the issue of the shares?
      `the director permitted the contravention of section 161 with respect to the issue of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you permit the contravention?
      `the director authorised the contravention of section 161 with respect to the issue of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161(7), is the director liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued` IS
    `s 161(7) the director is liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued` `the director knowingly contravened section 161 with respect to the issue of shares` `the director permitted the contravention of section 161 with respect to the issue of shares` `the director authorised the contravention of section 161 with respect to the issue of shares`

@export Under section 161(7), do the 2 years after the issue of the shares bar proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs?
GIVEN `the date of the issue of the shares` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares issued?
      `the date the proceedings are commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date were (or will) the proceedings be commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161(7), do the 2 years after the issue of the shares bar proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs` IS
    `s 161(7) the 2 years bar the proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs` `the date of the issue of the shares` `the date the proceedings are commenced`

§§ `Section 162: loans and similar dealings with directors`

@export Under section 162(2), is the company barred from making the restricted transaction?
GIVEN `the company is an exempt private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company an exempt private company?
      `the transaction is within an exception in section 162(3) and (4) or in section 163A or 163B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction within one of the exceptions in section 162(3) and (4), or in section 163A or 163B?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 162(2), is the company barred from making the restricted transaction` IS
    `s 162(2) the section bars the company from making the restricted transaction` `the company is an exempt private company` `the transaction is within an exception in section 162(3) and (4) or in section 163A or 163B`

@export Under section 162(5), are the directors who authorised the transaction jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss?
GIVEN `the transaction was made on the condition mentioned in subsection (4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction made on the condition that, if the company does not give prior approval at or before the next annual general meeting, the amount or liability must be repaid or discharged within 6 months of that meeting?
      `the prior approval of the company was given at or before the next following annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company give its prior approval at or before that next annual general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 162(5), are the directors who authorised the transaction jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss` IS
    `s 162(5) the directors who authorised the transaction are jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss` `the transaction was made on the condition mentioned in subsection (4)(b)` `the prior approval of the company was given at or before the next following annual general meeting`

@export Under section 162(6), is the director guilty of an offence?
GIVEN `the company contravened section 162` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company contravene section 162?
      `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the making of the restricted transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 162(6), is the director guilty of an offence` IS
    `s 162(6) the director is guilty of the offence` `the company contravened section 162` `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction`

@export Under section 162(6), what is the highest fine the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in Singapore dollars?
GIVEN `the company contravened section 162` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company contravene section 162?
      `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the making of the restricted transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 162(6), what is the highest fine the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in Singapore dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `s 162(6) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` `the company contravened section 162` `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction`
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 162(6) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 162(6), what is the longest term of imprisonment the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in years?
GIVEN `the company contravened section 162` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company contravene section 162?
      `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the making of the restricted transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 162(6), what is the longest term of imprisonment the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in years` IS
    CONSIDER `s 162(6) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` `the company contravened section 162` `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction`
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 162(6) the longest imprisonment, in years`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 162(7), does section 162 operate to prevent the company from recovering the amount?
GIVEN `the amount is owed to the company under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement made contrary to section 162, or is an amount for which the company becomes liable under a guarantee or security given contrary to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount one owed to the company under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement made contrary to section 162, or one the company is liable for under a guarantee or security given contrary to it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 162(7), does section 162 operate to prevent the company from recovering the amount` IS
    `s 162(7) section 162 operates to prevent the company from recovering the amount` `the amount is owed to the company under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement made contrary to section 162, or is an amount for which the company becomes liable under a guarantee or security given contrary to it`

§§ `Sections 163, 163A and 163B: loans and similar dealings connected with directors`

@export Under section 163(1), does the subsection make the dealing unlawful?
GIVEN `the kind of dealing` IS A `s 163(1) kind of dealing` @desc Which kind of dealing is it?
      `the company is an exempt private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company an exempt private company?
      `the interest condition of subsection (1) or of subsections (2) and (3) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest condition met (the director or directors are interested in 20% or more of the voting power of the other company, limited liability partnership or VCC, or subsection (2) and (3) applies)?
      `the thing done is within an exception in subsection (4) or in section 163A or 163B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing done within an exception in subsection (4) or in section 163A or 163B?
      `the prior approval the section requires has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prior approval the section requires been given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 163(1), does the subsection make the dealing unlawful` IS
    `s 163(1) the subsection makes the dealing unlawful` `the kind of dealing` `the company is an exempt private company` `the interest condition of subsection (1) or of subsections (2) and (3) is met` `the thing done is within an exception in subsection (4) or in section 163A or 163B` `the prior approval the section requires has been given`

@export Under section 163(7), is the director guilty of an offence?
GIVEN `the company contravened section 163` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company contravene section 163?
      `the director authorised the making of the loan or quasi-loan, the entering into of the credit transaction, guarantee or arrangement, or the providing of the security, contrary to section 163` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the dealing that contravened section 163?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 163(7), is the director guilty of an offence` IS
    `s 163(7) the director is guilty of the offence` `the company contravened section 163` `the director authorised the making of the loan or quasi-loan, the entering into of the credit transaction, guarantee or arrangement, or the providing of the security, contrary to section 163`

@export Under section 163(7), what is the highest fine the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in Singapore dollars?
GIVEN `the company contravened section 163` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company contravene section 163?
      `the director authorised the making of the loan or quasi-loan, the entering into of the credit transaction, guarantee or arrangement, or the providing of the security, contrary to section 163` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the dealing that contravened section 163?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 163(7), what is the highest fine the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in Singapore dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `s 163(7) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` `the company contravened section 163` `the director authorised the making of the loan or quasi-loan, the entering into of the credit transaction, guarantee or arrangement, or the providing of the security, contrary to section 163`
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 163(7) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 163(7), what is the longest term of imprisonment the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in years?
GIVEN `the company contravened section 163` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company contravene section 163?
      `the director authorised the making of the loan or quasi-loan, the entering into of the credit transaction, guarantee or arrangement, or the providing of the security, contrary to section 163` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the dealing that contravened section 163?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 163(7), what is the longest term of imprisonment the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in years` IS
    CONSIDER `s 163(7) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` `the company contravened section 163` `the director authorised the making of the loan or quasi-loan, the entering into of the credit transaction, guarantee or arrangement, or the providing of the security, contrary to section 163`
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 163(7) the longest imprisonment, in years`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 163(6), does section 163 operate to prevent the recovery of the amount or the enforcement of the guarantee or security?
GIVEN `the amount is owed under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement, or is secured by a guarantee or security, made or given by the company or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount owed under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement, or secured by a guarantee or security, made or given by the company or any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 163(6), does section 163 operate to prevent the recovery of the amount or the enforcement of the guarantee or security` IS
    `s 163(6) section 163 operates to prevent the recovery of the amount or the enforcement of the guarantee or security` `the amount is owed under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement, or is secured by a guarantee or security, made or given by the company or any other person`

@export Under section 163B, is the thing done within the exception from sections 162, 163 and 172?
GIVEN `the company provided a director of the company with funds by way of a loan to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by the director in defending himself or herself in an investigation by a regulatory authority or against any action proposed to be taken by a regulatory authority, in connection with an alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by the director in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company lend a director funds to meet the director's expenditure in defending himself or herself in an investigation by a regulatory authority, or against action proposed by one, over an alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust towards the company?
      `the company did the thing to enable such a director to avoid incurring such expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company do the thing to enable such a director to avoid incurring that expenditure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 163B, is the thing done within the exception from sections 162, 163 and 172` IS
    `s 163B the thing done is within the exception from sections 162, 163 and 172` `the company provided a director of the company with funds by way of a loan to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by the director in defending himself or herself in an investigation by a regulatory authority or against any action proposed to be taken by a regulatory authority, in connection with an alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by the director in relation to the company` `the company did the thing to enable such a director to avoid incurring such expenditure`

§§ `Section 164: the register of directors' and chief executive officers' shareholdings`

@export Under section 164(1), must the company show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings?
GIVEN `the kind of holding` IS A `s 164(1) kind of holding` @desc Which kind of holding is it: shares, debentures or participatory interests, rights or options, contracts to call for or deliver shares, or some other holding?
      `the director holds the item, or has the interest, right or benefit the paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold it, or have an interest, right or benefit in it, as the kind of holding describes?
      `the item is shares in a related corporation that is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the company or of another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares in a related corporation that is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the company or of another corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 164(1), must the company show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` IS
    `s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` `the kind of holding` `the director holds the item, or has the interest, right or benefit the paragraph names` `the item is shares in a related corporation that is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the company or of another corporation`

@export Under section 164(1A), must the company show the particulars of the holding in its register of the chief executive officer's shareholdings?
GIVEN `the kind of holding` IS A `s 164(1A) kind of holding` @desc Which kind of holding is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts to call for or deliver shares, or some other holding?
      `the chief executive officer holds the item, or has the interest, right or benefit the paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold it, or have an interest, right or benefit in it, as the kind of holding describes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 164(1A), must the company show the particulars of the holding in its register of the chief executive officer's shareholdings` IS
    `s 164(1A) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the chief executive officer's shareholdings` `the kind of holding` `the chief executive officer holds the item, or has the interest, right or benefit the paragraph names`

@export Under section 164(1)(a), does the director have an interest in the shares?
GIVEN `I have authority to dispose of, or to control the disposal of, the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of the shares, or to control their disposal?
      `I have an interest under a trust whose property includes the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does property held in trust include the shares, and do you have an interest under that trust?
      `I know, or have reasonable grounds to believe, that I have that interest under the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know, or have reasonable grounds to believe, that you have that interest under the trust?
      `I have entered into a contract to purchase a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you entered into a contract to purchase a share?
      `I have a right to have a share transferred to me or to my order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right (other than as a beneficiary of a trust) to have a share transferred to you or to your order?
      `I have the right to acquire a share, or an interest in one, under an option` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option?
      `I am entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share I do not hold as registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled (other than as a proxy or representative at a meeting) to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share of which you are not the registered holder?
      `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or issued for one and held by the scheme's manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a unit in a collective investment scheme that has been subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or is issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager?
      `I hold the share as bare trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the share as bare trustee?
      `my ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your ordinary business include the lending of money?
      `I hold the interest only by way of security for an ordinary-course money-lending transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money?
      `I hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office?
      `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares bought under sections 76B to 76G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)?
      `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 164(1)(a), does the director have an interest in the shares` IS
    `s 164(1)(a) the director has an interest in the shares` `my interest facts`
    WHERE
        `my interest facts` MEANS `s 7 interest facts` WITH
            `the person has authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of, the shares` IS `I have authority to dispose of, or to control the disposal of, the shares`
            `property held in trust consists of or includes the shares and the person has an interest under the trust` IS `I have an interest under a trust whose property includes the shares`
            `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has that interest under the trust` IS `I know, or have reasonable grounds to believe, that I have that interest under the trust`
            `the person has entered into a contract to purchase a share` IS `I have entered into a contract to purchase a share`
            `the person has a right, otherwise than by reason of having an interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to the person or to the person's order` IS `I have a right to have a share transferred to me or to my order`
            `the person has the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option` IS `I have the right to acquire a share, or an interest in one, under an option`
            `the person is entitled, otherwise than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share of which the person is not the registered holder` IS `I am entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share I do not hold as registered holder`
            `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme that has been subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or is issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager` IS `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or issued for one and held by the scheme's manager`
            `the person holds the share as bare trustee` IS `I hold the share as bare trustee`
            `the person's ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS `my ordinary business includes the lending of money`
            `the person holds the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS `I hold the interest only by way of security for an ordinary-course money-lending transaction`
            `the person holds the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS `I hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office`
            `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)` IS `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares bought under sections 76B to 76G`
            `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons` IS `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons`
            -- Not asked: an interest held only through a body corporate under section 7(4). The list is left empty, so a person whose only interest runs through a body corporate answers as if they had none (see NOTES.md, Seams).
            `the bodies corporate through which the person may be deemed to have the interest` IS EMPTY

@export Under section 164(14), does the person have an interest in the debenture or participatory interest?
GIVEN `I have authority to dispose of, or to control the disposal of, the debentures or participatory interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of the debentures or participatory interests, or to control their disposal?
      `I have an interest under a trust whose property includes the debentures or participatory interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does property held in trust include the debentures or participatory interests, and do you have an interest under that trust?
      `I know, or have reasonable grounds to believe, that I have that interest under the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know, or have reasonable grounds to believe, that you have that interest under the trust?
      `I have entered into a contract to purchase a debenture or participatory interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you entered into a contract to purchase a debenture or participatory interest?
      `I have a right to have a debenture or participatory interest transferred to me or to my order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right (other than as a beneficiary of a trust) to have a debenture or participatory interest transferred to you or to your order?
      `I have the right to acquire a debenture or participatory interest, or an interest in one, under an option` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to acquire a debenture or participatory interest, or an interest in a debenture or participatory interest, under an option?
      `I am entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a debenture or participatory interest I do not hold as registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled (other than as a proxy or representative at a meeting) to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a debenture or participatory interest of which you are not the registered holder?
      `I hold the debenture or participatory interest as bare trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the debenture or participatory interest as bare trustee?
      `my ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your ordinary business include the lending of money?
      `I hold the interest only by way of security for an ordinary-course money-lending transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money?
      `I hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office?
      `the interest is a company's interest in its own debentures or participatory interests bought under sections 76B to 76G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest a company's interest in its own debentures or participatory interests purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)?
      `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 164(14), does the person have an interest in the debenture or participatory interest` IS
    `s 164(14) the person has an interest in the debenture or participatory interest` `my interest facts`
    WHERE
        `my interest facts` MEANS `s 7 interest facts` WITH
            `the person has authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of, the shares` IS `I have authority to dispose of, or to control the disposal of, the debentures or participatory interests`
            `property held in trust consists of or includes the shares and the person has an interest under the trust` IS `I have an interest under a trust whose property includes the debentures or participatory interests`
            `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has that interest under the trust` IS `I know, or have reasonable grounds to believe, that I have that interest under the trust`
            `the person has entered into a contract to purchase a share` IS `I have entered into a contract to purchase a debenture or participatory interest`
            `the person has a right, otherwise than by reason of having an interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to the person or to the person's order` IS `I have a right to have a debenture or participatory interest transferred to me or to my order`
            `the person has the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option` IS `I have the right to acquire a debenture or participatory interest, or an interest in one, under an option`
            `the person is entitled, otherwise than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share of which the person is not the registered holder` IS `I am entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a debenture or participatory interest I do not hold as registered holder`
            `the person holds the share as bare trustee` IS `I hold the debenture or participatory interest as bare trustee`
            `the person's ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS `my ordinary business includes the lending of money`
            `the person holds the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS `I hold the interest only by way of security for an ordinary-course money-lending transaction`
            `the person holds the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS `I hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office`
            `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)` IS `the interest is a company's interest in its own debentures or participatory interests bought under sections 76B to 76G`
            `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons` IS `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons`
            -- Section 164(14) applies section 7 except subsection (3), so the unit field is not asked and is set to FALSE.
            `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme that has been subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or is issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager` IS FALSE
            -- Not asked: an interest held only through a body corporate under section 7(4). The list is left empty, so a person whose only interest runs through a body corporate answers as if they had none (see NOTES.md, Seams).
            `the bodies corporate through which the person may be deemed to have the interest` IS EMPTY

@export Under section 164(5), did the company enter the particulars in its register within 3 days after receiving my notice?
GIVEN `the day the company received the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company receive your notice?
