@export Under section 168(2), must the director take all reasonable steps to secure that the particulars are included in or sent with the notice of the offer?
GIVEN `a payment is to be made to the director in connection with the transfer to any person, as a result of an offer made to shareholders, of all or any of the shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a payment to be made to you in connection with the transfer of the company's shares to someone as a result of an offer made to shareholders?
      `those particulars are furnished to the shareholders by virtue of any requirement of law relating to take-over offers or any requirement of the Take-over Code mentioned in section 139 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those particulars furnished to the shareholders because a law on take-over offers, or the Take-over Code, requires it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 168(2), must the director take all reasonable steps to secure that the particulars are included in or sent with the notice of the offer` IS
    `s 168(2) the director must take all reasonable steps to secure that the particulars are included in or sent with the notice of the offer` `a payment is to be made to the director in connection with the transfer to any person, as a result of an offer made to shareholders, of all or any of the shares in the company` `those particulars are furnished to the shareholders by virtue of any requirement of law relating to take-over offers or any requirement of the Take-over Code mentioned in section 139 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`

@export Under section 168(4), what is the amount deemed to have been a payment by way of compensation for loss of office?
GIVEN `the price to be paid to the director for the shares the director holds` IS A NUMBER @desc What price is to be paid to the director for the shares the director holds, in dollars?
      `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What price could other holders of the like shares have obtained at the time, in dollars?
      `the money value of any valuable consideration given to the director` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the money value of any other valuable consideration given to the director, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 168(4), what is the amount deemed to have been a payment by way of compensation for loss of office` IS
    `s 168(4) the amount deemed to have been a payment by way of compensation for loss of office` `the price to be paid to the director for the shares the director holds` `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of the like shares` `the money value of any valuable consideration given to the director`

@export Under section 168(5), is the payment one that the references in the section to compensation for loss of office do not include?
GIVEN `the date of the agreement under which the payment is made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the agreement under which the payment is made entered into?
      `the payment is made under an agreement particulars of which have been disclosed to and approved by special resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made under an agreement whose particulars were disclosed to and approved by special resolution of the company?
      `the payment is a bona fide payment by way of damages for breach of contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment a bona fide payment by way of damages for breach of contract?
      `the payment is a bona fide payment by way of pension or lump sum payment in respect of past services, including any superannuation or retiring allowance, superannuation gratuity or similar payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment a bona fide pension or lump sum for past services (including a superannuation or retiring allowance, gratuity or similar payment)?
      `the value or amount of the pension or payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value or amount of the pension or payment, in dollars?
      `the part of that value or amount attributable to contributions made by the director` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of it is attributable to the director's own contributions, in dollars?
      `the total emoluments of the director in the 3 years immediately preceding his or her retirement or death` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the director's total emoluments in the 3 years immediately before retirement or death, in dollars?
      `the payment is made pursuant to an agreement made between the company and the director before the director became a director, as the consideration or part of the consideration for the director agreeing to serve the company as a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made under an agreement made before the director became a director, as the consideration for agreeing to serve as a director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 168(5), is the payment one that the references in the section to compensation for loss of office do not include` IS
    `s 168(5) the payment is one that the references in the section to compensation for loss of office do not include` `my answer under paragraph (a)` `my answer under paragraph (b)` `my answer under paragraph (c)` `my answer under paragraph (d)` `my answer under paragraph (e)`
    WHERE
        `my answer under paragraph (a)` MEANS `s 168(5)(a) the payment is made under an agreement entered into before 1 January 1967` `the date of the agreement under which the payment is made`
        `my answer under paragraph (b)` MEANS `s 168(5)(b) the payment is made under an agreement disclosed to and approved by special resolution of the company` `the payment is made under an agreement particulars of which have been disclosed to and approved by special resolution of the company`
        `my answer under paragraph (c)` MEANS `s 168(5)(c) the payment is a bona fide payment by way of damages for breach of contract` `the payment is a bona fide payment by way of damages for breach of contract`
        `my answer under paragraph (d)` MEANS `s 168(5)(d) the payment is a bona fide pension or lump sum payment in respect of past services within the limit` `the payment is a bona fide payment by way of pension or lump sum payment in respect of past services, including any superannuation or retiring allowance, superannuation gratuity or similar payment` `the value or amount of the pension or payment` `the part of that value or amount attributable to contributions made by the director` `the total emoluments of the director in the 3 years immediately preceding his or her retirement or death`
        `my answer under paragraph (e)` MEANS `s 168(5)(e) the payment is made pursuant to an agreement made before the director became a director` `the payment is made pursuant to an agreement made between the company and the director before the director became a director, as the consideration or part of the consideration for the director agreeing to serve the company as a director`

§§ `Section 169: provision and improvement of a director's emoluments`

@export Under section 169(1), is the provision or improvement of the director's emoluments barred?
GIVEN `the company provides emoluments or improves emoluments for a director in respect of his or her office as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company provide or improve emoluments for a director in respect of his or her office as director?
      `the provision is approved by a resolution that is not related to other matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision approved by a resolution that is not related to other matters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 169(1), is the provision or improvement of the director's emoluments barred` IS
    `s 169(1) the provision or improvement of the emoluments is barred` `the company provides emoluments or improves emoluments for a director in respect of his or her office as such` `the provision is approved by a resolution that is not related to other matters`

@export Under section 169(1), is the resolution void?
GIVEN `the resolution was passed in breach of the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed in breach of section 169?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 169(1), is the resolution void` IS
    `s 169(1) the resolution is void` `the resolution was passed in breach of the section`

@export Under section 169(2), is the payment or benefit within the word emoluments?
GIVEN `the kind of payment or benefit` IS A `s 169(2) kind of benefit` @desc Is it fees or percentages, a sum paid as an expenses allowance, a pension scheme contribution, a benefit received otherwise than in cash for the services as director, or something else?
      `the sum is charged to income tax in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an expenses allowance, is the sum charged to income tax in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 169(2), is the payment or benefit within the word emoluments` IS
    `s 169(2) the payment or benefit is within the word emoluments` `the kind of payment or benefit` `the sum is charged to income tax in Singapore`

§§ `Section 171: the secretary of a company`

@export Under section 171(1), is the person qualified to be a secretary of the company?
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a natural person?
      `the person has his or her principal or only place of residence in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have his or her principal or only place of residence in Singapore?
      `the person is debarred under section 155B from acting as secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person debarred under section 155B from acting as secretary of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171(1), is the person qualified to be a secretary of the company` IS
    `s 171(1) the person is qualified to be a secretary of the company` `the person is a natural person` `the person has his or her principal or only place of residence in Singapore` `the person is debarred under section 155B from acting as secretary of the company`

@export Under section 171(1B), did the person file the declaration at the time of the appointment?
GIVEN `the day the person was appointed as a secretary by the directors` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you appointed as secretary by the directors?
      `the day the declaration was filed with the Registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the declaration filed with the Registrar?
      `the declaration is in the prescribed form, states that the person consents to act as secretary and gives the prescribed particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the declaration in the prescribed form, saying that you consent to act as secretary and giving the prescribed particulars?
      `the filing was made by the person or through a registered qualified individual authorised by the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it filed by you, or through a registered qualified individual you authorised?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171(1B), did the person file the declaration at the time of the appointment` IS
    `s 171(1B) the person filed the declaration at the time of the appointment` `the day the person was appointed as a secretary by the directors` `the day the declaration was filed with the Registrar` `the declaration is in the prescribed form, states that the person consents to act as secretary and gives the prescribed particulars` `the filing was made by the person or through a registered qualified individual authorised by the person`

@export Under section 171(1E), must the sole director not act or be appointed as the secretary of the company?
GIVEN `the person is the sole director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the sole director of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171(1E), must the sole director not act or be appointed as the secretary of the company` IS
    `s 171(1E) the person must not act or be appointed as the secretary of the company` `the person is the sole director of the company`

@export Under section 171(3) and (3A), has the company met the requirement of a secretary at the registered office?
GIVEN `at least one of the secretaries is physically present at the registered office on the days and at the hours during which the registered office is to be accessible to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is at least one secretary (or his or her agent or clerk) physically present at the registered office on the days and at the hours it is to be accessible to the public?
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `a secretary or his or her agent or clerk of the private company is readily contactable by a person at the registered office by telephone or other means of instantaneous communication during those times` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a secretary (or his or her agent or clerk) readily contactable by telephone or other instant means from the registered office during those times?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171(3) and (3A), has the company met the requirement of a secretary at the registered office` IS
    `s 171(3) and (3A) the company has met the requirement of a secretary at the registered office` `at least one of the secretaries is physically present at the registered office on the days and at the hours during which the registered office is to be accessible to the public` `the company is a private company` `a secretary or his or her agent or clerk of the private company is readily contactable by a person at the registered office by telephone or other means of instantaneous communication during those times`

@export Under section 171(4A), was the office of secretary not left vacant for more than 6 months?
GIVEN `the day the office of secretary became vacant` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the office of secretary become vacant?
      `the day the vacancy was filled` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the vacancy filled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171(4A), was the office of secretary not left vacant for more than 6 months` IS
    `s 171(4A) the office of secretary was not left vacant for more than 6 months` `the day the office of secretary became vacant` `the day the vacancy was filled`

§§ `Sections 172, 172A and 172B: protection of officers from liability`

@export Under section 172(1), is the provision purporting to exempt an officer from liability void?
GIVEN `the provision purports to exempt an officer of the company (to any extent) from a liability that would otherwise attach to the officer in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision purport to exempt an officer of the company, to any extent, from a liability that would otherwise attach to the officer for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust towards the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 172(1), is the provision purporting to exempt an officer from liability void` IS
    `s 172(1) the provision purporting to exempt an officer from liability is void` `the provision purports to exempt an officer of the company (to any extent) from a liability that would otherwise attach to the officer in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company`

@export Under section 172(2), is the provision by which the company indemnifies an officer void?
GIVEN `the provision is one by which the company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for an officer of the company against a liability attaching to the officer in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision one by which the company, directly or indirectly, indemnifies an officer to any extent against a liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust towards the company?
      `the company purchases and maintains for an officer of the company insurance against a liability mentioned in section 172(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement insurance the company buys and maintains for the officer against such a liability?
      `the indemnity is against liability incurred by the officer to a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the indemnity against a liability the officer incurs to a person other than the company?
      `the indemnity is against a liability of the officer to pay a fine in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indemnify a fine in criminal proceedings?
      `the indemnity is against a liability of the officer to pay a sum to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indemnify a penalty payable to a regulatory authority for non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature?
      `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in defending criminal proceedings in which the officer is convicted, the conviction being the final decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indemnify the cost of defending criminal proceedings in which the officer is finally convicted?
      `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in defending civil proceedings brought by the company or by a company deemed by section 6 to be related to it, in which judgment is given against the officer as the final decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indemnify the cost of defending civil proceedings brought by the company or a related company in which judgment is finally given against the officer?
      `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in connection with an application for relief referred to in subsection (4) in which the court refuses to grant relief as the final decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indemnify a liability connected with an application for relief under section 76A(13) or 391 that the court finally refuses?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 172(2), is the provision by which the company indemnifies an officer void` IS
    `s 172(2) the provision for an indemnity is void` `the provision is one by which the company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for an officer of the company against a liability attaching to the officer in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company` `my provision is permitted by section 172A or 172B`
    WHERE
        `my provision is permitted by section 172A or 172B` MEANS ((`s 172A the insurance is within the exception from section 172(2)` `the company purchases and maintains for an officer of the company insurance against a liability mentioned in section 172(2)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR ((`s 172B(1) the provision for indemnity is within the exception from section 172(2)` `the indemnity is against liability incurred by the officer to a person other than the company` `the indemnity is against a liability of the officer to pay a fine in criminal proceedings` `the indemnity is against a liability of the officer to pay a sum to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in defending criminal proceedings in which the officer is convicted, the conviction being the final decision` `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in defending civil proceedings brought by the company or by a company deemed by section 6 to be related to it, in which judgment is given against the officer as the final decision` `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in connection with an application for relief referred to in subsection (4) in which the court refuses to grant relief as the final decision`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)

