DECIDE `Under section 173H(1), is the person guilty of an offence` IS
    `s 173H(1) the person is guilty of the offence` `default is made by the company in section 173A(1) or 173C` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`

@export Under section 173H(1), what is the highest fine the person may be sentenced to on conviction, in Singapore dollars?
GIVEN `default is made by the company in section 173A(1) or 173C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is default made by the company in section 173A(1) or 173C?
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the company?
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 173H(1), what is the highest fine the person may be sentenced to on conviction, in Singapore dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `s 173H(1) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `default is made by the company in section 173A(1) or 173C` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 173H the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

