    `s 173I the company must continue to keep the record on the day` `the record` `the person was a director (for paragraph (a)) or a secretary (for paragraph (b)) of the company immediately before 3 January 2016` `there is documentary evidence of a change in the person's name` `the person has ceased to be a director or secretary of the company` `the day the person ceased to be a director or secretary of the company` `the day in question`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sgc1 (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force 6 May to 20 October 2026 -- THE SEAT LAYER of sgc1
-- (Part 6 Division 1, ss 199 to 204, and the Twelfth Schedule).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member of a company incorporated under the Act, or who deals with one.
-- Nothing here is new law: each question calls one rule of the layer-1 modules imported above, with the facts the person can state, and returns the answer as that rule gives it.
-- A rule's answer passes through unchanged: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text's own no, NOTHING is "the text does not answer this case" (NOTES.md, Reading a result).
-- The seat never turns NOTHING into a no, and never restates a rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no, number, date or choice inputs, one per fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked.
-- Where a layer-1 rule takes an optional number (the longer period the Registrar may allow, s 202B(2)), the question asks for the number and 0 means "none".
-- Where a layer-1 rule takes the result of s 201(12), (13) and (15A) (a departure from the Accounting Standards), the question asks the four facts those subsections turn on, and the composite rule works it out.
-- The one figure the Minister may substitute, the amount in s 201A(5)(a)(ii) and (iii) ($500,000 as the section states it), is an input of the s 201A(5)(a) question:
-- the person states the amount that applies to the company, which is $500,000 unless the Minister has prescribed another amount in substitution (Guide section 4: a number set by an instrument that is not among the sources is an input).
-- Regulative rules (the DEONTIC ones) are not questions: the person asks "by when" through the last-day and in-time rules, and "what follows" through the offence and penalty rules.
-- The seat has a question for each rule that a person in this seat asks; the rules that only the Registrar, the Minister or the Court exercise appear as what they mean to the person (may the Registrar give me a notice; may the Court order costs against me).


§ `Section 199: accounting records and systems of control`

-- calls 's 199(1) the company has caused the records to be kept as the subsection requires' (sgc1-s199.l4)
@export Under section 199(1), has my company caused its accounting and other records to be kept as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the records sufficiently explain the transactions and financial position of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the records sufficiently explain the transactions and financial position of the company?
      `the records enable true and fair financial statements and any documents required to be attached to them to be prepared from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the records enable true and fair financial statements and any documents required to be attached to them to be prepared from time to time?
      `the records are kept in such manner as to enable them to be conveniently and properly audited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the records are kept in such manner as to enable them to be conveniently and properly audited?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 199(1), has my company caused its accounting and other records to be kept as the subsection requires` IS
    `s 199(1) the company has caused the records to be kept as the subsection requires` `the records sufficiently explain the transactions and financial position of the company` `the records enable true and fair financial statements and any documents required to be attached to them to be prepared from time to time` `the records are kept in such manner as to enable them to be conveniently and properly audited`

-- calls 's 199(2) the last day of the period for which the company must retain the records' (sgc1-s199.l4)
@export Under section 199(2), what is the last day of the period for which my company must retain its records?
GIVEN `the last day of the financial year in which the transactions or operations to which the records relate are completed` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the financial year end in which the transactions or operations recorded were completed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 199(2), what is the last day of the period for which my company must retain its records` IS
    `s 199(2) the last day of the period for which the company must retain the records` `the last day of the financial year in which the transactions or operations to which the records relate are completed`

-- calls 's 199(2) the subsection requires the company to retain the records on the day' (sgc1-s199.l4)
@export Under section 199(2), must my company still retain its records on the day I ask about?
GIVEN `the last day of the financial year in which the transactions or operations to which the records relate are completed` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the financial year end in which the transactions or operations recorded were completed?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 199(2), must my company still retain its records on the day I ask about` IS
    `s 199(2) the subsection requires the company to retain the records on the day` `the last day of the financial year in which the transactions or operations to which the records relate are completed` `the day asked about`

-- calls 's 199(2A) the company must devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls' (sgc1-s199.l4)
@export Under section 199(2A), must my company devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a public company?
      `the company is a subsidiary company of a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a subsidiary company of a public company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 199(2A), must my company devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls` IS
    `s 199(2A) the company must devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls` `the company is a public company` `the company is a subsidiary company of a public company`

-- calls 's 199(2A) the company has devised and maintained the system the subsection requires' (sgc1-s199.l4)
@export Under section 199(2A), has my company devised and maintained the system of internal accounting controls the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a public company?
      `the company is a subsidiary company of a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a subsidiary company of a public company?
      `the company has devised and maintains a system of internal accounting controls` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company has devised and maintains a system of internal accounting controls?
      `the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that assets are safeguarded against loss from unauthorised use or disposition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that assets are safeguarded against loss from unauthorised use or disposition?
      `the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that transactions are properly authorised and recorded as necessary to permit the preparation of true and fair financial statements and to maintain accountability of assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that transactions are properly authorised and recorded as necessary to permit the preparation of true and fair financial statements and to maintain accountability of assets?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 199(2A), has my company devised and maintained the system of internal accounting controls the subsection requires` IS
    `s 199(2A) the company has devised and maintained the system the subsection requires` `the company is a public company` `the company is a subsidiary company of a public company` `the company has devised and maintains a system of internal accounting controls` `the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that assets are safeguarded against loss from unauthorised use or disposition` `the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that transactions are properly authorised and recorded as necessary to permit the preparation of true and fair financial statements and to maintain accountability of assets`

-- calls 's 199(3) the records are kept as the subsection requires' (sgc1-s199.l4)
@export Under section 199(3), are my company's records kept as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the records are kept at the registered office of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the records are kept at the registered office of the company?
      `the records are kept at another place that the directors think fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the records are kept at another place that the directors think fit?
      `the records are at all times open to inspection by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the records are at all times open to inspection by the directors?
