@export Under section 199(4), has my company complied with the subsection on records kept outside Singapore?
GIVEN `the accounting and other records are kept by the company at a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the accounting and other records are kept by the company at a place outside Singapore?
      `statements and returns with respect to the business dealt with in the records so kept have been sent to and kept at a place in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that statements and returns with respect to the business dealt with in the records so kept have been sent to and kept at a place in Singapore?
      `those statements and returns are at all times open to inspection by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that those statements and returns are at all times open to inspection by the directors?
      `those statements and returns enable true and fair financial statements and any documents required to be attached to them to be prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that those statements and returns enable true and fair financial statements and any documents required to be attached to them to be prepared?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 199(4), has my company complied with the subsection on records kept outside Singapore` IS
    `s 199(4) the company has complied with the subsection` `the accounting and other records are kept by the company at a place outside Singapore` `statements and returns with respect to the business dealt with in the records so kept have been sent to and kept at a place in Singapore` `those statements and returns are at all times open to inspection by the directors` `those statements and returns enable true and fair financial statements and any documents required to be attached to them to be prepared`

-- calls 's 199(5) the Court may order the records to be open to inspection by the public accountant' (sgc1-s199.l4)
@export Under section 199(5), may the Court order the records to be open to inspection by a public accountant acting for me as a director?
GIVEN `the public accountant is acting for a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the public accountant is acting for a director of the company?
      `an undertaking in writing has been given to the Court that information acquired by the public accountant during the inspection must not be disclosed by the public accountant except to that director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an undertaking in writing has been given to the Court that information acquired by the public accountant during the inspection must not be disclosed by the public accountant except to that director?
