      `the company is a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a listed company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 201B(9), must the directors describe the audit committee's functions in the statement` IS
    `s 201B(9) the directors must describe the audit committee's functions in the statement` `the directors of the company or of a parent company are required to make a statement under section 201(16)` `the company is a listed company`

-- calls "s 201B(9) the directors' statement describes the audit committee's functions as the subsection requires" (sgc1-s201b.l4)
@export Under section 201B(9), does the directors' statement describe the audit committee's functions as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the directors of the company or of a parent company are required to make a statement under section 201(16)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors of the company or of a parent company are required to make a statement under section 201(16)?
      `the company is a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a listed company?
      `the statement describes the nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee pursuant to subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement describes the nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee pursuant to subsection (5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 201B(9), does the directors' statement describe the audit committee's functions as the subsection requires` IS
    `s 201B(9) the directors' statement describes the audit committee's functions as the subsection requires` `the directors of the company or of a parent company are required to make a statement under section 201(16)` `the company is a listed company` `the statement describes the nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee pursuant to subsection (5)`

-- calls 's 201B(11) the director is an executive director' (sgc1-s201b.l4)
@export Under section 201B(11), is the director an executive director?
GIVEN `the person is an employee of the company or holds any other office of profit in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an employee of the company or holds any other office of profit in the company?
      `the person is an employee of, or holds any other office of profit in, another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an employee of, or holds any other office of profit in, another corporation?
      `the other corporation is deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other corporation is deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 201B(11), is the director an executive director` IS
    `s 201B(11) the director is an executive director` `the person is an employee of the company or holds any other office of profit in the company` `the person is an employee of, or holds any other office of profit in, another corporation` `the other corporation is deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6`

-- calls 's 201C(1) the directors need not lay financial statements before the company at its annual general meeting' (sgc1-s201b.l4)
@export Under section 201C(1), is it the case that the directors of a private company need not lay financial statements before the company at its annual general meeting?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a private company?
      `the company need not hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company need not hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 201C(1), is it the case that the directors of a private company need not lay financial statements before the company at its annual general meeting` IS
    `s 201C(1) the directors need not lay financial statements before the company at its annual general meeting` `the company is a private company` `the company need not hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)`

-- calls 's 201C(2) the reference in section 207(1) is read as a reference to the documents sent under section 203(1)' (sgc1-s201b.l4)
@export Under section 201C(2), is the reference in section 207(1) read as a reference to the documents sent under section 203(1)?
GIVEN `the financial statements or consolidated financial statements are not laid before the company at its annual general meeting under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the financial statements or consolidated financial statements are not laid before the company at its annual general meeting under subsection (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 201C(2), is the reference in section 207(1) read as a reference to the documents sent under section 203(1)` IS
    `s 201C(2) the reference in section 207(1) is read as a reference to the documents sent under section 203(1)` `the financial statements or consolidated financial statements are not laid before the company at its annual general meeting under subsection (1)`

§ `Sections 202, 202A and 202B: relief, revision and the Registrar's notice`

-- calls 's 202(1) the directors may apply to the Registrar in writing for an order relieving them from the requirement' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202(1), may the directors apply to the Registrar in writing for an order relieving them from the requirement?
GIVEN `the requirement relates to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the requirement relates to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements?
      `the requirement is a requirement of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the requirement is a requirement of the Accounting Standards?
      `the requirement relates to the form and content of the statement required by section 201(16)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the requirement relates to the form and content of the statement required by section 201(16)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202(1), may the directors apply to the Registrar in writing for an order relieving them from the requirement` IS
    `s 202(1) the directors may apply to the Registrar in writing for an order relieving them from the requirement` `the requirement relates to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements` `the requirement is a requirement of the Accounting Standards` `the requirement relates to the form and content of the statement required by section 201(16)`

-- calls 's 202(1) the Registrar may make the order on condition that the directors comply with the other requirement' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202(1), may the Registrar make the order on condition that the directors comply with the other requirement?
GIVEN `the other requirement relates to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements or the directors' statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other requirement relates to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements or the directors' statement?
      `the Registrar thinks it fit to impose the other requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar thinks it fit to impose the other requirement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202(1), may the Registrar make the order on condition that the directors comply with the other requirement` IS
    `s 202(1) the Registrar may make the order on condition that the directors comply with the other requirement` `the other requirement relates to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements or the directors' statement` `the Registrar thinks it fit to impose the other requirement`

-- calls 's 202(4) the order made under section 202(1) has not ended' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202(4), has the order made under section 202(1) not ended?
GIVEN `the order is limited to a specific period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is limited to a specific period?
      `that specific period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that that specific period has ended?
      `the Registrar has revoked the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar has revoked the order?
      `the Registrar has suspended the operation of the order and the suspension has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar has suspended the operation of the order and the suspension has not ended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202(4), has the order made under section 202(1) not ended` IS
    `s 202(4) the order made under section 202(1) has not ended` `the order is limited to a specific period` `that specific period has ended` `the Registrar has revoked the order` `the Registrar has suspended the operation of the order and the suspension has not ended`

-- calls "s 202(1) the directors are relieved by the Registrar's order from the requirement" (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202(1), are the directors relieved by the Registrar's order from the requirement?
GIVEN `the Registrar has made an order on the directors' application that covers the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar has made an order on the directors' application that covers the requirement?
      `the order is limited to a specific period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is limited to a specific period?
      `that specific period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that that specific period has ended?
      `the Registrar has revoked the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar has revoked the order?
      `the Registrar has suspended the operation of the order and the suspension has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar has suspended the operation of the order and the suspension has not ended?
      `the order was made on condition that the directors comply with other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order was made on condition that the directors comply with other requirements?
      `the directors comply with those other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors comply with those other requirements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202(1), are the directors relieved by the Registrar's order from the requirement` IS
    `s 202(1) the directors are relieved by the Registrar's order from the requirement` `the Registrar has made an order on the directors' application that covers the requirement` `the order is limited to a specific period` `that specific period has ended` `the Registrar has revoked the order` `the Registrar has suspended the operation of the order and the suspension has not ended` `the order was made on condition that the directors comply with other requirements` `the directors comply with those other requirements`

-- calls "s 202(2) the directors are relieved by the Registrar's order for a class of companies from the requirement" (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202(2), are the directors relieved by the Registrar's order for a class of companies from the requirement?
GIVEN `the Registrar has made an order for a specified class of companies that includes the company and specifies the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar has made an order for a specified class of companies that includes the company and specifies the requirement?
      `the order was made on condition that the directors comply with other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order was made on condition that the directors comply with other requirements?
      `the directors comply with those other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors comply with those other requirements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202(2), are the directors relieved by the Registrar's order for a class of companies from the requirement` IS
    `s 202(2) the directors are relieved by the Registrar's order for a class of companies from the requirement` `the Registrar has made an order for a specified class of companies that includes the company and specifies the requirement` `the order was made on condition that the directors comply with other requirements` `the directors comply with those other requirements`

-- calls 's 202(3) the Registrar is not barred from making an order under section 202(1)' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202(3), is the Registrar not barred from making an order under section 202(1)?
GIVEN `the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance with the requirements of this Act would render the financial statements, consolidated financial statements or directors' statement misleading or inappropriate to the circumstances of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance with the requirements of this Act would render the financial statements, consolidated financial statements or directors' statement misleading or inappropriate to the circumstances of the company?
      `the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance would impose unreasonable burdens on the company or any officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance would impose unreasonable burdens on the company or any officer of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202(3), is the Registrar not barred from making an order under section 202(1)` IS
    `s 202(3) the Registrar is not barred from making an order under section 202(1)` `the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance with the requirements of this Act would render the financial statements, consolidated financial statements or directors' statement misleading or inappropriate to the circumstances of the company` `the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance would impose unreasonable burdens on the company or any officer of the company`

-- calls 's 202A(1) the section applies' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202A(1), does section 202A apply to the financial statements now?
GIVEN `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A?
      `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been sent to the members of the company under section 203` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been sent to the members of the company under section 203?
      `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been laid before the company at an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been laid before the company at an annual general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202A(1), does section 202A apply to the financial statements now` IS
    `s 202A(1) the section applies` `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A` `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been sent to the members of the company under section 203` `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been laid before the company at an annual general meeting`

-- calls 's 202A(2) the directors may cause the financial statements to be revised' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202A(2), may the directors cause the financial statements to be revised?
GIVEN `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A?
      `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been sent to the members of the company under section 203` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been sent to the members of the company under section 203?
      `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been laid before the company at an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been laid before the company at an annual general meeting?
      `it appears to the directors that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet, do not comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it appears to the directors that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet, do not comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202A(2), may the directors cause the financial statements to be revised` IS
    `s 202A(2) the directors may cause the financial statements to be revised` `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A` `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been sent to the members of the company under section 203` `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been laid before the company at an annual general meeting` `it appears to the directors that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet, do not comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)`

-- calls 's 202A(3) the revision is confined as the subsection requires' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202A(3), is the revision confined as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the revision changes something other than the aspects in which the statements did not comply with this Act and the necessary consequential revisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the revision changes something other than the aspects in which the statements did not comply with this Act and the necessary consequential revisions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202A(3), is the revision confined as the subsection requires` IS
    `s 202A(3) the revision is confined as the subsection requires` `the revision changes something other than the aspects in which the statements did not comply with this Act and the necessary consequential revisions`

-- calls 's 202A(4) the directors are barred from causing the financial statements to be revised' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202A(4), are the directors barred from causing the financial statements to be revised?
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the directors of the company a notice under section 202B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar has given the directors of the company a notice under section 202B(1)?
      `the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner in which to revise the statements referred to in section 202B(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner in which to revise the statements referred to in section 202B(2)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202A(4), are the directors barred from causing the financial statements to be revised` IS
    `s 202A(4) the directors are barred from causing the financial statements to be revised` `the Registrar has given the directors of the company a notice under section 202B(1)` `the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner in which to revise the statements referred to in section 202B(2)(b)`

-- calls 's 202B(1) the Registrar may give the directors a notice' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202B(1), may the Registrar give the directors a notice?
GIVEN `it appears to the Registrar that there is, or may be, a question whether the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it appears to the Registrar that there is, or may be, a question whether the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202B(1), may the Registrar give the directors a notice` IS
    `s 202B(1) the Registrar may give the directors a notice` `it appears to the Registrar that there is, or may be, a question whether the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)`

-- calls 's 202B(2) the number of days allowed for the response' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202B(2), how many days are the directors allowed to respond to the Registrar's notice?
GIVEN `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did the Registrar specify for the directors to respond?
      `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total number of days the Registrar has allowed for the response, if the Registrar allowed a longer period than the first? (0 if no longer period was allowed)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 202B(2), how many days are the directors allowed to respond to the Registrar's notice` IS
    `s 202B(2) the number of days allowed for the response` `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` (IF `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed` EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed`)

-- calls 's 202B(2) the last day for the directors to respond' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202B(2), what is the last day for the directors to respond to the Registrar's notice?
GIVEN `the day the Registrar gave the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Registrar give the notice?
      `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did the Registrar specify for the directors to respond?
      `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total number of days the Registrar has allowed for the response, if the Registrar allowed a longer period than the first? (0 if no longer period was allowed)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 202B(2), what is the last day for the directors to respond to the Registrar's notice` IS
    `s 202B(2) the last day for the directors to respond` `the day the Registrar gave the notice` `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` (IF `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed` EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed`)

-- calls 's 202B(2)(a) the directors must give the Registrar an explanation of the financial statements' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202B(2)(a), must the directors give the Registrar an explanation of the financial statements?
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the directors notice under section 202B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar has given the directors notice under section 202B(1)?
      `the directors propose to revise the financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors propose to revise the financial statements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
