-- calls 's 202B(2) the directors responded by the end of the period' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202B(2), did the directors respond by the end of the period?
GIVEN `the day the Registrar gave the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Registrar give the notice?
      `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did the Registrar specify for the directors to respond?
      `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total number of days the Registrar has allowed for the response, if the Registrar allowed a longer period than the first? (0 if no longer period was allowed)
      `the day the directors respond` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the directors respond?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202B(2), did the directors respond by the end of the period` IS
    `s 202B(2) the directors responded by the end of the period` `the day the Registrar gave the notice` `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` (IF `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed` EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed`) `the day the directors respond`

-- calls 's 202B(3) the directors need take no further action on the notice' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202B(3), is it the case that the directors need take no further action on the notice?
GIVEN `the directors gave the Registrar an explanation under subsection (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors gave the Registrar an explanation under subsection (2)(a)?
      `the Registrar is satisfied with the explanation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar is satisfied with the explanation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202B(3), is it the case that the directors need take no further action on the notice` IS
    `s 202B(3) the directors need take no further action on the notice` `the directors gave the Registrar an explanation under subsection (2)(a)` `the Registrar is satisfied with the explanation`

-- calls 's 202B(4) the directors may cause the financial statements to be revised in the manner agreed' (sgc1-s202.l4)
@export Under section 202B(4), may the directors cause the financial statements to be revised in the manner agreed?
GIVEN `the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner in which to revise the statements referred to in subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner in which to revise the statements referred to in subsection (2)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
