GIVEN `the person asking is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person asking an auditor of the company?
      `the person the auditor asks` IS A `s 207(5) person asked` @desc Whom is the auditor asking: an officer of the company, an auditor of another company, or any other person?
      `the company is the holding company of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company the holding company of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor?
      `the company is a subsidiary of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a subsidiary of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor?
      `the company is a subsidiary of the holding company of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a subsidiary of the holding company of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor?
      `they are information and explanations that the auditor desires for the purposes of audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they information and explanations the auditor desires for the purposes of the audit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 207(5), is the auditor entitled to require information and explanations from the person` IS
    `s 207(5) the auditor is entitled to require information and explanations from the person` `the person asking is an auditor of the company` `the person the auditor asks` `the company is the holding company of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` `the company is a subsidiary of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` `the company is a subsidiary of the holding company of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` `they are information and explanations that the auditor desires for the purposes of audit`

-- The auditor, or an agent authorised by the auditor in writing, is entitled to attend any general meeting. NOTHING: the text names no one else.
@export Under section 207(8), is the person entitled to attend any general meeting of the company?
GIVEN `the person claiming the right` IS A `s 207(8) person` @desc Who claims the right: an auditor of the company, an agent the auditor authorised in writing, or any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 207(8), is the person entitled to attend any general meeting of the company` IS
    `s 207(8) the person is entitled to attend any general meeting of the company` `the person claiming the right`

-- An auditor who is satisfied of a breach of the Act that the auditor thinks will not be adequately dealt with in the report or by telling the directors must immediately report it in writing to the Registrar.
@export Under section 207(9), is the auditor in default of the duty to report the matter to the Registrar?
GIVEN `the auditor is satisfied that there has been a breach or non-observance of a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor satisfied that there has been a breach or non-observance of a provision of the Act?
      `in the auditor's opinion the matter has not been or will not be adequately dealt with by comment in the auditor's report or by bringing it to the notice of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the auditor's opinion, has the matter not been, or will it not be, adequately dealt with by comment in the report or by telling the directors?
      `the auditor has reported the matter in writing to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor reported the matter in writing to the Registrar?
      `the auditor did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the auditor do so immediately?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 207(9), is the auditor in default of the duty to report the matter to the Registrar` IS
    `s 207(9) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Registrar` `the auditor is satisfied that there has been a breach or non-observance of a provision of this Act` `in the auditor's opinion the matter has not been or will not be adequately dealt with by comment in the auditor's report or by bringing it to the notice of the directors` `the auditor has reported the matter in writing to the Registrar` `the auditor did so immediately`

-- The auditor of a public company (or its subsidiary corporation) who has reason to believe a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty has been committed against the company must immediately report it to the Minister.
@export Under section 207(9A), is the auditor in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister?
GIVEN `the auditor is an auditor of a public company or of a subsidiary corporation of a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor the auditor of a public company, or of a subsidiary corporation of a public company?
      `the auditor has reason to believe that an offence is being or has been committed against the company by officers or employees of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor have reason to believe that an offence is being or has been committed against the company by its officers or employees?
      `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in years?
      `the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained from the commission of the offence, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the property obtained, or likely to be obtained, from the offence, in Singapore dollars?
      `the auditor is not required to make a report to the Minister because of section 207(9C)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor already relieved of reporting to the Minister because the auditor is under a legal duty to report to the Monetary Authority of Singapore and has already reported the same offence to it?
      `the auditor has reported the matter to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor reported the matter to the Minister?
      `the auditor did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the auditor do so immediately?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 207(9A), is the auditor in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` IS
    `s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` `the auditor is an auditor of a public company or of a subsidiary corporation of a public company` `the auditor has reason to believe that an offence is being or has been committed against the company by officers or employees of the company` `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in years` `the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained from the commission of the offence, in Singapore dollars` `the auditor is not required to make a report to the Minister because of section 207(9C)` `the auditor has reported the matter to the Minister` `the auditor did so immediately`

-- Officers of a company, and officers and auditors of a subsidiary corporation, who refuse access or information without lawful excuse, or who hinder, obstruct or delay an auditor, are guilty of an offence.
@export Under section 207(10), is the person guilty of the offence?
GIVEN `the person charged under section 207(10)` IS A `s 207(10) person` @desc Who is the person: an officer of a company, an officer of a subsidiary corporation, an auditor of a subsidiary corporation, or any other person?
      `the conduct charged under section 207(10)` IS A `s 207(10) conduct` @desc What did the person do: refuse access (to the company's records, or to a subsidiary corporation's records for the parent company's auditor), refuse information or explanation, or otherwise hinder, obstruct or delay the auditor?
      `the person had lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person have a lawful excuse?
      `the item the auditor asks to see` IS A `s 207(5) access item` @desc What does the auditor ask to see: an accounting or other record that is not a register, a register other than one kept under Part 11A, or a register kept under Part 11A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 207(10), is the person guilty of the offence` IS
    `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `the person charged under section 207(10)` `the conduct charged under section 207(10)` `the person had lawful excuse` `the item the auditor asks to see`

-- The fine for the offences in section 207(10) is not more than $4,000.
@export Under section 207(10), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction?
GIVEN `the person charged under section 207(10)` IS A `s 207(10) person` @desc Who is the person: an officer of a company, an officer of a subsidiary corporation, an auditor of a subsidiary corporation, or any other person?
      `the conduct charged under section 207(10)` IS A `s 207(10) conduct` @desc What did the person do: refuse access (to the company's records, or to a subsidiary corporation's records for the parent company's auditor), refuse information or explanation, or otherwise hinder, obstruct or delay the auditor?
      `the person had lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person have a lawful excuse?
      `the item the auditor asks to see` IS A `s 207(5) access item` @desc What does the auditor ask to see: an accounting or other record that is not a register, a register other than one kept under Part 11A, or a register kept under Part 11A?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 207(10), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction` IS
    `s 207(10) the most the person may be fined on conviction` `the person charged under section 207(10)` `the conduct charged under section 207(10)` `the person had lawful excuse` `the item the auditor asks to see`

-- An auditor is not liable in defamation, absent malice, for a statement made in the course of the auditor's duties. NOTHING: the text does not say what follows if there was malice.
@export Under section 208(1), is the auditor not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the statement?
GIVEN `the statement is one which the auditor makes in the course of the auditor's duties as such, whether orally or in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement one the auditor made, orally or in writing, in the course of the auditor's duties as auditor?
      `there is malice on the auditor's part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there malice on the auditor's part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 208(1), is the auditor not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the statement` IS
    `s 208(1) the auditor is not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the statement` `the statement is one which the auditor makes in the course of the auditor's duties as such, whether orally or in writing` `there is malice on the auditor's part`

-- A provision exempting an auditor from, or indemnifying the auditor against, liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust is void, but the company may indemnify the auditor for the costs of successfully defending proceedings or for relief granted by the court.
@export Under section 208A(1) and (2), is the provision void under the section?
GIVEN `the provision exempts the auditor of the company from, or indemnifies the auditor against, a liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision exempt the auditor of the company from a liability, or indemnify the auditor against one?
      `the liability is one which by law would otherwise attach to the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a liability which by law would otherwise attach to the auditor?
      `the liability is in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust of which the auditor may be guilty in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust of which the auditor may be guilty in relation to the company?
      `the indemnity is against a liability incurred or that will be incurred by the auditor in defending proceedings (whether civil or criminal)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the indemnity against a liability incurred, or to be incurred, by the auditor in defending proceedings (civil or criminal)?
      `judgment is given in the auditor's favour in those proceedings or the auditor is acquitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was judgment given in the auditor's favour in those proceedings, or was the auditor acquitted?
      `the indemnity is against a liability incurred or that will be incurred by the auditor in connection with an application under section 76A(13) or 391 or any other provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the indemnity against a liability incurred, or to be incurred, by the auditor in connection with an application under section 76A(13) or 391 or any other provision of the Act?
      `relief is granted to the auditor by the court in that application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was relief granted to the auditor by the court in that application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 208A(1) and (2), is the provision void under the section` IS
    `s 208A(1) and (2) the provision is void under the section` (`s 208A(2) the section does not prevent the company from indemnifying the auditor` `the indemnity is against a liability incurred or that will be incurred by the auditor in defending proceedings (whether civil or criminal)` `judgment is given in the auditor's favour in those proceedings or the auditor is acquitted` `the indemnity is against a liability incurred or that will be incurred by the auditor in connection with an application under section 76A(13) or 391 or any other provision of this Act` `relief is granted to the auditor by the court in that application` EQUALS JUST TRUE) (`s 208A(1) the provision is void` `the provision exempts the auditor of the company from, or indemnifies the auditor against, a liability` `the liability is one which by law would otherwise attach to the auditor` `the liability is in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust of which the auditor may be guilty in relation to the company`)

§ `Section 209: the auditor of a borrowing corporation and the trustee for debenture holders`

-- Within 7 days after furnishing the borrowing corporation with its financial statements or any report, certificate or other document, the auditor must send a copy by post to every trustee for the debenture holders.
@export Under section 209(1), what is the last day for the auditor to send a copy to every trustee?
GIVEN `the day the auditor furnished the corporation with the financial statements or the report, certificate or other document` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the auditor furnish the corporation with the financial statements or the report, certificate or other document?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 209(1), what is the last day for the auditor to send a copy to every trustee` IS
    `s 209(1) the last day for the auditor to send a copy to every trustee` `the day the auditor furnished the corporation with the financial statements or the report, certificate or other document`

-- JUST TRUE: the auditor missed the last day. JUST FALSE: sent in time, or the time is still running, or the corporation is not a borrowing corporation.
@export Under section 209(1), is the auditor in default of the duty to send a copy to every trustee?
GIVEN `the corporation is a borrowing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a borrowing corporation (liable to repay money received from the public for debentures)?
      `the auditor has furnished the corporation with financial statements or a report, certificate or other document which the auditor is required by this Act or by the debentures or trust deed to give to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor furnished the corporation with financial statements, or a report, certificate or other document the auditor must give it under the Act or the debentures or trust deed?
      `the day the auditor furnished it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the auditor furnish it to the corporation?
      `the auditor has sent by post to every trustee for the holders of debentures of the corporation a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor sent by post a copy to every trustee for the debenture holders?
      `the day the copy was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the copy sent? (Any date if it has not been.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 209(1), is the auditor in default of the duty to send a copy to every trustee` IS
    `s 209(1) the auditor is in default of the duty to send a copy to every trustee` `the corporation is a borrowing corporation` `the auditor has furnished the corporation with financial statements or a report, certificate or other document which the auditor is required by this Act or by the debentures or trust deed to give to the corporation` `the day the auditor furnished it` `the auditor has sent by post to every trustee for the holders of debentures of the corporation a copy` `the day the copy was sent` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- Within 7 days after becoming aware of a matter relevant to the trustee's powers and duties, the auditor must send a written report to the borrowing corporation and a copy to the trustee.
@export Under section 209(2), is the auditor in default of the duty to send the report?
GIVEN `the corporation is a borrowing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a borrowing corporation (liable to repay money received from the public for debentures)?
      `the auditor has become aware, in the performance of the auditor's duties as auditor of the borrowing corporation, of a matter which is in the auditor's opinion relevant to the exercise and performance of the powers and duties imposed by this Act or by any trust deed upon any trustee for the holders of debentures of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor become aware, in performing the audit of the borrowing corporation, of a matter that in the auditor's opinion is relevant to the powers and duties of the trustee for the debenture holders?
      `the day the auditor became aware of the matter` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the auditor become aware of the matter?
      `the auditor has sent by post a report in writing on the matter to the borrowing corporation and a copy of it to the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor sent by post a written report on the matter to the borrowing corporation and a copy to the trustee?
      `the day the report and the copy were sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the report and the copy sent? (Any date if they have not been.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 209(2), is the auditor in default of the duty to send the report` IS
    `s 209(2) the auditor is in default of the duty to send the report` `the corporation is a borrowing corporation` `the auditor has become aware, in the performance of the auditor's duties as auditor of the borrowing corporation, of a matter which is in the auditor's opinion relevant to the exercise and performance of the powers and duties imposed by this Act or by any trust deed upon any trustee for the holders of debentures of the corporation` `the day the auditor became aware of the matter` `the auditor has sent by post a report in writing on the matter to the borrowing corporation and a copy of it to the trustee` `the day the report and the copy were sent` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- A person who fails to comply with subsection (2) is guilty of an offence: a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also a default penalty (the default penalty's amount is in section 408, outside this part).
@export Under section 209(3), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction?
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person fail to comply with section 209(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 209(3), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction` IS
    `s 209(3) the most the person may be fined on conviction` `the person fails to comply with subsection (2)`

§ `Thirteenth Schedule: the small company and the small group (for section 205C)`

-- A company is a small company if it qualifies under paragraph 2, 3 or 4 and continues to be one until it ceases under paragraph 5. Revenue and total assets of at most $10 million and at most 50 employees are the criteria; any 2 of the 3 suffice.
@export Under schedule 13 paragraph 1(a), is the company a small company for the financial year?
GIVEN `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the first financial year after incorporation as 1, which financial year is this?
      `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company incorporated?
      `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting as 1 the first financial year that commences on or after 1 July 2015, which financial year is this?
      `the company was a small company for the financial year immediately preceding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company a small company for the immediately preceding financial year?
      `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company throughout the financial year?
      `the company ceases to be a private company at any time during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company cease to be a private company at any time during the financial year?
      `the revenue of the financial year, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the revenue for the financial year, in Singapore dollars?
      `the total assets at the end of the financial year, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the total assets at the end of the financial year, in Singapore dollars?
      `the number of employees at the end of the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees are there at the end of the financial year?
      `the revenue of the financial year immediately preceding, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the revenue for the immediately preceding financial year, in Singapore dollars?
      `the total assets at the end of the financial year immediately preceding, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the total assets at the end of the immediately preceding financial year, in Singapore dollars?
      `the number of employees at the end of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees were there at the end of the immediately preceding financial year?
      `the revenue of the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the revenue for the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars?
      `the total assets at the end of the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the total assets at the end of the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars?
      `the number of employees at the end of the financial year before that` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees were there at the end of the financial year before that?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 13 paragraph 1(a), is the company a small company for the financial year` IS
    `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` `the number of the financial year after incorporation, counting the first as 1` `the date the company was incorporated` `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` `the company was a small company for the financial year immediately preceding` `the company is a private company throughout the financial year` `the company ceases to be a private company at any time during the financial year` (`sch 13 year figures` OF `the revenue of the financial year, in Singapore dollars`, `the total assets at the end of the financial year, in Singapore dollars`, `the number of employees at the end of the financial year`) (`sch 13 year figures` OF `the revenue of the financial year immediately preceding, in Singapore dollars`, `the total assets at the end of the financial year immediately preceding, in Singapore dollars`, `the number of employees at the end of the financial year immediately preceding`) (`sch 13 year figures` OF `the revenue of the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars`, `the total assets at the end of the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars`, `the number of employees at the end of the financial year before that`)

-- A group is a small group if it qualifies under paragraph 7, 8 or 9 and continues to be one until it ceases under paragraph 10.
@export Under schedule 13 paragraph 1(b), is the group a small group for the financial year?
GIVEN `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the first financial year after the group is formed as 1, which financial year is this?
      `the date the group was formed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the group formed?
      `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting as 1 the first financial year that commences on or after 1 July 2015, which financial year is this?
      `the group was a small group for the financial year immediately preceding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the group a small group for the immediately preceding financial year?
      `the revenue of the financial year, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the revenue for the financial year, in Singapore dollars?
      `the total assets at the end of the financial year, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the total assets at the end of the financial year, in Singapore dollars?
      `the number of employees at the end of the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees are there at the end of the financial year?
      `the revenue of the financial year immediately preceding, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the revenue for the immediately preceding financial year, in Singapore dollars?
      `the total assets at the end of the financial year immediately preceding, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the total assets at the end of the immediately preceding financial year, in Singapore dollars?
      `the number of employees at the end of the financial year immediately preceding` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees were there at the end of the immediately preceding financial year?
      `the revenue of the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the revenue for the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars?
      `the total assets at the end of the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the total assets at the end of the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars?
      `the number of employees at the end of the financial year before that` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees were there at the end of the financial year before that?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 13 paragraph 1(b), is the group a small group for the financial year` IS
    `sch 13 para 1(b) the group is a small group for the financial year` `the number of the financial year after the group is formed, counting the first as 1` `the date the group was formed` `the number of the financial year, counting as 1 the first that commences on or after 1 July 2015` `the group was a small group for the financial year immediately preceding` (`sch 13 year figures` OF `the revenue of the financial year, in Singapore dollars`, `the total assets at the end of the financial year, in Singapore dollars`, `the number of employees at the end of the financial year`) (`sch 13 year figures` OF `the revenue of the financial year immediately preceding, in Singapore dollars`, `the total assets at the end of the financial year immediately preceding, in Singapore dollars`, `the number of employees at the end of the financial year immediately preceding`) (`sch 13 year figures` OF `the revenue of the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars`, `the total assets at the end of the financial year before that, in Singapore dollars`, `the number of employees at the end of the financial year before that`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sgd (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 6 May 2026 to 20 October 2026 (an SSO rendering, not the official text)
-- Part 7, ss 210 to 215K -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company, or who deals with one: a creditor,
-- a holder of units of shares, a dissenting shareholder, a person to whom the company owes an obligation. Nothing here is new law, and there is no seat for the
-- Registrar, the Court, the Official Receiver or the Minister: where a provision addresses one of them, the question asks what it means to the individual.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices), one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc
-- worded as that person would be asked. The records the layer-1 rules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME
-- layer-1 rule is then called; no rule is restated here. Amounts, rates and periods the text leaves to others are inputs, never numbers from memory.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. JUST TRUE: the test is met on the facts you gave. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words. NOTHING: not covered by the text of
-- Part 7 as rendered here. Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- THE NAME OF EVERY QUESTION begins "Under section N," and asks the question its body answers, in the same direction as the layer-1 rule it calls: where the rule is
-- a bar, the name asks about the bar; where it is a permission, about the permission; where it is a duty, "must". NOTES.md lists the questions whose name and
-- body differ in direction or subject (none, after the fix recorded there).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Inputs of sections 210 to 212, each defined once: the same fact keeps the same name and the same @desc in every question.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§ `Companies Act 1967, Part 7: arrangements, reconstructions and amalgamations -- the individual's questions`

§§ `Section 210: compromise or arrangement with creditors, members or holders of units of shares`

-- s 210(2). The persons who may apply for a meeting: for a company being wound up, the liquidator; in any other case, the company or any creditor, member or holder of units of shares.
-- JUST TRUE: you are one of them. JUST FALSE: the text names others and you are not one. The layer-1 rule is a permission, and so is the question.
@export Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement?
GIVEN `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company being wound up (in the course of being wound up)?
      `how the applicant stands to the company` IS A `s 210(2) applicant` @desc Who is applying: the liquidator of the company, the company itself, a creditor, a member, a holder of units of shares, or some other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement` IS
    `s 210(2) the person is a person referred to in subsection (1)` `the company is being wound up` `how the applicant stands to the company`

-- s 210(1). The Court's power to order a meeting, on the application of a person section 210(2) names. A permission, as the question is.
@export Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed?
GIVEN `the kind of compromise or arrangement that is proposed` IS A `s 210(1) proposal` @desc What is proposed: a compromise or arrangement with the company's creditors (or a class of them), with its members (or a class), with holders of units of shares of the company (or a class), or something else?
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company being wound up (in the course of being wound up)?
      `how the applicant stands to the company` IS A `s 210(2) applicant` @desc Who is applying: the liquidator of the company, the company itself, a creditor, a member, a holder of units of shares, or some other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed` IS
    `s 210(1) the Court may order a meeting to be summoned` `the kind of compromise or arrangement that is proposed` `the company is being wound up` `how the applicant stands to the company`

-- s 210(3). A meeting ordered by the Court may be adjourned if the resolution to adjourn is approved by a majority in number representing three-fourths in value of those present and voting.
@export Under section 210(3), may the meeting be adjourned on the vote that was taken?
GIVEN `the number of people present and voting at the meeting, in person or by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people were present and voting at the meeting, in person or by proxy?
      `the number of those people who voted in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those, how many voted in favour?
      `the value held by the people present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value (of the claims, shares or units) held by the people present and voting?
      `the value held by those who voted in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value held by those who voted in favour?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(3), may the meeting be adjourned on the vote that was taken` IS
    `s 210(3) the meeting may be adjourned` `the vote`
    WHERE
        `the vote` MEANS `s 210(3) vote` WITH
            `s 210(3) the number of persons present and voting in person or by proxy` IS `the number of people present and voting at the meeting, in person or by proxy`
            `s 210(3) the number of those persons who voted in favour` IS `the number of those people who voted in favour`
            `s 210(3) the value held by the persons present and voting` IS `the value held by the people present and voting`
            `s 210(3) the value held by those who voted in favour` IS `the value held by those who voted in favour`

-- s 210(3AB). The conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding: a majority in number (or the number the Court orders), three-fourths in value, and the Court's approval by order.
@export Under section 210(3AB), are the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding satisfied?
GIVEN `the number of people present and voting at the meeting, in person or by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people were present and voting at the meeting, in person or by proxy?
      `the number of those people who voted in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those, how many voted in favour?
      `the value held by the people present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value (of the claims, shares or units) held by the people present and voting?
      `the value held by those who voted in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value held by those who voted in favour?
      `the Court has ordered a number other than a majority in number to agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that some number other than a majority in number must agree?
      `the number of people the Court has ordered must agree` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people has the Court ordered must agree? (0 if it has made no such order)
      `the Court has approved the compromise or arrangement by order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court approved the compromise or arrangement by order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(3AB), are the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding satisfied` IS
    `s 210(3AB) the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding are satisfied` `the vote` `the Court has ordered a number other than a majority in number to agree` `the number of people the Court has ordered must agree` `the Court has approved the compromise or arrangement by order`
    WHERE
        `the vote` MEANS `s 210(3) vote` WITH
            `s 210(3) the number of persons present and voting in person or by proxy` IS `the number of people present and voting at the meeting, in person or by proxy`
            `s 210(3) the number of those persons who voted in favour` IS `the number of those people who voted in favour`
            `s 210(3) the value held by the persons present and voting` IS `the value held by the people present and voting`
            `s 210(3) the value held by those who voted in favour` IS `the value held by those who voted in favour`

-- s 210(3AA). If the conditions of (3AB) are satisfied, the compromise or arrangement binds the persons (3AA) names. The conditions are worked out here from the vote, then (3AA) is asked.
@export Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me?
GIVEN `the party the compromise or arrangement may bind` IS A `s 210(3AA) party` @desc Who are you in relation to the compromise or arrangement: the liquidator of a company being wound up, a contributory of such a company, the company (not being wound up), a creditor of the class concerned, a member of the class concerned, a holder of units of shares of the class concerned, or some other person?
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company being wound up (in the course of being wound up)?
      `the number of people present and voting at the meeting, in person or by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people were present and voting at the meeting, in person or by proxy?
      `the number of those people who voted in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those, how many voted in favour?
      `the value held by the people present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value (of the claims, shares or units) held by the people present and voting?
      `the value held by those who voted in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value held by those who voted in favour?
      `the Court has ordered a number other than a majority in number to agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that some number other than a majority in number must agree?
      `the number of people the Court has ordered must agree` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people has the Court ordered must agree? (0 if it has made no such order)
      `the Court has approved the compromise or arrangement by order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court approved the compromise or arrangement by order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` IS
    `s 210(3AA) the compromise or arrangement is binding on the party` (`s 210(3AB) the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding are satisfied` `the vote` `the Court has ordered a number other than a majority in number to agree` `the number of people the Court has ordered must agree` `the Court has approved the compromise or arrangement by order` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the company is being wound up` `the party the compromise or arrangement may bind`
    WHERE
        `the vote` MEANS `s 210(3) vote` WITH
            `s 210(3) the number of persons present and voting in person or by proxy` IS `the number of people present and voting at the meeting, in person or by proxy`
            `s 210(3) the number of those persons who voted in favour` IS `the number of those people who voted in favour`
            `s 210(3) the value held by the persons present and voting` IS `the value held by the people present and voting`
            `s 210(3) the value held by those who voted in favour` IS `the value held by those who voted in favour`

-- s 210(4). The Court may grant its approval subject to such alterations or conditions as it thinks just.
@export Under section 210(4), may the Court grant its approval subject to an alteration or condition?
GIVEN `the Court thinks the alteration or condition just` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Court think the alteration or condition just?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(4), may the Court grant its approval subject to an alteration or condition` IS
    `s 210(4) the Court may grant its approval subject to the alteration or condition` `the Court thinks the alteration or condition just`

-- s 210(5). The order has no effect until a copy is lodged with the Registrar. The layer-1 rule is the bar ("cannot yet have effect"), and so is the question.
@export Under section 210(5), is the Court's order unable yet to have effect because no copy has been lodged with the Registrar?
GIVEN `a copy of the Court's order has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the Court's order been lodged with the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(5), is the Court's order unable yet to have effect because no copy has been lodged with the Registrar` IS
    `s 210(5) the order cannot yet have effect` `a copy of the Court's order has been lodged with the Registrar`

@export Under section 210(5), from what date does the Court's order take effect?
GIVEN `a copy of the Court's order has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the Court's order been lodged with the Registrar?
      `the day the copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the copy of the order lodged with the Registrar? (any date if it has not been)
      `the order specifies a date determined by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order specify a date that the Court has determined?
      `the date the order specifies` IS A DATE @desc What date does the order specify? (any date if it specifies none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 210(5), from what date does the Court's order take effect` IS
    `s 210(5) the date from which the order takes effect` `a copy of the Court's order has been lodged with the Registrar` `the day the copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` `the order specifies a date determined by the Court` `the date the order specifies`

-- s 210(6). A copy of every order made under (3AB)(c) must be annexed to every copy of the constitution issued after the order, subject to (7). A duty of the company, asked as one.
@export Under section 210(6), must a copy of the Court's order be annexed to the copy of the constitution that is being issued?
GIVEN `the constitution copy is issued after the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy of the constitution being issued after the order was made?
      `the Court has exempted the company from annexing the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court by order exempted the company from annexing the order?
      `the Court has fixed a period for annexing the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court determined the period during which the company must annex the order?
      `the copy is issued within the period the Court fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy of the constitution issued within that period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(6), must a copy of the Court's order be annexed to the copy of the constitution that is being issued` IS
    `s 210(6) a copy of the order must be annexed to the copy of the constitution` `the constitution copy is issued after the order was made` `the Court has exempted the company from annexing the order` `the Court has fixed a period for annexing the order` `the copy is issued within the period the Court fixed`

-- s 210(7). The Court may, by order, exempt a company from (6) or determine the period during which it must comply.
@export Under section 210(7), may the Court do what the order does about annexing?
GIVEN `what the Court's order does about annexing` IS A `s 210(7) what the Court does` @desc What does the Court's order do: exempt the company from annexing the order, fix the period during which it must annex it, or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(7), may the Court do what the order does about annexing` IS
    `s 210(7) the Court may do it by order` `what the Court's order does about annexing`

-- s 210(8)(a). Where the members by resolution direct that accountants or solicitors report on the proposals, the directors must instruct them. A duty, asked as one.
@export Under section 210(8)(a), must the directors instruct the accountants or solicitors named in the resolution to report?
GIVEN `a compromise or arrangement has been proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a compromise or arrangement been proposed?
      `a meeting of the members has directed by resolution that accountants or solicitors report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a meeting of the members directed by resolution that accountants or solicitors, or both, report on the proposals?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(8)(a), must the directors instruct the accountants or solicitors named in the resolution to report` IS
    `s 210(8)(a) the directors must instruct the accountants or solicitors named in the resolution to report` `a compromise or arrangement has been proposed` `a meeting of the members has directed by resolution that accountants or solicitors report`

-- s 210(8)(b). The reports must be made available for inspection at the registered office at least 7 days before the meeting.
@export Under section 210(8)(b), were the reports made available at the registered office at least 7 days before the meeting?
GIVEN `the day of the meeting ordered by the Court` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the meeting ordered by the Court?
      `the day the reports were made available at the registered office` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the reports made available at the registered office for inspection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(8)(b), were the reports made available at the registered office at least 7 days before the meeting` IS
    `s 210(8)(b) the reports have been made available at least 7 days before the meeting` `the day of the meeting ordered by the Court` `the day the reports were made available at the registered office`

-- s 210(9). The company that makes default in complying with (6) or (8), and every officer of it in default, is guilty of an offence; fine not exceeding $2,000.
@export Under section 210(9), is the company guilty of an offence for its default in annexing the order or in giving effect to the members' direction?
GIVEN `the company is in default of annexing the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in annexing the order to every copy of its constitution as section 210(6) requires?
      `the company is in default of making the reports available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in giving effect to the members' direction that accountants or solicitors report, as section 210(8) requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(9), is the company guilty of an offence for its default in annexing the order or in giving effect to the members' direction` IS
    `s 210(9) the company is guilty of the offence` `the company is in default of annexing the order` `the company is in default of making the reports available`

@export Under section 210(9), am I guilty of an offence as an officer of the company in default?
GIVEN `the company is in default of annexing the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in annexing the order to every copy of its constitution as section 210(6) requires?
      `the company is in default of making the reports available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in giving effect to the members' direction that accountants or solicitors report, as section 210(8) requires?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is` @desc What is your position in the company: a director, the secretary, a person employed in an executive capacity, a receiver and manager under an instrument, a liquidator in a voluntary winding up, a receiver who is not also a manager, a receiver and manager appointed by the Court, a liquidator appointed by the Court or the creditors, a judicial manager, or anyone else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(9), am I guilty of an offence as an officer of the company in default` IS
    `s 210(9) the officer is guilty of the offence` `the company is in default of annexing the order` `the company is in default of making the reports available` `I am an officer of the company who is in default` `my position in the company`

@export Under section 210(9), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction as an officer in default?
GIVEN `the company is in default of annexing the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in annexing the order to every copy of its constitution as section 210(6) requires?
      `the company is in default of making the reports available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in giving effect to the members' direction that accountants or solicitors report, as section 210(8) requires?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is` @desc What is your position in the company: a director, the secretary, a person employed in an executive capacity, a receiver and manager under an instrument, a liquidator in a voluntary winding up, a receiver who is not also a manager, a receiver and manager appointed by the Court, a liquidator appointed by the Court or the creditors, a judicial manager, or anyone else?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 210(9) penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 210(9), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction as an officer in default` IS
    `s 210(9) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` (`s 210(9) the officer is guilty of the offence` `the company is in default of annexing the order` `the company is in default of making the reports available` `I am an officer of the company who is in default` `my position in the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

-- s 210(10). The Court may restrain further proceedings against the company; once restrained, they may not continue without the Court's permission.
@export Under section 210(10), may the Court restrain further proceedings against the company?
GIVEN `no order or resolution for winding up has been made or passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has no order been made, and no resolution passed, for the winding up of the company?
      `a compromise or arrangement has been proposed with the creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a compromise or arrangement been proposed between the company and its creditors or any class of them?
      `the application is by the company or a member, creditor or holder of units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made in a summary way by the company or by a member, creditor or holder of units of shares of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(10), may the Court restrain further proceedings against the company` IS
    `s 210(10) the Court may restrain further proceedings against the company` `no order or resolution for winding up has been made or passed` `a compromise or arrangement has been proposed with the creditors` `the application is by the company or a member, creditor or holder of units`

@export Under section 210(10), may further proceedings against the company continue?
GIVEN `the Court has restrained further proceedings against the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court restrained further proceedings against the company?
      `the Court has given permission to proceed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission to proceed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(10), may further proceedings against the company continue` IS
    `s 210(10) further proceedings against the company may continue` `the Court has restrained further proceedings against the company` `the Court has given permission to proceed`

-- s 210(10A). Money or other consideration held in trust under the terms must be transferred to the Official Receiver before 10 years from receipt expire.
@export Under section 210(10A), was what is held in trust for a person transferred to the Official Receiver within the time the subsection allows?
GIVEN `the terms provide for money or other consideration to be held in trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms of the compromise or arrangement provide for money or other consideration to be held in trust for a person?
      `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the money or other consideration received by the person holding it?
      `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it (or will it be) transferred to the Official Receiver?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(10A), was what is held in trust for a person transferred to the Official Receiver within the time the subsection allows` IS
    `s 210(10A) the transfer to the Official Receiver is within the time the subsection allows` `the terms provide for money or other consideration to be held in trust` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver`

-- s 210(10B). What the Official Receiver must do with what is received. The Official Receiver is not the seat; the question asks what happens to what was held for the individual.
@export Under section 210(10B), how is what has been transferred to the Official Receiver dealt with?
GIVEN `what was received is money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what was received money?
      `what was received is other consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what was received other consideration (not money)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 210(10B) treatment`
DECIDE `Under section 210(10B), how is what has been transferred to the Official Receiver dealt with` IS
    `s 210(10B) how the Official Receiver must deal with what is received` `what was received is money` `what was received is other consideration`

-- s 210(11). Definitions for the section: "arrangement", "company", "holder of units of shares".
@export Under section 210(11), is the thing within the word "arrangement"?
GIVEN `the thing is a consolidation of shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a reorganisation of the share capital of a company by the consolidation of shares of different classes?
      `the thing is a division of shares into different classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a reorganisation of the share capital of a company by the division of shares into shares of different classes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(11), is the thing within the word "arrangement"` IS
    `s 210(11) "arrangement" the thing is within the word arrangement` `the thing is a consolidation of shares of different classes` `the thing is a division of shares into different classes`

@export Under section 210(11), is the body a "company" for the purposes of section 210?
GIVEN `the body is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(11), is the body a "company" for the purposes of section 210` IS
    `s 210(11) "company" the body is a company` `the body is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`

@export Under section 210(11), am I a "holder of units of shares"?
GIVEN `I hold units of shares only beneficially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the units of shares only beneficially (not as the registered holder)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(11), am I a "holder of units of shares"` IS
    `s 210(11) "holder of units of shares" the person is a holder of units of shares` `I hold units of shares only beneficially`

