§§ `Section 211: the information that must go with the notice of the meeting`

-- s 211(1). With every notice summoning the meeting sent to a creditor, member or holder of units, a statement explaining the compromise or arrangement and the directors' material interests; in a notice by advertisement, either such a statement or a notification of where to obtain copies.
@export Under section 211(1), does the notice carry what the subsection requires?
GIVEN `a meeting is summoned under section 210` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a meeting summoned under section 210?
      `the kind of notice` IS A `s 211(1) notice` @desc What kind of notice is it: one summoning the meeting that is sent to a creditor, member or holder of units of shares, or one summoning the meeting that is given by advertisement?
      `a statement explaining the compromise or arrangement is sent with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement sent with the notice?
      `the statement states the directors' material interests and the effect on them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state any material interests of the directors (whether as directors, members, creditors or otherwise) and the effect of the compromise or arrangement on them so far as it differs from its effect on the like interests of other persons?
      `the advertised notice includes such a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice include such a statement?
      `the advertised notice says where and how copies of the statement may be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice include a notification of the place at which and the manner in which copies of such a statement may be obtained?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 211(1), does the notice carry what the subsection requires` IS
    `s 211(1) the notice carries what the subsection requires` `a meeting is summoned under section 210` `the kind of notice` `a statement explaining the compromise or arrangement is sent with the notice` `the statement states the directors' material interests and the effect on them` `the advertised notice includes such a statement` `the advertised notice says where and how copies of the statement may be obtained`

@export Under section 211(2), does the statement give what the subsection requires about the trustee for the debenture holders?
GIVEN `the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the compromise or arrangement affect the rights of debenture holders of the company?
      `the statement gives the like explanation about the trustee for the debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the like explanation with respect to the trustee for the debenture holders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 211(2), does the statement give what the subsection requires about the trustee for the debenture holders` IS
    `s 211(2) the statement gives what the subsection requires` `the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders` `the statement gives the like explanation about the trustee for the debenture holders`

-- s 211(3). Where a notice is given by advertisement that copies of the statement can be obtained, the company must furnish a copy free of charge to every creditor, member or holder of units entitled to attend who applies in the manner the notice indicates.
@export Under section 211(3), must the company furnish me with a copy of the statement free of charge?
GIVEN `the advertised notice says copies of the statement can be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice given by advertisement include a notification that copies of the statement can be obtained?
      `I am a creditor, member or holder of units entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the company entitled to attend the meeting?
      `I have applied in the manner the notice indicates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for a copy in the manner indicated by the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 211(3), must the company furnish me with a copy of the statement free of charge` IS
    `s 211(3) the company must furnish the person with a copy of the statement free of charge` `the advertised notice says copies of the statement can be obtained` `I am a creditor, member or holder of units entitled to attend the meeting` `I have applied in the manner the notice indicates`

-- s 211(4). A director, and a trustee for debenture holders, must give the company the notice needed to comply with the section within 7 days of receiving a request in writing for the information.
@export Under section 211(4), did the director or trustee give notice within 7 days of the receipt of the request?
GIVEN `the day the director or trustee was asked in writing for information` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the director or trustee receive the request in writing for information?
      `the day the director or trustee gave notice to the company` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the director or trustee give notice to the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 211(4), did the director or trustee give notice within 7 days of the receipt of the request` IS
    `s 211(4) the director or trustee gave notice within 7 days of the receipt of the request` `the day the director or trustee was asked in writing for information` `the day the director or trustee gave notice to the company`

-- s 211(5), (6) and (7). Default is an offence of the company and of every officer in default (the liquidator and a trustee for debenture holders are deemed officers); a director has a defence if the default was due to another's refusal to supply particulars.
@export Under section 211(5), is the company guilty of the offence?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with a requirement of section 211` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with a requirement of section 211?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 211(5), is the company guilty of the offence` IS
    `s 211(5) the company is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with a requirement of section 211`

@export Under section 211(6), am I deemed to be an officer of the company for subsection (5)?
GIVEN `I am the liquidator of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the liquidator of the company?
      `I am a trustee for debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a trustee for debenture holders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 211(6), am I deemed to be an officer of the company for subsection (5)` IS
    `s 211(6) the person is deemed to be an officer of the company for subsection (5)` `I am the liquidator of the company` `I am a trustee for debenture holders`

@export Under section 211(7), does the section give me a defence?
GIVEN `I show the default was due to another director's refusal to supply particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that the default was due to the refusal of another director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars as to that person's interests?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 211(7), does the section give me a defence` IS
    `s 211(7) the section gives the person a defence` `I show the default was due to another director's refusal to supply particulars`

@export Under section 211(5), am I guilty of the offence as an officer in default?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with a requirement of section 211` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with a requirement of section 211?
      `I am an officer in default of the section 211 requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is` @desc What is your position in the company: a director, the secretary, a person employed in an executive capacity, a receiver and manager under an instrument, a liquidator in a voluntary winding up, a receiver who is not also a manager, a receiver and manager appointed by the Court, a liquidator appointed by the Court or the creditors, a judicial manager, or anyone else?
      `I am the liquidator of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the liquidator of the company?
      `I am a trustee for debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a trustee for debenture holders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 211(5), am I guilty of the offence as an officer in default` IS
    `s 211(5) the officer is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with a requirement of section 211` `I am an officer in default of the section 211 requirement` `my position in the company` `I am the liquidator of the company` `I am a trustee for debenture holders`

@export Under section 211(5) and (7), am I liable under subsection (5)?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with a requirement of section 211` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with a requirement of section 211?
      `I am an officer in default of the section 211 requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is` @desc What is your position in the company: a director, the secretary, a person employed in an executive capacity, a receiver and manager under an instrument, a liquidator in a voluntary winding up, a receiver who is not also a manager, a receiver and manager appointed by the Court, a liquidator appointed by the Court or the creditors, a judicial manager, or anyone else?
      `I am the liquidator of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the liquidator of the company?
      `I am a trustee for debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a trustee for debenture holders?
      `I show the default was due to another director's refusal to supply particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that the default was due to the refusal of another director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars as to that person's interests?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 211(5) and (7), am I liable under subsection (5)` IS
    `s 211(5) and (7) the person is liable under subsection (5)` (`s 211(5) the officer is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with a requirement of section 211` `I am an officer in default of the section 211 requirement` `my position in the company` `I am the liquidator of the company` `I am a trustee for debenture holders` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `I show the default was due to another director's refusal to supply particulars`

@export Under section 211(5), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with a requirement of section 211` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with a requirement of section 211?
      `I am an officer in default of the section 211 requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is` @desc What is your position in the company: a director, the secretary, a person employed in an executive capacity, a receiver and manager under an instrument, a liquidator in a voluntary winding up, a receiver who is not also a manager, a receiver and manager appointed by the Court, a liquidator appointed by the Court or the creditors, a judicial manager, or anyone else?
      `I am the liquidator of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the liquidator of the company?
      `I am a trustee for debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a trustee for debenture holders?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 210(9) penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 211(5), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction` IS
    `s 211(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` (`s 211(5) the officer is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with a requirement of section 211` `I am an officer in default of the section 211 requirement` `my position in the company` `I am the liquidator of the company` `I am a trustee for debenture holders` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

§§ `Section 212: the Court's order approving a reconstruction or an amalgamation scheme`

@export Under section 212(1), may the Court provide for the matter by its order?
GIVEN `the company applied to the Court under Part 7 or section 71 of the 2018 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an application made to the Court under Part 7 (or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018) for approval of a compromise or arrangement?
      `it is shown the compromise is for a reconstruction or amalgamation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it shown to the Court that the compromise or arrangement has been proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies or the amalgamation of any 2 or more companies?
      `it is shown the scheme transfers the undertaking or property to another company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it shown to the Court that under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of a company concerned is to be transferred to another company?
      `the matter the order would provide for` IS A `s 212(1) matter` @desc What would the order provide for: a transfer of the undertaking, property or liabilities; an allotment or appropriation of shares or like interests; continuation of legal proceedings; dissolution without winding up; provision for dissenters; incidental matters; or some other matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(1), may the Court provide for the matter by its order` IS
    `s 212(1) the Court may provide for the matter by its order` `the company applied to the Court under Part 7 or section 71 of the 2018 Act` `it is shown the compromise is for a reconstruction or amalgamation` `it is shown the scheme transfers the undertaking or property to another company` `the matter the order would provide for`

@export Under section 212(2), does the property vest in the transferee company, and do the liabilities become its liabilities, by virtue of the order?
GIVEN `the order provides for the transfer of property or liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an order made under section 212 provide for the transfer of property or liabilities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(2), does the property vest in the transferee company, and do the liabilities become its liabilities, by virtue of the order` IS
    `s 212(2) the property vests in the transferee company and the liabilities become its liabilities by virtue of the order` `the order provides for the transfer of property or liabilities`

@export Under section 212(2), does the particular property vest free from the charge?
GIVEN `the order directs that the particular property is free from the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order direct that the particular property is free from the charge?
      `the charge is by the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge, by virtue of the compromise or arrangement, to cease to have effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(2), does the particular property vest free from the charge` IS
    `s 212(2) the particular property vests free from the charge` `the order directs that the particular property is free from the charge` `the charge is by the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect`

-- s 212(3). Within 7 days of the order the company must lodge a copy with the Registrar (and, for land, an office copy with the appropriate authority). Default is an offence of the company and of every officer in default.
@export Under section 212(3), was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar within 7 days of the making of the order?
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made?
      `the lodgment was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar?
      `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar? (any date if it was not)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(3), was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar within 7 days of the making of the order` IS
    `s 212(3) the lodgment was made within 7 days of the making of the order` `the day the order was made` `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar, if it was`
    WHERE
        `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar, if it was` MEANS IF `the lodgment was made` THEN JUST `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 212(3), has the company lodged what the subsection requires within 7 days of the making of the order?
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made?
      `the lodgment was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar?
      `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar? (any date if it was not)
      `the order relates to land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order relate to land?
      `an office copy was lodged with the appropriate authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an office copy of the order lodged with the appropriate authority?
      `the day the office copy was lodged with the appropriate authority` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it lodged? (any date if it was not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(3), has the company lodged what the subsection requires within 7 days of the making of the order` IS
    `s 212(3) the company has lodged what the subsection requires within 7 days of the making of the order` `the day the order was made` `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar, if it was` `the order relates to land` `the day the office copy was lodged, if it was`
    WHERE
        `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar, if it was` MEANS IF `the lodgment was made` THEN JUST `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` ELSE NOTHING
        `the day the office copy was lodged, if it was` MEANS IF `an office copy was lodged with the appropriate authority` THEN JUST `the day the office copy was lodged with the appropriate authority` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 212(3), is the company guilty of the offence?
GIVEN `the company is in default of section 212` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in complying with section 212?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(3), is the company guilty of the offence` IS
    `s 212(3) the company is guilty of the offence` `the company is in default of section 212`

@export Under section 212(3), am I guilty of the offence as an officer in default?
GIVEN `the company is in default of section 212` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in complying with section 212?
      `I am an officer in default of section 212` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is` @desc What is your position in the company: a director, the secretary, a person employed in an executive capacity, a receiver and manager under an instrument, a liquidator in a voluntary winding up, a receiver who is not also a manager, a receiver and manager appointed by the Court, a liquidator appointed by the Court or the creditors, a judicial manager, or anyone else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(3), am I guilty of the offence as an officer in default` IS
    `s 212(3) the officer is guilty of the offence` `the company is in default of section 212` `I am an officer in default of section 212` `my position in the company`

@export Under section 212(3), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction?
GIVEN `the company is in default of section 212` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in complying with section 212?
      `I am an officer in default of section 212` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is` @desc What is your position in the company: a director, the secretary, a person employed in an executive capacity, a receiver and manager under an instrument, a liquidator in a voluntary winding up, a receiver who is not also a manager, a receiver and manager appointed by the Court, a liquidator appointed by the Court or the creditors, a judicial manager, or anyone else?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 210(9) penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 212(3), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction` IS
    `s 212(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` (`s 212(3) the officer is guilty of the offence` `the company is in default of section 212` `I am an officer in default of section 212` `my position in the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

@export Under section 212(4), is the vesting order unable yet to have effect in vesting the land because the entries have not been made?
GIVEN `the appropriate entries have been made with respect to the vesting of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the appropriate entries been made by the appropriate authority with respect to the vesting of the land?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(4), is the vesting order unable yet to have effect in vesting the land because the entries have not been made` IS
    `s 212(4) the vesting order cannot yet have effect in vesting the land` `the appropriate entries have been made with respect to the vesting of the land`

@export Under section 212(5), is the thing within the word "liabilities"?
GIVEN `the thing is a duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(5), is the thing within the word "liabilities"` IS
    `s 212(5) "liabilities" the thing is within the word liabilities` `the thing is a duty`

@export Under section 212(5), is the thing within the word "property"?
GIVEN `the thing is property, a right or a power of any description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing property, a right or a power of any description?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(5), is the thing within the word "property"` IS
    `s 212(5) "property" the thing is within the word property` `the thing is property, a right or a power of any description`

@export Under section 212(6), is the body a "company" for the purposes of section 212?
GIVEN `the body is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(6), is the body a "company" for the purposes of section 212` IS
