§§ `Section 215K: money or other consideration held in trust`

-- s 215K(1). Money or other consideration held in trust under the terms of the proposal must be transferred to the Official Receiver before 10 years from receipt expire.
@export Under section 215K(1), was what is held in trust transferred to the Official Receiver within the time the subsection allows?
GIVEN `the terms of the proposal provide for money or other consideration to be held in trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms of the approved amalgamation proposal provide for money or other consideration to be held in trust for a person?
      `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the money or other consideration received by the person holding it?
      `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it (or will it be) transferred to the Official Receiver?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 215K(1), was what is held in trust transferred to the Official Receiver within the time the subsection allows` IS
    `s 215K(1) the transfer to the Official Receiver is within the time the subsection allows` `the terms of the proposal provide for money or other consideration to be held in trust` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver`

@export Under section 215K(2), how is what has been transferred to the Official Receiver dealt with?
GIVEN `what was received under section 215K(1) is money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what was received under section 215K(1) money?
      `what was received under section 215K(1) is other consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what was received under section 215K(1) other consideration (not money)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 215K(2) treatment`
DECIDE `Under section 215K(2), how is what has been transferred to the Official Receiver dealt with` IS
    `s 215K(2) how the Official Receiver must deal with what is received under subsection (1)` `what was received under section 215K(1) is money` `what was received under section 215K(1) is other consideration`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sgf (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- ss 216, 216A and 216B -- THE SEAT LAYER (LAYER 2; part sgf). This file is generated from one table of inputs and one table of
-- questions (work/gen_seat.py in the author's sandbox), so that the same fact keeps the same name and the same @desc in every question.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- incorporated under the Act, or of a foreign company registered under it, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what
-- the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve
-- or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is
-- addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership. There is never a seat for the
-- Registrar, the Minister, the Authority or the Court: their powers appear here only as what they mean to the individual.)
--
-- This layer asks, for a minority member above all, the questions ss 216 to 216B answer: may I apply to the Court for an order on the
-- ground of oppression or injustice; on what ground; what may the Court order; what must I lodge, by when, and what follows if I do
-- not; may I bring an action or arbitration in the company's name, what notice must I give the directors and by when; what the Court may
-- order for the costs; when the case can be stopped. It IMPORTs the layer-1 modules and calls their rules; it restates none.
--
-- HOW AN ANSWER READS. Most answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE: the text says yes. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words.
-- NOTHING: the text does not say (an input outside what a provision names, or a power whose gate is not met): it is NOT a no. A
-- question named for a power or a permission ("may") is never answered no by NOTHING; a question named as a bar ("is ... barred") has
-- JUST TRUE as "yes, barred" and NOTHING as "the section does not say it is barred". The Court's own opinions and decisions (that a ground
-- is established, that notice is not expedient, that a person is a proper person) are inputs: the person states what the Court has done.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Each input is one fact the person can state, with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The Minister is not a
-- seat: where a layer-1 rule asks "is the person the Minister" this layer passes FALSE, and the one question about the Minister asks
-- what his power means for the company's members and directors. "Declared company under Part 9" is a term of another part: asked as a fact.
-- A debenture-holder's standing takes "I hold a debenture of the company" as a fact; the meaning of "debenture" is s 4(1) and is not
-- recomputed here (NOTES.md, Seams).

§ `Section 216: the personal remedy for oppression or injustice -- may I apply, and on what ground`

-- These questions are for a member, a person to whom shares have been transmitted, or a holder of a debenture who thinks the company is being run unfairly. Ask them when you are considering an application to the Court under section 216.

@ref s 216(1)
@export Under section 216(1), may I, as a member, a person to whom shares have been transmitted by operation of law, or a holder of a debenture of a company, apply to the Court for an order on the ground of oppression or injustice? JUST TRUE means the section lets me; NOTHING means the section does not say.
GIVEN `the company was incorporated under the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company incorporated under the Companies Act 1967?
      `the company was incorporated under an earlier written law relating to companies that corresponds with a provision of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company incorporated under an earlier written law relating to companies, once in force in Singapore, that corresponds with a provision of the Companies Act 1967? (Answer no if it was incorporated under the Companies Act itself.)
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member (shareholder) of the company?
      `shares in the company have been transmitted to me by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have shares in the company been transmitted to you by operation of law (for example on a member's death or bankruptcy)? Answer no if you became a member in the ordinary way.
      `I hold a debenture of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a debenture of the company (debenture stock, a bond, a note or any other security of the company, but not a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of money or bill of exchange)?
      `I would apply to the General Division of the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you make the application to the General Division of the High Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216(1), may I apply to the Court for an order on the ground of oppression or injustice` IS
