GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216A(3), am I barred from bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, in the company's name` IS
    `s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` `I would bring the action or arbitration, or make the intervention, under section 216A` `the number of directors of the company` `the number of directors I gave the notice to` `my notice said that I intend to apply to the Court if the directors do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action or arbitration` `the date I gave the notice` `the date I will apply to the Court` `I am acting in good faith` `it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company that the action or arbitration be brought, prosecuted, defended or discontinued`

@ref s 216A(4)
@export Under section 216A(4), where I establish to the satisfaction of the Court that it is not expedient to give the notice section 216A(3)(a) requires, may the Court make an interim order pending my giving the notice?
GIVEN `I have established to the satisfaction of the Court that it is not expedient to give notice as required in subsection (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established to the satisfaction of the Court that it is not expedient to give the directors the notice section 216A(3)(a) requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216A(4), may the Court make an interim order pending my giving notice because it is not expedient to give it now` IS
    `s 216A(4) the Court may make an interim order pending the complainant giving notice` `I have established to the satisfaction of the Court that it is not expedient to give notice as required in subsection (3)(a)`

@ref s 216A(5)
@export Under section 216A(5), in granting me permission, may the Court make such orders or interim orders as it thinks fit in the interests of justice?
GIVEN `the Court is granting me permission under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court granting you permission under section 216A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216A(5), may the Court make orders or interim orders in the interests of justice when it grants me permission` IS
    `s 216A(5) the Court may make the orders or interim orders it thinks fit in the interests of justice` `the Court is granting me permission under section 216A`

@ref s 216A(5)(a)
@export Under section 216A(5)(a), in granting me permission, may the Court make an order authorising me or any other person to control the conduct of the action or arbitration?
GIVEN `the Court is granting me permission under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court granting you permission under section 216A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216A(5)(a), may the Court authorise me or another person to control the conduct of the action or arbitration` IS
    `s 216A(5)(a) the Court may make an order authorising the complainant or any other person to control the conduct of the action or arbitration` `the Court is granting me permission under section 216A`

@ref s 216A(5)(b)
@export Under section 216A(5)(b), in granting me permission, may the Court make an order giving directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person so authorised?
GIVEN `the Court is granting me permission under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court granting you permission under section 216A?
      `a person has been authorised to control the conduct of the action or arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person been authorised to control the conduct of the action or arbitration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216A(5)(b), may the Court give directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person authorised` IS
    `s 216A(5)(b) the Court may make an order giving directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person so authorised` `the Court is granting me permission under section 216A` `a person has been authorised to control the conduct of the action or arbitration`

@ref s 216A(5)(c)
@export Under section 216A(5)(c), in granting me permission, may the Court order the company to pay the reasonable legal fees and disbursements I incurred in connection with the action or arbitration?
GIVEN `the Court is granting me permission under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court granting you permission under section 216A?
      `the legal fees and disbursements are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the legal fees and disbursements reasonable?
      `I incurred the legal fees and disbursements in connection with the action or arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you incur the legal fees and disbursements in connection with the action or arbitration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216A(5)(c), may the Court order the company to pay my reasonable legal fees and disbursements for the action or arbitration` IS
    `s 216A(5)(c) the Court may make an order requiring the company to pay the complainant's legal fees and disbursements` `the Court is granting me permission under section 216A` `the legal fees and disbursements are reasonable` `I incurred the legal fees and disbursements in connection with the action or arbitration`

@ref s 216A(6)
@export Under section 216A(6), where the action has been commenced or is to be brought in the State Courts, must my application for permission be made in a District Court?
GIVEN `the action has been commenced or is to be brought in the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the action been commenced, or is it to be brought, in the State Courts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216A(6), must my application for permission be made in a District Court` IS
    `s 216A(6) the application for permission is required to be made in a District Court` `the action has been commenced or is to be brought in the State Courts`

§ `Section 216B: the members' approval, Court approval to discontinue, and interim costs`

-- Ask these once your application or action under section 216A is under way.

@ref s 216B(1)
@export Under section 216B(1), must my application or action under section 216A not be stayed or dismissed by reason only that it is shown that an alleged breach of a right or duty owed to the company has been or may be approved by the members?
GIVEN `my application is made, or my action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application made, or your action brought or intervened in, under section 216A?
      `the only reason for the stay or dismissal is that it is shown that an alleged breach of a right or duty owed to the company has been or may be approved by the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason for the stay or dismissal that it is shown that an alleged breach of a right or duty owed to the company has been or may be approved by the members of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216B(1), is a stay or dismissal of my application or action barred where the only reason is that the members have approved, or may approve, the alleged breach` IS
    `s 216B(1) the stay or dismissal is barred where the only reason is the members' approval of the alleged breach` `my application is made, or my action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` `the only reason for the stay or dismissal is that it is shown that an alleged breach of a right or duty owed to the company has been or may be approved by the members of the company`

@ref s 216B(1)
@export Under section 216B(1), may the Court take evidence of approval by the members into account in making an order under section 216A?
GIVEN `there is evidence of approval by the members of the alleged breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that the members have approved the alleged breach?
      `the Court is making an order under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court making an order under section 216A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216B(1), may the Court take the members' approval of the alleged breach into account in making an order under section 216A` IS
    `s 216B(1) the Court may take evidence of approval by the members into account in making an order under section 216A` `there is evidence of approval by the members of the alleged breach` `the Court is making an order under section 216A`

@ref s 216B(2)
@export Under section 216B(2), must my application or action under section 216A not be stayed, discontinued, settled or dismissed for want of prosecution without the approval of the Court?
GIVEN `my application is made, or my action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application made, or your action brought or intervened in, under section 216A?
      `what is sought in my application or action` IS A `s 216B(2) what is sought` @desc What is sought in your application or action: a stay, a discontinuance, a settlement, a dismissal for want of prosecution, or a dismissal for another reason?
      `the Court has approved it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court approved it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216B(2), is a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution of my application or action barred without the Court's approval` IS
    `s 216B(2) the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution is barred without the approval of the Court` `my application is made, or my action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` `what is sought in my application or action` `the Court has approved it`

@ref s 216B(2)
@export Under section 216B(2), may the Court give its approval to a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution upon such terms as it thinks fit?
GIVEN `my application is made, or my action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application made, or your action brought or intervened in, under section 216A?
      `the Court is giving its approval to the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court giving its approval to the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216B(2), may the Court give its approval on such terms as it thinks fit` IS
    `s 216B(2) the Court may give its approval upon such terms as it thinks fit` `my application is made, or my action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` `the Court is giving its approval to the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution`

@ref s 216B(2)
@export Under section 216B(2), if the Court determines that my interest may be substantially affected by a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal, may the Court order any party to give me notice?
GIVEN `my application is made, or my action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application made, or your action brought or intervened in, under section 216A?
      `the Court has determined that the interest of a complainant may be substantially affected by the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court determined that the interest of any complainant may be substantially affected by the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216B(2), may the Court order a party to give me notice of a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal` IS
    `s 216B(2) the Court may order a party to give notice to the complainant` `my application is made, or my action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` `the Court has determined that the interest of a complainant may be substantially affected by the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal`

@ref s 216B(3)
@export Under section 216B(3), in my application or action under section 216A, may the Court at any time order the company to pay me interim costs, including legal fees and disbursements?
GIVEN `my application is made, or my action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application made, or your action brought or intervened in, under section 216A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216B(3), may the Court order the company to pay me interim costs` IS
    `s 216B(3) the Court may order the company to pay the complainant interim costs` `my application is made, or my action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A`

@ref s 216B(3)
@export Under section 216B(3), may I be accountable for interim costs the Court ordered the company to pay me, upon final disposition of my application or action?
GIVEN `the Court has ordered the company to pay me interim costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered the company to pay you interim costs?
      `my application or action has been finally disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your application or action been finally disposed of?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 216B(3), may I be made accountable for the interim costs when my application or action is finally disposed of` IS
    `s 216B(3) the complainant may be accountable for the interim costs` `the Court has ordered the company to pay me interim costs` `my application or action has been finally disposed of`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sge (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- PART 10A, TRANSFER OF REGISTRATION, ss 355 to 364A -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- This is a rendering of the text for study, not the official text; it is not endorsed by the Singapore Government or the Attorney-General's Chambers.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, company secretary or member of a company, or who deals with one, here:
-- the director of a foreign corporate entity that wants to be registered in Singapore (before registration), and a director, secretary or
-- member of the company it becomes (after registration), or a person who deals with that company (a holder of shares, debentures or a share
-- warrant, a person interested in a charge). Part 10A provides for a transfer of registration INTO Singapore only. There is no seat for the
-- Registrar, the Minister or the Court: their powers appear below only as what they mean to the person asking.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person would ask. Nothing here is
-- new law, and no rule is restated: every question calls a layer-1 function and passes it plain facts.
--
-- READING AN ANSWER. Every question asks yes or no in the direction its name says, and its answer is JUST TRUE (yes), JUST FALSE (the text
-- says no in its own words) or NOTHING (the text does not say). NOTHING is never "no". A question whose layer-1 function is a bar is named as
-- the bar; one whose layer-1 function is a permission is named as the permission.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs, one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person is asked,
-- and a fact has the same name and the same @desc in every question that asks it. Two judgments the Part leaves to others are taken as
-- plain facts: whether the Registrar "thinks fit" (s 359(1)) and what the Registrar "is satisfied" of (s 360). The figures the Minister may
-- prescribe (the form, manner, particulars, other documents and fee of s 358(2)) are asked as yes or no: whether the prescribed thing was done.

§ `Sections 355 and 356: whether Part 10A applies to the body, and the words it defines`

-- s 355: layer-1 rule called: `s 355 this Part applies to the body`
@export Under section 355, does Part 10A of the Companies Act apply to the body I act for?
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a body corporate (a legal person of its own, not an unincorporated group)?
      `the body is incorporated outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the body incorporated outside Singapore?
      `the body intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under the Companies Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body intend to be registered in Singapore as a company limited by shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 355, does Part 10A of the Companies Act apply to the body I act for` IS
    `s 355 this Part applies to the body` `the body is a foreign corporate entity as section 356 defines it` `the body intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under the Companies Act`
    WHERE
        `the body is a foreign corporate entity as section 356 defines it` MEANS `s 356 "foreign corporate entity" the body is a foreign corporate entity` `the body is a body corporate` `the body is incorporated outside Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 356: layer-1 rule called: `s 356 "foreign corporate entity" the body is a foreign corporate entity`
@export Under section 356, is the body I act for a foreign corporate entity?
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a body corporate (a legal person of its own, not an unincorporated group)?
      `the body is incorporated outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the body incorporated outside Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 356, is the body I act for a foreign corporate entity` IS
    `s 356 "foreign corporate entity" the body is a foreign corporate entity` `the body is a body corporate` `the body is incorporated outside Singapore`

-- s 356: layer-1 rule called: `s 356 "date of registration" the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity`
@export Under section 356, what is the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity?
GIVEN `the entity has applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under Part 10A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity applied to be registered in Singapore as a company limited by shares under Part 10A of the Companies Act?
      `the Registrar has issued a notice of transfer of registration for the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar issued a notice of transfer of registration for the entity?
      `the date of registration the notice of transfer of registration specifies` IS A DATE @desc What date of registration does the notice of transfer of registration specify? (day, month, year)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 356, what is the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity` IS
    `s 356 "date of registration" the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity` `the entity has applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under Part 10A` `the Registrar has issued a notice of transfer of registration for the entity` `the date of registration the notice of transfer of registration specifies`

-- s 356: layer-1 rule called: `s 356 "place of incorporation" the place of incorporation of the foreign corporate entity`
@export Under section 356, what is the place of incorporation of the foreign corporate entity?
GIVEN `the entity transferred its domicile after it was incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the entity transfer its domicile to another jurisdiction after it was incorporated?
      `the jurisdiction where the entity is domiciled when it applies for registration` IS A STRING @desc In which jurisdiction is the entity domiciled at the time it applies for registration?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under section 356, what is the place of incorporation of the foreign corporate entity` IS
    `s 356 "place of incorporation" the place of incorporation of the foreign corporate entity` `the entity transferred its domicile after it was incorporated` `the jurisdiction where the entity is domiciled when it applies for registration`

-- s 356: layer-1 rule called: `s 356 "register" and "registered" the foreign corporate entity is registered`
@export Under section 356, is the foreign corporate entity registered?
GIVEN `the entity has applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under Part 10A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity applied to be registered in Singapore as a company limited by shares under Part 10A of the Companies Act?
      `the Registrar has registered the entity under section 359(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar registered the entity under section 359(1) of the Companies Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 356, is the foreign corporate entity registered` IS
    `s 356 "register" and "registered" the foreign corporate entity is registered` `the entity has applied to be registered as a company limited by shares under Part 10A` `the Registrar has registered the entity under section 359(1)`

§ `Section 357: reserving the name of the intended company`

-- s 357(1): layer-1 rule called: `s 357(1) the foreign corporate entity must apply to reserve the name of the intended company`
@export Under section 357(1), must the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to reserve the name of the intended company?
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a body corporate (a legal person of its own, not an unincorporated group)?
      `the body is incorporated outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the body incorporated outside Singapore?
      `the body intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under the Companies Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body intend to be registered in Singapore as a company limited by shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 357(1), must the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to reserve the name of the intended company` IS
    `s 357(1) the foreign corporate entity must apply to reserve the name of the intended company` `the body is a foreign corporate entity as section 356 defines it` `the body intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under the Companies Act`
    WHERE
        `the body is a foreign corporate entity as section 356 defines it` MEANS `s 356 "foreign corporate entity" the body is a foreign corporate entity` `the body is a body corporate` `the body is incorporated outside Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 357(2): layer-1 rule called: `s 357(2) section 27 applies to and in respect of the application`
@export Under section 357(2), does section 27 apply to and in respect of my application to reserve the name?
GIVEN `the application is one to reserve the name of the company the entity intends to become` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one under section 357(1) to reserve the name of the company the entity intends to become?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 357(2), does section 27 apply to and in respect of my application to reserve the name` IS
    `s 357(2) section 27 applies to and in respect of the application` `the application is one to reserve the name of the company the entity intends to become`

-- s 357(3): layer-1 rule called: `s 357(3) the subsection bars the registration of the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)`
@export Under section 357(3), does the section bar registration of the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)?
GIVEN `the name the entity is to be registered under has been reserved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the name that the entity is to be registered under been reserved for it under section 27, as section 357(2) applies it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 357(3), does the section bar registration of the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)` IS
    `s 357(3) the subsection bars the registration of the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)` `the name the entity is to be registered under has been reserved`

§ `Section 358: applying to be registered`

-- s 358(1): layer-1 rule called: `s 358(1) the foreign corporate entity may apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares`
@export Under section 358(1), may the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares?
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a body corporate (a legal person of its own, not an unincorporated group)?
      `the body is incorporated outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the body incorporated outside Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 358(1), may the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares` IS
    `s 358(1) the foreign corporate entity may apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares` `the body is a foreign corporate entity as section 356 defines it`
    WHERE
        `the body is a foreign corporate entity as section 356 defines it` MEANS `s 356 "foreign corporate entity" the body is a foreign corporate entity` `the body is a body corporate` `the body is incorporated outside Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 358(2): layer-1 rule called: `s 358(2) the application meets the requirements of the subsection`
@export Under section 358(2), does the application meet the requirements of the subsection?
GIVEN `the application is made in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made in the form that is prescribed?
      `the application is made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made in the manner that is prescribed?
      `the application contains the prescribed particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application contain the particulars that are prescribed?
      `the entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the entity have a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation?
      `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a copy of that instrument accompany the application?
      `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy certified, in the prescribed manner, to be a true copy of the instrument?
      `the constitution the entity proposes to be registered under accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the constitution by which the entity proposes to be registered accompany the application?
      `all the other documents prescribed for the application accompany it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the other documents prescribed for the application accompany it? (answer yes if none is prescribed)
      `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prescribed fee accompany the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 358(2), does the application meet the requirements of the subsection` IS
    `s 358(2) the application meets the requirements of the subsection` `the application the person describes`
    WHERE
        `the application the person describes` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
            `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS `the application is made in the prescribed form`
            `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS `the application is made in the prescribed manner`
            `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS `the application contains the prescribed particulars`
            `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS `the entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation`
            `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application`
            `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy`
            `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS `the constitution the entity proposes to be registered under accompanies the application`
            `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS `all the other documents prescribed for the application accompany it`
            `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS `the prescribed fee accompanies the application`

-- s 358(2)(b): layer-1 rule called: `s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires`
@export Under section 358(2)(b), is the application accompanied as the paragraph requires?
GIVEN `the entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the entity have a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation?
      `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a copy of that instrument accompany the application?
      `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy certified, in the prescribed manner, to be a true copy of the instrument?
      `the constitution the entity proposes to be registered under accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the constitution by which the entity proposes to be registered accompany the application?
      `all the other documents prescribed for the application accompany it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the other documents prescribed for the application accompany it? (answer yes if none is prescribed)
      `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prescribed fee accompany the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 358(2)(b), is the application accompanied as the paragraph requires` IS
    `s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires` `the application the person describes`
    WHERE
        `the application the person describes` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the paragraph this question asks about, (b), does not read the next three fields (form, manner, particulars are paragraph (a)).
            `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS TRUE
            `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS TRUE
            `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS TRUE
            `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS `the entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation`
            `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application`
            `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy`
            `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS `the constitution the entity proposes to be registered under accompanies the application`
            `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS `all the other documents prescribed for the application accompany it`
            `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS `the prescribed fee accompanies the application`

-- s 358(3): layer-1 rule called: `s 358(3) the Registrar may require the applicant to furnish further information or documents`
@export Under section 358(3), may the Registrar require me as applicant to furnish further information or documents?
GIVEN `I am an applicant for registration, or act for one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or is the entity you act for, an applicant for registration under section 358(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 358(3), may the Registrar require me as applicant to furnish further information or documents` IS
    `s 358(3) the Registrar may require the applicant to furnish further information or documents` `I am an applicant for registration, or act for one`

§ `Section 359: registration, the notice of transfer, and deregistration abroad`

-- s 359(1): layer-1 rule called: `s 359(1) the Registrar may register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares`
-- Section 359(1) is "Subject to section 360" only. The separate bar of section 357(3) (no registration without a reserved name) is asked by its own question above, not here: each section answers for itself (ruling E1 of 2026-11-04, option C).
@export Under section 359(1), may the Registrar register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares?
GIVEN `the Registrar says section 360 requires it to refuse to register the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar said that section 360 requires it to refuse to register the entity?
      `the entity has complied with section 358` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity complied with section 358 (its application and what must accompany it)?
      `the Registrar thinks fit to register the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Registrar think fit to register the entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
