    `s 362(5) the company has ceased to be a company as defined in section 4(1)` `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette` `the date I ask about`

-- s 362(5): layer-1 rule called: `s 362(5) the provisions of this Act have ceased to apply to the company`
@export Under section 362(5), have the provisions of the Act ceased to apply to the company?
GIVEN `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the notice of the order of revocation been published in the Gazette?
      `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of the order of revocation published in the Gazette? (day, month, year; any date if it has not been)
      `the date I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which date do you want the answer? (day, month, year)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 362(5), have the provisions of the Act ceased to apply to the company` IS
    `s 362(5) the provisions of this Act have ceased to apply to the company` `the notice of the order of revocation has been published in the Gazette` `the date the notice of the order of revocation was published in the Gazette` `the date I ask about`

-- s 362(6): layer-1 rule called: `s 362(6) the order of revocation is final`
@export Under section 362(6), is the order of revocation final?
GIVEN `the order is an order of revocation made under section 362(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order an order of revocation made under section 362(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 362(6), is the order of revocation final` IS
    `s 362(6) the order of revocation is final` `the order is an order of revocation made under section 362(3)`

-- s 362(7): layer-1 rule called: `s 362(7) the liability of the person continues despite the order of revocation`
@export Under section 362(7), does my liability continue despite the order of revocation?
GIVEN `an order of revocation has been made under section 362(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order of revocation been made under section 362(3)?
      `I am an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company?
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `I have a liability in respect of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a liability in respect of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 362(7), does my liability continue despite the order of revocation` IS
    `s 362(7) the liability of the person continues despite the order of revocation` `an order of revocation has been made under section 362(3)` `I am an officer of the company` `I am a member of the company` `I have a liability in respect of the company`

-- s 362(8): layer-1 rule called: `s 362(8) section 362 prejudices the enforcement of the right or claim`
@export Under section 362(8), does section 362 prejudice the enforcement of the right or claim?
GIVEN `the enforcement of the right or claim` IS A `s 362(8) enforcement` @desc Which do you ask about: a person enforcing a right or claim against the company, the company enforcing one against a person, or some other enforcement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 362(8), does section 362 prejudice the enforcement of the right or claim` IS
    `s 362(8) section 362 prejudices the enforcement of the right or claim` `the enforcement of the right or claim`

§ `Section 363: charges that existed before registration`

-- s 363(1): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(1) a statement of the charge must be lodged with the Registrar`
@export Under section 363(1), must a statement of the charge be lodged with the Registrar?
GIVEN `the charge existed before the entity was registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the charge exist before the entity was registered?
      `the charge would have had to be registered under Division 8 of Part 4 had the entity been incorporated under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the charge have had to be registered under Division 8 of Part 4 if the entity had been incorporated as a company under the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363(1), must a statement of the charge be lodged with the Registrar` IS
    `s 363(1) a statement of the charge must be lodged with the Registrar` `the charge existed before the entity was registered` `the charge would have had to be registered under Division 8 of Part 4 had the entity been incorporated under the Act`

-- s 363(1): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(1) the last day for lodging the statement of the charge`
@export Under section 363(1), what is the last day for lodging the statement of the charge?
GIVEN `the date of registration of the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company registered? (day, month, year)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 363(1), what is the last day for lodging the statement of the charge` IS
    `s 363(1) the last day for lodging the statement of the charge` `the date of registration of the company`

-- s 363(1): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(1) the statement of the charge has been lodged as the subsection requires`
@export Under section 363(1), has the statement of the charge been lodged as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the date of registration of the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company registered? (day, month, year)
      `a statement of the charge has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a statement of the charge been lodged with the Registrar?
      `the statement was lodged in the prescribed manner and has the prescribed particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement lodged in the prescribed manner, and does it contain the prescribed particulars of the charge?
      `the date the statement was lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the statement lodged? (day, month, year; any date if it has not been)
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is the date today? (day, month, year)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363(1), has the statement of the charge been lodged as the subsection requires` IS
    `s 363(1) the statement of the charge has been lodged as the subsection requires` `the date of registration of the company` `a statement of the charge has been lodged with the Registrar` `the statement was lodged in the prescribed manner and has the prescribed particulars` `the date the statement was lodged` `the date today`

-- s 363(2): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(2) the person may lodge the documents and particulars required to be lodged`
@export Under section 363(2), may I lodge the documents and particulars required to be lodged?
GIVEN `I am the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company concerned?
      `I am interested in the documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person interested in the documents?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363(2), may I lodge the documents and particulars required to be lodged` IS
    `s 363(2) the person may lodge the documents and particulars required to be lodged` `I am the company concerned` `I am interested in the documents`

-- s 363(3): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(3) the person is entitled to recover the fees from the company`
@export Under section 363(3), am I entitled to recover the fees from the company?
GIVEN `the registration was effected by a person other than the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the registration effected by a person other than the company concerned?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363(3), am I entitled to recover the fees from the company` IS
    `s 363(3) the person is entitled to recover the fees from the company` `the registration was effected by a person other than the company concerned`

-- s 363(3): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(3) the amount of fees the person is entitled to recover from the company`
@export Under section 363(3), how much in fees am I entitled to recover from the company?
GIVEN `the registration was effected by a person other than the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the registration effected by a person other than the company concerned?
      `the fees I properly paid for the registration, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in Singapore dollars, did you properly pay in fees for the registration?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 363(3), how much in fees am I entitled to recover from the company` IS
    `s 363(3) the amount of fees the person is entitled to recover from the company` `the registration was effected by a person other than the company concerned` `the fees I properly paid for the registration, in Singapore dollars`

-- s 363(4): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(4) the person is guilty of an offence`
@export Under section 363(4), is the person I ask about guilty of an offence?
GIVEN `default has been made in complying with section 363(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 363(1) (lodging the statement of the charge)?
      `the person I ask about is the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you ask about the company itself?
      `the person I ask about is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you ask about an officer of the company who is in default (as section 408(3) defines it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363(4), is the person I ask about guilty of an offence` IS
    `s 363(4) the person is guilty of an offence` `default has been made in complying with section 363(1)` `the person I ask about is the company` `the person I ask about is an officer of the company who is in default`

-- s 363(4): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction`
@export Under section 363(4), what is the most the person I ask about may be sentenced to on conviction?
GIVEN `default has been made in complying with section 363(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 363(1) (lodging the statement of the charge)?
      `the person I ask about is the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you ask about the company itself?
      `the person I ask about is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you ask about an officer of the company who is in default (as section 408(3) defines it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 363(4) penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 363(4), what is the most the person I ask about may be sentenced to on conviction` IS
    `s 363(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `default has been made in complying with section 363(1)` `the person I ask about is the company` `the person I ask about is an officer of the company who is in default`

-- s 363(5): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(5) the failure to comply with section 363(1) affects the continuity of status, operation or effect of the thing of the charge`
@export Under section 363(5), does a failure to comply with section 363(1) affect the continuity of status, operation or effect of the charge?
GIVEN `there has been a failure to comply with section 363(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been a failure to comply with section 363(1)?
      `the thing of the charge` IS A `s 363(5) what of the charge` @desc Which do you ask about: a security, a right, a priority or an obligation of the charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363(5), does a failure to comply with section 363(1) affect the continuity of status, operation or effect of the charge` IS
    `s 363(5) the failure to comply with section 363(1) affects the continuity of status, operation or effect of the thing of the charge` `there has been a failure to comply with section 363(1)` `the thing of the charge`

-- s 363(6): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(6) the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified`
@export Under section 363(6), may the Court order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified?
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied the omission or mis-statement was accidental, inadvertent or had some other sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that the omission or mis-statement was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause?
      `the Court is satisfied the omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice creditors or shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that the omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders?
      `the Court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief?
      `the application to the Court is made by the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application to the Court made by the company concerned?
      `the application to the Court is made by a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application to the Court made by a person interested?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363(6), may the Court order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` IS
    `s 363(6) the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` `the Court is satisfied the omission or mis-statement was accidental, inadvertent or had some other sufficient cause` `the Court is satisfied the omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice creditors or shareholders` `the Court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` `the application to the Court is made by the company concerned` `the application to the Court is made by a person interested`

-- s 363(6): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(6) the Court may impose the term or condition on its order`
@export Under section 363(6), may the Court impose the term or condition on its order?
GIVEN `the term or condition seems to the Court just and expedient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term or condition seem to the Court just and expedient?
      `the term or condition is that the rectification is without prejudice to any liability already incurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the term or condition that the rectification is to be without prejudice to any liability already incurred by the company or any of its officers in respect of the default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363(6), may the Court impose the term or condition on its order` IS
    `s 363(6) the Court may impose the term or condition on its order` `the term or condition seems to the Court just and expedient` `the term or condition is that the rectification is without prejudice to any liability already incurred`

-- s 363(7): layer-1 rule called: `s 363(7) the section applies to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied`
@export Under section 363(7), does the section apply to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied?
GIVEN `the charge is required to be lodged under section 363(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge required to be lodged under section 363(1)?
      `the section of the Act` IS A `s 363(7) section` @desc Which section do you ask about: section 134, 135, 136 or 138, or another?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363(7), does the section apply to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` IS
    `s 363(7) the section applies to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` `the charge is required to be lodged under section 363(1)` `the section of the Act`

§ `Section 364: certificates, share warrants and the Court's order`

-- s 364(1): layer-1 rule called: `s 364(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of the person`
@export Under section 364(1), must the company complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of me?
