GIVEN `the date of registration of the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company registered? (day, month, year)
      `the company has completed and has ready for delivery appropriate certificates for all registered holders of existing shares or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company completed, and does it have ready for delivery, appropriate certificates for all persons registered as holders of existing shares or debentures as at the date of registration?
      `the date the certificates were completed and ready for delivery` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the certificates completed and ready for delivery? (day, month, year; any date if they are not)
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is the date today? (day, month, year)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 364(1), has the company completed the certificates, and does it have them ready for delivery, within 60 days after the date of registration` IS
    `s 364(1) the company has completed and has ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` `the date of registration of the company` `the company has completed and has ready for delivery appropriate certificates for all registered holders of existing shares or debentures` `the date the certificates were completed and ready for delivery` `the date today`

-- s 364(2): layer-1 rule called: `s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to be operative`
@export Under section 364(2), has my prior certificate ceased to be operative?
GIVEN `my prior certificate is for shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered to their holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your prior certificate for shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered to their holders?
      `the new certificates have been delivered to the holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the new certificates been delivered to the holders under section 364(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 364(2), has my prior certificate ceased to be operative` IS
    `s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to be operative` `my prior certificate is for shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered to their holders` `the new certificates have been delivered to the holders`

-- s 364(2): layer-1 rule called: `s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to have any validity for the purposes of this Act`
@export Under section 364(2), has my prior certificate ceased to have any validity for the purposes of the Act?
GIVEN `my prior certificate is for shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered to their holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your prior certificate for shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered to their holders?
      `the new certificates have been delivered to the holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the new certificates been delivered to the holders under section 364(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 364(2), has my prior certificate ceased to have any validity for the purposes of the Act` IS
    `s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to have any validity for the purposes of this Act` `my prior certificate is for shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered to their holders` `the new certificates have been delivered to the holders`

-- s 364(3): layer-1 rule called: `s 364(3) the share warrant is void`
@export Under section 364(3), is the share warrant void?
GIVEN `the document is a share warrant stating that the bearer is entitled to the shares and enabling transfer by delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a share warrant stating that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares specified in it and enabling the shares to be transferred by delivery of the warrant?
      `the share warrant was issued by the foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the share warrant issued by the foreign corporate entity?
      `the date the share warrant was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the share warrant issued? (day, month, year)
      `the date of registration of the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company registered? (day, month, year)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 364(3), is the share warrant void` IS
    `s 364(3) the share warrant is void` `the document is a share warrant stating that the bearer is entitled to the shares and enabling transfer by delivery` `the share warrant was issued by the foreign corporate entity` `the date the share warrant was issued` `the date of registration of the company`

-- s 364(4): layer-1 rule called: `s 364(4) the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice`
@export Under section 364(4), has the company failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice?
GIVEN `a notice has been served on the company requiring it to make good a default in complying with section 364` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice been served on the company requiring it to make good a default in complying with section 364?
      `the date the notice was served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice served? (day, month, year)
      `the company has made good the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made good the default?
      `the date the company made good the default` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company make good the default? (day, month, year; any date if it has not)
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is the date today? (day, month, year)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 364(4), has the company failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` IS
    `s 364(4) the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` `a notice has been served on the company requiring it to make good a default in complying with section 364` `the date the notice was served` `the company has made good the default` `the date the company made good the default` `the date today`

-- s 364(4): layer-1 rule called: `s 364(4) the Court may make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default`
@export Under section 364(4), may the Court make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default?
GIVEN `a notice has been served on the company requiring it to make good a default in complying with section 364` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice been served on the company requiring it to make good a default in complying with section 364?
      `the date the notice was served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice served? (day, month, year)
      `the company has made good the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made good the default?
      `the date the company made good the default` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company make good the default? (day, month, year; any date if it has not)
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is the date today? (day, month, year)
      `the application to the Court is made by the person entitled to have the certificates or debentures delivered to that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application to the Court made by the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to that person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 364(4), may the Court make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default` IS
    `s 364(4) the Court may make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default` `the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice, as section 364(4) reads` `the application to the Court is made by the person entitled to have the certificates or debentures delivered to that person`
    WHERE
        `the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice, as section 364(4) reads` MEANS `s 364(4) the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` `a notice has been served on the company requiring it to make good a default in complying with section 364` `the date the notice was served` `the company has made good the default` `the date the company made good the default` `the date today` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 364(4): layer-1 rule called: `s 364(4) the order may direct the person to make good the default`
@export Under section 364(4), may the order direct the person I ask about to make good the default?
GIVEN `the person the order might address` IS A `s 364(4) person` @desc Which do you ask about: the company, an officer of the company who is in default, an officer who is not in default, or another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 364(4), may the order direct the person I ask about to make good the default` IS
    `s 364(4) the order may direct the person to make good the default` `the person the order might address`

-- s 364(4): layer-1 rule called: `s 364(4) the order may provide that the costs of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the person`
@export Under section 364(4), may the order provide that the costs are to be borne by the person I ask about?
GIVEN `the person the order might address` IS A `s 364(4) person` @desc Which do you ask about: the company, an officer of the company who is in default, an officer who is not in default, or another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 364(4), may the order provide that the costs are to be borne by the person I ask about` IS
    `s 364(4) the order may provide that the costs of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the person` `the person the order might address`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sgg (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026",
-- Part 11 Division 2 (foreign companies), ss 365 to 386 -- THE SEAT LAYER (part sgg, layer 2).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a secretary or a member of a foreign company, or its authorised representative,
-- or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what Division 2 of Part 11 requires or lets them do. There is never a seat for the Registrar,
-- the Minister, the Authority or the Court: a provision addressed to one of them is asked here only for what it means to the person (may the
-- foreign company appeal, must a notice be lodged, is a name barred), never as a question the official answers.
--
-- THE QUESTIONS. Every question is named "Under section N, ..." and asks what its body answers: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text's no,
-- NOTHING is "the text does not say". A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Each question is the layer-1 function of the same section,
-- called with the facts the person states; no rule is restated here. The questions follow the text, section by section.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every input is a yes/no, a number, a date, a string or one of the modules' own choices (the person's role, the kind of activity,
-- the kind of change, the earlier holder of a name, the provision not complied with), each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- The two records the modules take (`s 4(1) body`, ten facts about a body; `s 368(1) lodgment`, fifteen facts about what has been lodged) are built
-- inside the question, in its WHERE, from those answers. The date a person asks on is the shared input `the date asked`.
-- A fact keeps one name and one @desc in every question that asks it. Amounts, periods and numbers the text leaves to regulations are inputs.
--
-- ONE QUESTION THE KEEL'S SHARED INPUT TABLE HAS THAT THIS LAYER DOES NOT USE: `the company is a foreign company registered under Part 11`.
-- Division 2 asks whether the company IS a foreign company (section 365) and whether it is registered, as separate facts, so it takes them as the
-- ten facts of the body and as `the foreign company is registered under this Division` where section 367 asks it.
--
-- The text is a rendering of the Act (an informal consolidation), not the official text; nothing here is verified against the official text.


§ `Section 365: Foreign companies to which this Division applies`

@export Under section 365, does this Division apply to the foreign company?
GIVEN `the company is a body corporate formed or incorporated or existing in Singapore or outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company is a body corporate formed or incorporated or existing in Singapore or outside Singapore?
      `the company is a company, corporation, society, association or other body incorporated outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company is a company, corporation, society, association or other body incorporated outside Singapore?
      `the company is an unincorporated society, association or other body which under the law of its place of origin may sue or be sued, or hold property in the name of the secretary or other officer of the body or association duly appointed for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company is an unincorporated society, association or other body which under the law of its place of origin may sue or be sued, or hold property in the name of the secretary or other officer of the body or association duly appointed for that purpose?
      `the company has its head office or principal place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company has its head office or principal place of business in Singapore?
      `the company is incorporated in Singapore and declared by notification of the Minister in the Gazette to be a public authority, an instrumentality or agency of the Government, or a body corporate which is not incorporated for commercial purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company is incorporated in Singapore and declared by notification of the Minister in the Gazette to be a public authority, an instrumentality or agency of the Government, or a body corporate which is not incorporated for commercial purposes?
      `the company is a corporation sole` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company is a corporation sole?
      `the company is a cooperative society` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company is a cooperative society?
      `the company is a registered trade union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company is a registered trade union?
      `the company is a platform work association registered under the Platform Workers Act 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company is a platform work association registered under the Platform Workers Act 2024?
      `the company is a limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company is a limited liability partnership?
      `the foreign company establishes a place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the foreign company establishes a place of business in Singapore?
      `the foreign company carries on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the foreign company carries on business in Singapore?
      `the foreign company intends to establish a place of business or carry on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the foreign company intends to establish a place of business or carry on business in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 365, does this Division apply to the foreign company` IS
    `s 365 this Division applies to the foreign company` `the company's body` `the foreign company establishes a place of business in Singapore` `the foreign company carries on business in Singapore` `the foreign company intends to establish a place of business or carry on business in Singapore`
    WHERE
        `the company's body` MEANS `s 4(1) body` WITH
            `it is a body corporate formed or incorporated or existing in Singapore or outside Singapore` IS `the company is a body corporate formed or incorporated or existing in Singapore or outside Singapore`
            `it is a company, corporation, society, association or other body incorporated outside Singapore` IS `the company is a company, corporation, society, association or other body incorporated outside Singapore`
            `it is an unincorporated society, association or other body which under the law of its place of origin may sue or be sued, or hold property in the name of the secretary or other officer of the body or association duly appointed for that purpose` IS `the company is an unincorporated society, association or other body which under the law of its place of origin may sue or be sued, or hold property in the name of the secretary or other officer of the body or association duly appointed for that purpose`
            `it has its head office or principal place of business in Singapore` IS `the company has its head office or principal place of business in Singapore`
            `it is incorporated in Singapore and declared by notification of the Minister in the Gazette to be a public authority, an instrumentality or agency of the Government, or a body corporate which is not incorporated for commercial purposes` IS `the company is incorporated in Singapore and declared by notification of the Minister in the Gazette to be a public authority, an instrumentality or agency of the Government, or a body corporate which is not incorporated for commercial purposes`
            `it is a corporation sole` IS `the company is a corporation sole`
            `it is a cooperative society` IS `the company is a cooperative society`
            `it is a registered trade union` IS `the company is a registered trade union`
            `it is a platform work association registered under the Platform Workers Act 2024` IS `the company is a platform work association registered under the Platform Workers Act 2024`
            `it is a limited liability partnership` IS `the company is a limited liability partnership`


