§ `Making good a default, relodging lost documents, the form of documents (sections 13 to 15)`

-- calls layer-1: s 13(1) the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice
@export Under section 13(1), did the corporation or person fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice?
GIVEN `the day the notice requiring the default to be made good was served on the corporation or person` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the notice requiring the default to be made good was served on the corporation or person?
      `the default was made good` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the default made good?
      `the day the default was made good` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the default made good?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 13(1), did the corporation or person fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` IS
    `s 13(1) the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` `the day the notice requiring the default to be made good was served on the corporation or person` (IF `the default was made good` THEN JUST `the day the default was made good` ELSE NOTHING)

-- calls layer-1: s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default
@export Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default?
GIVEN `the corporation or person made default in complying with a provision of this Act or of another law requiring the filing or lodging with the Registrar of a return, account or other document or the giving of notice to the Registrar of a matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation or person made default in complying with a provision of this Act or of another law requiring the filing or lodging with the Registrar of a return, account or other document or the giving of notice to the Registrar of a matter?
      `the requirement is imposed by the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the requirement is imposed by the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018?
      `the corporation or person made default in complying with a request of the Registrar to amend or complete and resubmit a document or to submit a fresh document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation or person made default in complying with a request of the Registrar to amend or complete and resubmit a document or to submit a fresh document?
      `the corporation or person made default in complying with a request of the Registrar under section 12D(7) to rectify an error, defect or inaccuracy in particulars or a document in the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation or person made default in complying with a request of the Registrar under section 12D(7) to rectify an error, defect or inaccuracy in particulars or a document in the register?
      `the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice requiring it to be done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice requiring it to be done?
      `the applicant is a member or creditor of the corporation, or the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is a member or creditor of the corporation, or the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` IS
    `s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` `the corporation or person made default in complying with a provision of this Act or of another law requiring the filing or lodging with the Registrar of a return, account or other document or the giving of notice to the Registrar of a matter` `the requirement is imposed by the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` `the corporation or person made default in complying with a request of the Registrar to amend or complete and resubmit a document or to submit a fresh document` `the corporation or person made default in complying with a request of the Registrar under section 12D(7) to rectify an error, defect or inaccuracy in particulars or a document in the register` `the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice requiring it to be done` `the applicant is a member or creditor of the corporation, or the Registrar`

-- calls layer-1: s 13(2) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the bearer
@export Under section 13(2), may the order provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the person I name?
GIVEN `the order is an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is an order under subsection (1)?
      `who the order provides is to bear the costs` IS A `s 13(2) bearer of the costs` @desc Who does the order provide is to bear the costs?
      `the officer is responsible for the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the officer is responsible for the default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 13(2), may the order provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the person I name` IS
    `s 13(2) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the bearer` `the order is an order under subsection (1)` `who the order provides is to bear the costs` `the officer is responsible for the default`

-- calls layer-1: s 13(3) this section limits the operation of the written law
@export Under section 13(3), does section 13 limit the operation of the written law?
GIVEN `the written law imposes penalties on a corporation or its officers or such person in respect of the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the written law imposes penalties on a corporation or its officers or such person in respect of the default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 13(3), does section 13 limit the operation of the written law` IS
    `s 13(3) this section limits the operation of the written law` `the written law imposes penalties on a corporation or its officers or such person in respect of the default`

-- calls layer-1: s 14(1) the corporation may apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged
@export Under section 14(1), may the corporation apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged?
GIVEN `the corporation was incorporated or registered under this Act or a corresponding previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the corporation was incorporated or registered under this Act or a corresponding previous written law?
      `the constitution or another document relating to the corporation, filed or lodged with the Registrar, has been lost or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the constitution or another document relating to the corporation, filed or lodged with the Registrar, has been lost or destroyed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 14(1), may the corporation apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged` IS
    `s 14(1) the corporation may apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged` `the corporation was incorporated or registered under this Act or a corresponding previous written law` `the constitution or another document relating to the corporation, filed or lodged with the Registrar, has been lost or destroyed`

-- calls layer-1: s 14(2) the Registrar may direct notice of the application to be given to such persons and in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit
@export Under section 14(2), may the Registrar direct notice of the application to be given to such persons and in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit?
