    `s 14(2) the Registrar may direct notice of the application to be given to such persons and in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit` `an application under subsection (1) has been made`

-- calls layer-1: s 14(3) the Registrar may certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original
@export Under section 14(3), may the Registrar certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original?
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the original document has been lost or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar is satisfied that the original document has been lost or destroyed?
      `the Registrar is satisfied of the date of the filing or lodging of the original document with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar is satisfied of the date of the filing or lodging of the original document with the Registrar?
      `the Registrar is satisfied that a copy of the document produced to the Registrar is a correct copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar is satisfied that a copy of the document produced to the Registrar is a correct copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 14(3), may the Registrar certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` IS
    `s 14(3) the Registrar may certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` `the Registrar is satisfied that the original document has been lost or destroyed` `the Registrar is satisfied of the date of the filing or lodging of the original document with the Registrar` `the Registrar is satisfied that a copy of the document produced to the Registrar is a correct copy`

-- calls layer-1: s 14(4) the copy has for all purposes the same force and effect as the original
@export Under section 14(4), does the copy for all purposes have the same force and effect as the original?
GIVEN `the copy has been lodged on a direction under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the copy has been lodged on a direction under subsection (3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
