    `s 14(4) the copy has for all purposes the same force and effect as the original` `the copy has been lodged on a direction under subsection (3)`

-- calls layer-1: s 14(4) the date from which the copy has the same force and effect as the original
@export Under section 14(4), from what date does the copy have the same force and effect as the original?
GIVEN `the copy has been lodged on a direction under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the copy has been lodged on a direction under subsection (3)?
      `the date mentioned in the certificate as the date of the filing or lodging of the original` IS A DATE @desc What is the date mentioned in the certificate as the date of the filing or lodging of the original?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 14(4), from what date does the copy have the same force and effect as the original` IS
    `s 14(4) the date from which the copy has the same force and effect as the original` `the copy has been lodged on a direction under subsection (3)` `the date mentioned in the certificate as the date of the filing or lodging of the original`

