-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sgi (wave 2; merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force from 6 May 2026 to 20 October 2026 -- Part 3 Division 2, ss 23 to 42A -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, the company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company incorporated under the Act, or of a foreign company registered under it, or who deals with one.
-- The Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership (assumed, not ruled).
-- There is never a seat for the Registrar, the Minister or the Court: their powers appear here only as what they mean to the individual ("must the Registrar issue my company a certificate", "may the Court set this contract aside").
--
-- This layer asks the questions of layer 1 (sgi-capacity, sgi-ultra-vires, sgi-director-transactions, sgi-alteration, sgi-names, sgi-name-changes, sgi-conversion, sgi-objects, sgi-constitution, sgi-contracts-seal) in the individual's words.
-- Nothing here is new law: every question calls one layer-1 rule on the inputs the person states, and none restates a rule.
-- The only thing built here is the record s 25D(1) wants, from its 13 plain yes/no inputs.
--
-- NAMES. Every question begins "Under section N," with the Act's own numbering, and asks in the direction its body answers.
-- JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text's own no, and NOTHING is "the text does not say" (see the NOTES.md section "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- Where the layer-1 rule is a bar, the question is put as the bar ("is the Registrar barred from ...", "must the Registrar refuse ..."); where it is a grant, as the grant ("may my company ...").
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Each input is one fact the person can state, with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- An input's @desc repeats the layer-1 fact as a yes/no question where the fact is a yes/no fact; the keel's shared inputs keep the keel's @desc (`the date asked`, `the number of directors of the company`, `the company is a private company`).
-- The input every liability question needs is named `the liability of the company's members`, the keel's shared name.
-- Where the person is the one the fact is about, the input is put in the first person ("I am an officer of the company who is in default").
--
-- NOT ASKED HERE. The regulative rules (the DEONTIC rules for the duties with a deadline) are exercised in the layer-1 tests with #TRACE; a seat question is a decision, and the matching question asks whether the duty has been complied with.
-- Layer-1 rules that only define a word for another rule (`s 25D(1)(c)`, `(d)` and `(e)`) are reached through the s 25D(1) question.
-- The rules nobody in the seat is addressed by (deleted subsections, the Minister's power to prescribe model constitutions in s 36(2), commencement) have no question; NOTES.md says why for each.

§ `Companies Act 1967, ss 23 to 42A -- the questions of a director, secretary, member or person dealing with a company`


§ `Capacity and powers of the company (ss 23, 24)`

@export Under section 23(1)(a), does my company have full capacity to carry on this business or activity, do this act or enter into this transaction?
GIVEN `a provision of this Act limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a provision of this Act limits the company's capacity to do the act?
      `another written law limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that another written law limits the company's capacity to do the act?
      `the company's constitution limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company's constitution limits the company's capacity to do the act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 23(1)(a), does my company have full capacity to carry on this business or activity, do this act or enter into this transaction` IS
    `s 23(1)(a) the company has full capacity to carry on or undertake the business or activity, do the act or enter into the transaction` `a provision of this Act limits the company's capacity to do the act` `another written law limits the company's capacity to do the act` `the company's constitution limits the company's capacity to do the act`

@export Under section 23(1)(b), does my company have full rights, powers and privileges for the purposes of paragraph (a)?
GIVEN `the rights, powers and privileges are for the purposes of the business, activity, act or transaction in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the rights, powers and privileges are for the purposes of the business, activity, act or transaction in paragraph (a)?
      `a provision of this Act limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a provision of this Act limits the company's capacity to do the act?
      `another written law limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that another written law limits the company's capacity to do the act?
      `the company's constitution limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company's constitution limits the company's capacity to do the act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 23(1)(b), does my company have full rights, powers and privileges for the purposes of paragraph (a)` IS
    `s 23(1)(b) the company has full rights, powers and privileges for the purposes of paragraph (a)` `the rights, powers and privileges are for the purposes of the business, activity, act or transaction in paragraph (a)` `a provision of this Act limits the company's capacity to do the act` `another written law limits the company's capacity to do the act` `the company's constitution limits the company's capacity to do the act`

@export Under section 23(1A), may my company have its objects included in its constitution?
GIVEN `the provision states the objects of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the provision states the objects of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 23(1A), may my company have its objects included in its constitution` IS
    `s 23(1A) the company may have its objects included in its constitution` `the provision states the objects of the company`

@export Under section 23(1B), may my company's constitution contain this provision?
GIVEN `the provision restricts the company's capacity, rights, powers or privileges` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the provision restricts the company's capacity, rights, powers or privileges?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 23(1B), may my company's constitution contain this provision` IS
    `s 23(1B) the constitution may contain the provision` `the provision restricts the company's capacity, rights, powers or privileges`

@export Under section 24(1), are my company's powers deemed to include power to make this provision for the benefit of its employees on the cessation or transfer of its business?
GIVEN `the provision is made in connection with a cessation of the whole or any part of the business carried on by the company or any subsidiary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision made in connection with a cessation of the whole or any part of the business carried on by the company or any subsidiary of the company?
      `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company or its subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company or its subsidiary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 24(1), are my company's powers deemed to include power to make this provision for the benefit of its employees on the cessation or transfer of its business` IS
    `s 24(1) the powers of the company are deemed to include power to make the provision` `the provision is made in connection with a cessation of the whole or any part of the business carried on by the company or any subsidiary of the company` `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company or its subsidiary`

@export Under section 24(2), does section 24(1) affect what my company's constitution says on how the power is exercised?
GIVEN `the constitution requires the exercise of the power to be approved by the company in general meeting or otherwise prescribes the manner in which the power is to be exercised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the constitution requires the exercise of the power to be approved by the company in general meeting or otherwise prescribes the manner in which the power is to be exercised?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 24(2), does section 24(1) affect what my company's constitution says on how the power is exercised` IS
    `s 24(2) subsection (1) affects the constitution's provision on how the power is exercised` `the constitution requires the exercise of the power to be approved by the company in general meeting or otherwise prescribes the manner in which the power is to be exercised`


§ `Acts beyond the company's capacity, and dealing with the company (ss 25 to 25B)`

@export Under section 25(1), is this act invalid by reason only of my company's lack of capacity or power?
GIVEN `the thing is an act or purported act of the company (including an agreement it enters into, or an act done on its behalf by an officer or agent under purported authority, express or implied), or a conveyance or transfer of property, real or personal, to or by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an act or purported act of the company (including an agreement it enters into, or an act done on its behalf by an officer or agent under purported authority, express or implied), or a conveyance or transfer of property, real or personal, to or by the company?
      `the company was without capacity or power to do the act or to execute or take the conveyance or transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company without capacity or power to do the act or to execute or take the conveyance or transfer?
      `that lack of capacity or power is the only ground on which the act is said to be invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that that lack of capacity or power is the only ground on which the act is said to be invalid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25(1), is this act invalid by reason only of my company's lack of capacity or power` IS
