      `the person is a body corporate with which the director is connected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a body corporate with which the director is connected, within the meaning of section 25D(2)(b)?
      `the person acts as trustee of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person act as trustee of a trust?
      `the beneficiaries of the trust include the director or a person connected with the director through the family or a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the trust's beneficiaries include the director, or a member of the director's family, or a body corporate with which the director is connected?
      `the terms of the trust confer a power on the trustees that may be exercised for the benefit of the director or such a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms of the trust give the trustees a power that may be used for the benefit of the director or such a person?
      `the trust is for the purposes of an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust for the purposes of an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme?
      `the person acts as partner of the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person act as a partner of the director?
      `the person acts as partner of a person connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person act as a partner of a person who is connected with the director through the family, a body corporate or a trust?
      `the person is a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed?
      `the director is a partner in the firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the director a partner in the firm?
      `a partner in the firm is a person connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a partner in the firm a person connected with the director through the family, a body corporate or a trust?
      `a partner in the firm is a firm in which the director or a connected person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a partner in the firm a firm in which the director, or a person connected with the director, is a partner?
      `the person is himself or herself a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person himself or herself a director of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25D(1), is the person a person connected with the director` IS
    `s 25D(1) the person is a person connected with the director`
        (`s 25D(1) person` OF `the person is a member of the director's family`, `the person is a body corporate with which the director is connected`, `the person acts as trustee of a trust`, `the beneficiaries of the trust include the director or a person connected with the director through the family or a body corporate`, `the terms of the trust confer a power on the trustees that may be exercised for the benefit of the director or such a person`, `the trust is for the purposes of an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme`, `the person acts as partner of the director`, `the person acts as partner of a person connected with the director`, `the person is a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed`, `the director is a partner in the firm`, `a partner in the firm is a person connected with the director`, `a partner in the firm is a firm in which the director or a connected person is a partner`, `the person is himself or herself a director of the company`)



§ `Altering the constitution and entrenching provisions (ss 26, 26A)`

@export Under section 26(1), may my company's constitution be altered or added to by this resolution?
GIVEN `the kind of resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution` @desc Which one applies: the kind of resolution?
      `this Act otherwise provides for the alteration or addition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that this Act otherwise provides for the alteration or addition?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(1), may my company's constitution be altered or added to by this resolution` IS
    `s 26(1) the constitution may be altered or added to by the resolution` `the kind of resolution` `this Act otherwise provides for the alteration or addition`

@export Under section 26(1AA), on and from what date does the alteration or addition form part of my company's original constitution?
GIVEN `the alteration or addition was made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the alteration or addition was made under subsection (1)?
      `the date of the special resolution` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for this: the date of the special resolution?
      `the resolution specifies a later date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the resolution specifies a later date?
      `the later date specified in the resolution` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for this: the later date specified in the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 26(1AA), on and from what date does the alteration or addition form part of my company's original constitution` IS
    `s 26(1AA) the date on and from which the alteration or addition forms part of the original constitution` `the alteration or addition was made under subsection (1)` `the date of the special resolution` `the resolution specifies a later date` `the later date specified in the resolution`

@export Under section 26(1AB), does the special resolution need to set out the text of the model constitution adopted?
GIVEN `the special resolution adopts the whole or any part of the model constitution prescribed under section 36 for the description to which the company belongs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the special resolution adopts the whole or any part of the model constitution prescribed under section 36 for the description to which the company belongs?
      `the special resolution adopts it by reference to the title of the model constitution or to the numbers of the particular regulations of the model constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the special resolution adopts it by reference to the title of the model constitution or to the numbers of the particular regulations of the model constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(1AB), does the special resolution need to set out the text of the model constitution adopted` IS
    `s 26(1AB) the special resolution needs to set out the text of the model constitution adopted` `the special resolution adopts the whole or any part of the model constitution prescribed under section 36 for the description to which the company belongs` `the special resolution adopts it by reference to the title of the model constitution or to the numbers of the particular regulations of the model constitution`

@export Under section 26(1A), is the power to alter the constitution subject to an entrenching provision?
GIVEN `the constitution includes, in accordance with section 26A, an entrenching provision that covers the provision to be altered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the constitution includes, in accordance with section 26A, an entrenching provision that covers the provision to be altered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(1A), is the power to alter the constitution subject to an entrenching provision` IS
    `s 26(1A) the power in subsection (1) is subject to an entrenching provision` `the constitution includes, in accordance with section 26A, an entrenching provision that covers the provision to be altered`

@export Under section 26(1B), may this provision of my company's constitution be altered?
GIVEN `the provision was contained in the constitution of the company immediately before 1 April 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provision contained in the constitution of the company immediately before 1 April 2004?
      `the provision could not be altered under the provisions of this Act in force immediately before 1 April 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the provision could not be altered under the provisions of this Act in force immediately before 1 April 2004?
      `all the members of the company agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all the members of the company agree?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(1B), may this provision of my company's constitution be altered` IS
    `s 26(1B) the provision may be altered` `the provision was contained in the constitution of the company immediately before 1 April 2004` `the provision could not be altered under the provisions of this Act in force immediately before 1 April 2004` `all the members of the company agree`

@export Under section 26(2), has my company complied with its duty to lodge a copy of the resolution, order or other document?
GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed or the order was made` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for this: the day the resolution was passed or the order was made?
      `the company has lodged the copy with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company lodged the copy with the Registrar?
      `the day the company lodged the copy` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for this: the day the company lodged the copy?
      `a copy of the constitution as adopted or altered was lodged with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a copy of the constitution as adopted or altered was lodged with it?
      `the Registrar dispenses with the copy of the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar dispenses with the copy of the constitution?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(2), has my company complied with its duty to lodge a copy of the resolution, order or other document` IS
    `s 26(2) the company has complied with the duty to lodge a copy of the resolution, order or other document` `the day the resolution was passed or the order was made` `the company has lodged the copy with the Registrar` `the day the company lodged the copy` `a copy of the constitution as adopted or altered was lodged with it` `the Registrar dispenses with the copy of the constitution` `the date asked`

@export Under section 26(2A), am I guilty of the offence of default in lodging a copy of the resolution, order or other document?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that default is made in complying with subsection (2)?
      `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the company, or an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(2A), am I guilty of the offence of default in lodging a copy of the resolution, order or other document` IS
    `s 26(2A) the person is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default`

@export Under section 26(2A), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction for default in lodging a copy of the resolution, order or other document?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that default is made in complying with subsection (2)?
      `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the company, or an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 26(2A), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction for default in lodging a copy of the resolution, order or other document` IS
    `s 26(2A) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default`

@export Under section 26(3), must the Registrar register the document my company has lodged?
GIVEN `the document is a resolution, order or other document lodged with the Registrar under this Act that affects the constitution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a resolution, order or other document lodged with the Registrar under this Act that affects the constitution of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(3), must the Registrar register the document my company has lodged` IS
    `s 26(3) the Registrar must register the document` `the document is a resolution, order or other document lodged with the Registrar under this Act that affects the constitution of the company`

@export Under section 26(3), must the Registrar issue my company a notice of the registration of the order?
GIVEN `the document registered is an order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document registered an order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(3), must the Registrar issue my company a notice of the registration of the order` IS
    `s 26(3) the Registrar must issue to the company a notice of the registration of the order` `the document registered is an order`

@export Under section 26(5), must the notice of the registration be published in the manner directed?
GIVEN `the Court or the Registrar has directed a manner of publication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court or the Registrar has directed a manner of publication?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(5), must the notice of the registration be published in the manner directed` IS
    `s 26(5) the notice of the registration must be published in the manner directed` `the Court or the Registrar has directed a manner of publication`

@export Under section 26(6), must the Registrar issue my company a notice of incorporation in accordance with the alteration?
GIVEN `it is appropriate to issue a notice of incorporation in accordance with the alteration made to the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is appropriate to issue a notice of incorporation in accordance with the alteration made to the constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(6), must the Registrar issue my company a notice of incorporation in accordance with the alteration` IS
    `s 26(6) the Registrar must issue a notice of incorporation in accordance with the alteration` `it is appropriate to issue a notice of incorporation in accordance with the alteration made to the constitution`

@export Under section 26(7), must the Registrar issue my company a certificate confirming its incorporation in accordance with the alteration?
GIVEN `the company has applied to the Registrar for a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company applied to the Registrar for a certificate?
      `the company has paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the company has paid the prescribed fee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(7), must the Registrar issue my company a certificate confirming its incorporation in accordance with the alteration` IS
    `s 26(7) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation in accordance with the alteration` `the company has applied to the Registrar for a certificate` `the company has paid the prescribed fee`

@export Under section 26A(4), is this provision an entrenching provision?
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of the constitution of a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision a provision of the constitution of a company?
      `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be altered in the manner provided by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be altered in the manner provided by this Act?
      `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be so altered except by a resolution passed by a specified majority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be so altered except by a resolution passed by a specified majority?
      `the specified majority, in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number for this: the specified majority, in percent?
      `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be so altered except where other specified conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be so altered except where other specified conditions are met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26A(4), is this provision an entrenching provision` IS
    `s 26A(4) the provision is an entrenching provision` `the provision is a provision of the constitution of a company` `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be altered in the manner provided by this Act` `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be so altered except by a resolution passed by a specified majority` `the specified majority, in percent` `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be so altered except where other specified conditions are met`

@export Under section 26A(1)(a), may this entrenching provision be included in the constitution with which my company is formed?
GIVEN `the entrenching provision is included in the constitution with which the company is formed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entrenching provision included in the constitution with which the company is formed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26A(1)(a), may this entrenching provision be included in the constitution with which my company is formed` IS
    `s 26A(1)(a) the entrenching provision may be included in the constitution with which the company is formed` `the entrenching provision is included in the constitution with which the company is formed`

@export Under section 26A(1)(b), may this entrenching provision be inserted in my company's constitution?
GIVEN `the entrenching provision is to be inserted in the constitution of the company after it is formed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entrenching provision to be inserted in the constitution of the company after it is formed?
      `all the members of the company agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all the members of the company agree?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26A(1)(b), may this entrenching provision be inserted in my company's constitution` IS
    `s 26A(1)(b) the entrenching provision may be inserted in the constitution` `the entrenching provision is to be inserted in the constitution of the company after it is formed` `all the members of the company agree`

@export Under section 26A(2), may this entrenching provision be removed or altered?
GIVEN `all the members of the company agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all the members of the company agree?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26A(2), may this entrenching provision be removed or altered` IS
    `s 26A(2) the entrenching provision may be removed or altered` `all the members of the company agree`

@export Under section 26A(3), are the provisions of the Act on altering the constitution subject to the entrenching provision?
GIVEN `the constitution contains an entrenching provision that covers the provision to be altered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the constitution contains an entrenching provision that covers the provision to be altered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26A(3), are the provisions of the Act on altering the constitution subject to the entrenching provision` IS
    `s 26A(3) the provisions of this Act on the alteration of the constitution are subject to the entrenching provision` `the constitution contains an entrenching provision that covers the provision to be altered`


§ `The company's name (s 27)`

@export Under section 27(1), must the Registrar refuse to register my company under this name?
GIVEN `the Minister has consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister consented?
      `subsection (1B) applies to the name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that subsection (1B) applies to the name?
      `in the Registrar's opinion the name is undesirable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that in the Registrar's opinion the name is undesirable?
      `in the Registrar's opinion the name is identical to the name of any other company, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or corporation or to any registered business name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that in the Registrar's opinion the name is identical to the name of any other company, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or corporation or to any registered business name?
      `in the Registrar's opinion the name is identical to a name reserved under subsection (12B) or under a provision paragraph (c) lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that in the Registrar's opinion the name is identical to a name reserved under subsection (12B) or under a provision paragraph (c) lists?
      `the name is a name of a kind that the Minister has directed the Registrar not to accept for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name a name of a kind that the Minister has directed the Registrar not to accept for registration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(1), must the Registrar refuse to register my company under this name` IS
    `s 27(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the company under the name` `the Minister has consented` `subsection (1B) applies to the name` `in the Registrar's opinion the name is undesirable` `in the Registrar's opinion the name is identical to the name of any other company, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or corporation or to any registered business name` `in the Registrar's opinion the name is identical to a name reserved under subsection (12B) or under a provision paragraph (c) lists` `the name is a name of a kind that the Minister has directed the Registrar not to accept for registration`

@export Under section 27(1A), how many years must pass after the earlier holder's dissolution, cancellation or cessation before my company may take its name?
GIVEN `the earlier holder of the name` IS A `s 27(1A) earlier holder of the name` @desc Which kind of body held the name before?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 27(1A), how many years must pass after the earlier holder's dissolution, cancellation or cessation before my company may take its name` IS
    `s 27(1A) the years that must pass after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `the earlier holder of the name`

@export Under section 27(1A), must the Registrar refuse to register my company under the name of a dissolved or cancelled body?
GIVEN `the earlier holder of the name` IS A `s 27(1A) earlier holder of the name` @desc Which kind of body held the name before?
      `the name is identical to the name of the earlier holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name identical to the name of the earlier holder?
      `the day of the dissolution, cancellation or cessation` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for this: the day of the dissolution, cancellation or cessation?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the Minister has consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister consented?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(1A), must the Registrar refuse to register my company under the name of a dissolved or cancelled body` IS
    `s 27(1A) the Registrar must refuse to register the company under the name` `the earlier holder of the name` `the name is identical to the name of the earlier holder` `the day of the dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `the date asked` `the Minister has consented`

@export Under section 27(1B), may the Registrar register my company under the name of a foreign company or limited partnership that has ceased?
GIVEN `the name is identical to the name of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name identical to the name of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11?
      `notice was lodged under section 377(1) that the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore or ceased to carry on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that notice was lodged under section 377(1) that the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore or ceased to carry on business in Singapore?
      `the day of the foreign company's cessation` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for this: the day of the foreign company's cessation?
      `the name of the foreign company was struck off the register under section 377(8), (9) or (10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the name of the foreign company struck off the register under section 377(8), (9) or (10)?
      `the day the name of the foreign company was so struck off` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for this: the day the name of the foreign company was so struck off?
      `the name is identical to the name of a limited partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name identical to the name of a limited partnership?
      `notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that the limited partnership ceased to carry on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that the limited partnership ceased to carry on business in Singapore?
      `the day of the limited partnership's cessation` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for this: the day of the limited partnership's cessation?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(1B), may the Registrar register my company under the name of a foreign company or limited partnership that has ceased` IS
    `s 27(1B) the Registrar may register the company under the name` `the name is identical to the name of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11` `notice was lodged under section 377(1) that the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore or ceased to carry on business in Singapore` `the day of the foreign company's cessation` `the name of the foreign company was struck off the register under section 377(8), (9) or (10)` `the day the name of the foreign company was so struck off` `the name is identical to the name of a limited partnership` `notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that the limited partnership ceased to carry on business in Singapore` `the day of the limited partnership's cessation` `the date asked`

@export Under section 27(2), may the Registrar direct my company to change its name?
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d)?
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1A) until the expiry of the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1A) until the expiry of the relevant period?
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is permitted to be registered under subsection (1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is permitted to be registered under subsection (1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period?
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that so nearly resembles the name of any other company, or any corporation, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or registered business name, as to be likely to be mistaken for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that so nearly resembles the name of any other company, or any corporation, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or registered business name, as to be likely to be mistaken for it?
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name the use of which has been restrained by an injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that the company has been registered by a name the use of which has been restrained by an injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(2), may the Registrar direct my company to change its name` IS
    `s 27(2) the Registrar may direct the company to change its name` `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d)` `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1A) until the expiry of the relevant period` `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is permitted to be registered under subsection (1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period` `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that so nearly resembles the name of any other company, or any corporation, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or registered business name, as to be likely to be mistaken for it` `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name the use of which has been restrained by an injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998`

@export Under section 27(2), has my company complied with the Registrar's direction to change its name?
GIVEN `the day of the direction` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for this: the day of the direction?
      `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar allowed a longer period?
      `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for this: the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed?
