-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026) -- THE SEAT LAYER of part agent sgj.
-- Part 4 Divisions 4 to 7A, and Part 5 Division 1 (ss 79 to 91, 93 to 100, 121 to 130AE, 142 to 144; the repealed sections are not asked about).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company incorporated under the Act, or who deals with one.
-- The Registrar, the Minister and the Court have no seat here: what they decide appears only as what it means for that individual
-- (for example "Under section 87, can the Registrar extend the time for my notice").
-- Nothing here is new law: every question calls a layer-1 rule from the modules imported above and states no rule of its own.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, and the two choices the part 5 module declares for what an item is and what a person did),
-- each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records and lists the layer-1 rules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE or in its call.
--   * The public holidays the business-day rules need are a list in layer 1. A question that needs them asks for the first two public holidays in Singapore after the event date,
--     and the event date itself stands for "none": a business day is counted from the day after the event, so the event date is never a counted day.
--     A third public holiday inside the counting window cannot be given, so the answer can then be earlier than the true last day.
--   * The 14 facts of section 7 are asked one by one; the chain through bodies corporate in section 7(4) and (4A) is not a plain input and is passed empty,
--     so an interest held only through a body corporate is not seen by section 81(1).
--   * A person is never "the company": where a layer-1 offence asks whether the person is the company or an officer in default, the question fixes "the company" at FALSE.
--   * A MAYBE result is read as in the rest of this part: JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is the text's own no; NOTHING is not covered (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   * A rule that can give only a yes or a no has no not-covered case in sgj-cases-seat.l4, and a rule that can give no no has no no-case.
--

§ `Part 4, Division 4: substantial shareholdings (ss 79 to 91)`

-- s 79(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 79(2) the body is a company for the purposes of this Division`
@export Under section 79(2), is the body a company for the purposes of Division 4 of Part 4?
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the body is a body corporate incorporated in Singapore?
      `the body is a body that is not a body corporate formed in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the body is a body that is not a body corporate formed in Singapore?
      `the Minister has declared the body, by notification in the Gazette, to be a company for the purposes of Division 4 of Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Minister has declared the body, by notification in the Gazette, to be a company for the purposes of Division 4 of Part 4?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(2), is the body a company for the purposes of Division 4 of Part 4` IS
    `s 79(2) the body is a company for the purposes of this Division` `the body is a body corporate incorporated in Singapore` `the body is a body that is not a body corporate formed in Singapore` `the Minister has declared the body, by notification in the Gazette, to be a company for the purposes of Division 4 of Part 4`

-- s 81(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 81(1) the person has a substantial shareholding in the company`  (`s 81(1)(a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares 
-- The chain through bodies corporate in section 7(4) is not a plain input: the question passes the empty chain, so an interest held only through a body corporate is not seen here.
@export Under section 81(1), do I have a substantial shareholding in the company?
GIVEN `the body is a company for the purposes of Division 4 of Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the body is a company for the purposes of Division 4 of Part 4?
      `the shares are voting shares as section 4(1) defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the shares are voting shares as section 4(1) defines the term?
      `the shares are treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the shares are treasury shares?
      `I have authority, formal or informal, express or implied, to dispose of the shares or to control their disposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have authority, formal or informal, express or implied, to dispose of the shares or to control their disposal?
      `property held in trust includes the shares and I have an interest under the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that property held in trust includes the shares and you have an interest under the trust?
      `I know, or have reasonable grounds for believing, that I have that interest under the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you know, or have reasonable grounds for believing, that you have that interest under the trust?
      `I have entered into a contract to purchase a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have entered into a contract to purchase a share?
      `I have a right, apart from any interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to me or to my order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have a right, apart from any interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to you or to your order?
      `I have the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option?
      `I am entitled, other than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share that is not registered in my name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are entitled, other than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share that is not registered in your name?
      `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager?
      `I hold the share as bare trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you hold the share as bare trustee?
      `my ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your ordinary business includes the lending of money?
      `I hold the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you hold the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money?
      `I hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office?
      `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired under sections 76B to 76G, including treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired under sections 76B to 76G, including treasury shares?
      `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons?
      `the total votes attached to the shares in which I have an interest` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total votes attached to the shares in which you have an interest?
      `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 81(1), do I have a substantial shareholding in the company` IS
    `s 81(1) the person has a substantial shareholding in the company` `the body is a company for the purposes of Division 4 of Part 4` (`s 81(1)(a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares in the company` `the shares are voting shares as section 4(1) defines the term` `the shares are treasury shares` facts) (`s 81(1)(b) the votes are not less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company` `the total votes attached to the shares in which I have an interest` `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company`)
    WHERE
        facts MEANS `s 7 interest facts` OF `I have authority, formal or informal, express or implied, to dispose of the shares or to control their disposal`, `property held in trust includes the shares and I have an interest under the trust`, `I know, or have reasonable grounds for believing, that I have that interest under the trust`, `I have entered into a contract to purchase a share`, `I have a right, apart from any interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to me or to my order`, `I have the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option`, `I am entitled, other than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share that is not registered in my name`, `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager`, `I hold the share as bare trustee`, `my ordinary business includes the lending of money`, `I hold the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money`, `I hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office`, `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired under sections 76B to 76G, including treasury shares`, `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons`, EMPTY

-- s 81(3). Layer 1 rule called: `s 81(3) the person is a substantial shareholder in the company` (JUST ) (JUST )
@export Under section 81(3), am I a substantial shareholder in the company?
GIVEN `I have a substantial shareholding in the company under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have a substantial shareholding in the company under subsection (1)?
      `I have a substantial shareholding in the company under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have a substantial shareholding in the company under subsection (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 81(3), am I a substantial shareholder in the company` IS
    `s 81(3) the person is a substantial shareholder in the company` (JUST `I have a substantial shareholding in the company under subsection (1)`) (JUST `I have a substantial shareholding in the company under subsection (2)`)

-- s 82(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 82(1) the notice is the notice the subsection requires`
@export Under section 82(1), is my notice the notice the section requires?
GIVEN `I am a substantial shareholder in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a substantial shareholder in the company?
      `my notice is in writing and is given to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your notice is in writing and is given to the company?
      `my notice states my name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your notice states your name and address?
      `my notice states full particulars of the voting shares in the company in which I have an interest or interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your notice states full particulars of the voting shares in the company in which you have an interest or interests?
      `the interest or interests cannot be related to a particular share or shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the interest or interests cannot be related to a particular share or shares?
      `my notice states the name of the person who is registered as the holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your notice states the name of the person who is registered as the holder?
      `my notice states full particulars of each such interest and of the circumstances by reason of which I have that interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your notice states full particulars of each such interest and of the circumstances by reason of which you have that interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 82(1), is my notice the notice the section requires` IS
    `s 82(1) the notice is the notice the subsection requires` `I am a substantial shareholder in the company` `my notice is in writing and is given to the company` `my notice states my name and address` `my notice states full particulars of the voting shares in the company in which I have an interest or interests` `the interest or interests cannot be related to a particular share or shares` `my notice states the name of the person who is registered as the holder` `my notice states full particulars of each such interest and of the circumstances by reason of which I have that interest`

-- s 82(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 82(2) the last day for giving the notice`   (LIST , )
@export Under section 82(2), what is the last day for me to give notice that I am a substantial shareholder?
GIVEN `I was a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you were a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971?
      `the date on which I became a substantial shareholder` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you became a substantial shareholder?
      `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
      `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 82(2), what is the last day for me to give notice that I am a substantial shareholder` IS
    `s 82(2) the last day for giving the notice` `I was a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971` `the date on which I became a substantial shareholder` (LIST `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date`, `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date`)

-- s 82(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 82(2) the notice was given within the time the subsection allows`   (LIST , )
@export Under section 82(2), did I give my notice within the time the section allows?
GIVEN `I was a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you were a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971?
      `the date on which I became a substantial shareholder` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you became a substantial shareholder?
      `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
      `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
      `the date on which I gave my notice` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you gave your notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 82(2), did I give my notice within the time the section allows` IS
    `s 82(2) the notice was given within the time the subsection allows` `I was a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971` `the date on which I became a substantial shareholder` (LIST `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date`, `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date`) `the date on which I gave my notice`

-- s 83(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 83(1) the substantial shareholder must give notice of a change in the percentage level`
@export Under section 83(1), must I give notice of a change in my percentage level?
GIVEN `I am a substantial shareholder in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a substantial shareholder in the company?
      `my percentage level immediately before the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your percentage level immediately before the relevant time?
      `my percentage level immediately after the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your percentage level immediately after the relevant time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83(1), must I give notice of a change in my percentage level` IS
    `s 83(1) the substantial shareholder must give notice of a change in the percentage level` `I am a substantial shareholder in the company` `my percentage level immediately before the relevant time` `my percentage level immediately after the relevant time`

-- s 83(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 83(1) the last day for giving the notice`  (LIST , )
@export Under section 83(1), what is the last day for me to give notice of a change in my percentage level?
GIVEN `the date on which I became aware of the change in my percentage level` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you became aware of the change in your percentage level?
      `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
      `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 83(1), what is the last day for me to give notice of a change in my percentage level` IS
    `s 83(1) the last day for giving the notice` `the date on which I became aware of the change in my percentage level` (LIST `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date`, `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date`)

-- s 83(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 83(1) the notice was given within 2 business days after the substantial shareholder became aware`  (LIST , )
@export Under section 83(1), did I give notice of a change within 2 business days after I became aware of it?
GIVEN `the date on which I became aware of the change in my percentage level` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you became aware of the change in your percentage level?
      `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
      `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
      `the date on which I gave my notice` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you gave your notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83(1), did I give notice of a change within 2 business days after I became aware of it` IS
    `s 83(1) the notice was given within 2 business days after the substantial shareholder became aware` `the date on which I became aware of the change in my percentage level` (LIST `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date`, `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date`) `the date on which I gave my notice`

-- s 84(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 84(2) the last day for giving the notice`  (LIST , )
@export Under section 84(2), what is the last day for me to give notice that I have ceased to be a substantial shareholder?
GIVEN `the date on which I ceased to be a substantial shareholder` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you ceased to be a substantial shareholder?
      `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
      `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 84(2), what is the last day for me to give notice that I have ceased to be a substantial shareholder` IS
    `s 84(2) the last day for giving the notice` `the date on which I ceased to be a substantial shareholder` (LIST `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date`, `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date`)

-- s 84(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 84(2) the notice was given within 2 business days after the person ceased to be a substantial shareholder`  (LIST , )
@export Under section 84(2), did I give notice that I ceased to be a substantial shareholder within 2 business days?
GIVEN `the date on which I ceased to be a substantial shareholder` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you ceased to be a substantial shareholder?
      `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
      `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in Singapore that falls after that date? Give that date again if there is none.
      `the date on which I gave my notice` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you gave your notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(2), did I give notice that I ceased to be a substantial shareholder within 2 business days` IS
    `s 84(2) the notice was given within 2 business days after the person ceased to be a substantial shareholder` `the date on which I ceased to be a substantial shareholder` (LIST `the first public holiday in Singapore after that date`, `the second public holiday in Singapore after that date`) `the date on which I gave my notice`

-- s 86(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 86(1) the holder must give the non-resident a notice`   applies
@export Under section 86(1), must I give a non-resident who has an interest in voting shares that I hold a notice?
GIVEN `I hold voting shares in a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you hold voting shares in a company?
      `a non-resident has an interest in those voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a non-resident has an interest in those voting shares?
      `I am the Depository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are the Depository?
      `I hold the shares as the registered holder of the company's shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you hold the shares as the registered holder of the company's shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 86(1), must I give a non-resident who has an interest in voting shares that I hold a notice` IS
    `s 86(1) the holder must give the non-resident a notice` `I hold voting shares in a company` `a non-resident has an interest in those voting shares` applies
    WHERE
        applies MEANS `s 86(2A) section 86 applies to the person` `I am the Depository` `I hold the shares as the registered holder of the company's shares`

-- s 86(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 86(2) the last day for giving the notice`
@export Under section 86(2), what is the last day for me to give the non-resident the notice?
GIVEN `I held the shares on 1 October 1971` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you held the shares on 1 October 1971?
      `the date on which I became the holder of the shares` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you became the holder of the shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 86(2), what is the last day for me to give the non-resident the notice` IS
    `s 86(2) the last day for giving the notice` `I held the shares on 1 October 1971` `the date on which I became the holder of the shares`

-- s 87. Layer 1 rule called: `s 87 the Registrar has power to extend the time for giving the notice`
@export Under section 87, can the Registrar extend the time for my notice?
GIVEN `I am required to give a notice under Division 4 of Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are required to give a notice under Division 4 of Part 4?
      `I have applied to the Registrar for an extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have applied to the Registrar for an extension?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87, can the Registrar extend the time for my notice` IS
    `s 87 the Registrar has power to extend the time for giving the notice` `I am required to give a notice under Division 4 of Part 4` `I have applied to the Registrar for an extension`

-- s 88(3). Layer 1 rule called: `s 88(3) the last day for the company to send the copy`
@export Under section 88(3), what is the last day for the company to send me the copy of the register?
GIVEN `the date on which the company received my request for a copy` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the company received your request for a copy?
      `the number of days the Registrar has thought fit to allow, or 0 if the Registrar has fixed none` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of days the Registrar has thought fit to allow, or 0 if the Registrar has fixed none?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 88(3), what is the last day for the company to send me the copy of the register` IS
    `s 88(3) the last day for the company to send the copy` `the date on which the company received my request for a copy` `the number of days the Registrar has thought fit to allow, or 0 if the Registrar has fixed none`

-- s 88(5). Layer 1 rule called: `s 88(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`  FALSE
-- The person is the company: fixed at FALSE, because the seat is an individual.
@export Under section 88(5), am I guilty, as an officer in default, of the offence of the company's default under section 88?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 88` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that default is made in complying with section 88?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88(5), am I guilty, as an officer in default, of the offence of the company's default under section 88` IS
    `s 88(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 88` FALSE `I am an officer of the company who is in default`

-- s 88(5). Layer 1 rule called: `s 88(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction`  FALSE
@export Under section 88(5), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction as an officer in default?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 88` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that default is made in complying with section 88?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 88(5), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction as an officer in default` IS
    `s 88(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `default is made in complying with section 88` FALSE `I am an officer of the company who is in default`

-- s 89. Layer 1 rule called: `s 89 the person is guilty of the offence this section creates`
@export Under section 89, am I guilty of an offence for failing to give a notice that section 82, 83, 84 or 86 requires?
GIVEN `I fail to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you fail to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 89, am I guilty of an offence for failing to give a notice that section 82, 83, 84 or 86 requires` IS
    `s 89 the person is guilty of the offence this section creates` `I fail to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86`

-- s 89. Layer 1 rule called: `s 89 the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction`
@export Under section 89, what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction for failing to give a notice?
GIVEN `I fail to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you fail to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 89, what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction for failing to give a notice` IS
    `s 89 the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `I fail to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86`

-- s 90(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 90(1) this section gives a defence on these facts`   presumed
@export Under section 90(1), does section 90 give me a defence on these facts?
GIVEN `I am prosecuted for failing to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are prosecuted for failing to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86?
      `I prove that the failure was due to my not being aware of a fact or occurrence the existence of which was necessary to constitute the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you prove that the failure was due to your not being aware of a fact or occurrence the existence of which was necessary to constitute the offence?
      `I would, had I acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of my affairs, have been aware of it at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you would, had you acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of your affairs, have been aware of it at that time?
      `an employee or agent of mine, having duties or acting in relation to my interests in shares in the company, was aware of it at that time or would, had the employee or agent acted with reasonable diligence, have been aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an employee or agent of mine, having duties or acting in relation to your interests in shares in the company, was aware of it at that time or would, had the employee or agent acted with reasonable diligence, have been aware of it?
      `I was not so aware on the date of the summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you were not so aware on the date of the summons?
      `the date on which I became so aware` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you became so aware?
      `the date of the summons` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 90(1), does section 90 give me a defence on these facts` IS
    `s 90(1) this section gives a defence on these facts` `I am prosecuted for failing to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86` `I prove that the failure was due to my not being aware of a fact or occurrence the existence of which was necessary to constitute the offence` presumed `I was not so aware on the date of the summons` `the date on which I became so aware` `the date of the summons`
    WHERE
        presumed MEANS `s 90(2) the person is conclusively presumed to have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time` `I would, had I acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of my affairs, have been aware of it at that time` `an employee or agent of mine, having duties or acting in relation to my interests in shares in the company, was aware of it at that time or would, had the employee or agent acted with reasonable diligence, have been aware of it`

-- s 91(10). Layer 1 rule called: `s 91(10) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`
@export Under section 91(10), am I guilty of an offence if I contravene or fail to comply with a court order made under section 91?
GIVEN `I contravene or fail to comply with an order made under section 91 that is applicable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you contravene or fail to comply with an order made under section 91 that is applicable to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 91(10), am I guilty of an offence if I contravene or fail to comply with a court order made under section 91` IS
    `s 91(10) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `I contravene or fail to comply with an order made under section 91 that is applicable to me`

§ `Part 4, Division 5: debentures (ss 93 to 100)`

-- s 93(3). Layer 1 rule called: `s 93(3) the register must be open to the inspection of the person`
@export Under section 93(3), must the company's register of debenture holders be open to my inspection?
