      `I am a holder of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a holder of shares in the company?
      `the register is duly closed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the register is duly closed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 93(3), must the company's register of debenture holders be open to my inspection` IS
    `s 93(3) the register must be open to the inspection of the person` `I am a registered holder of debentures of the company` `I am a holder of shares in the company` `the register is duly closed`

-- s 93(5). Layer 1 rule called: `s 93(5) the company must supply the person with a copy of the register`
@export Under section 93(5), must the company supply me with a copy of the register of debenture holders?
GIVEN `I am a registered holder of debentures of the company or a holder of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a registered holder of debentures of the company or a holder of shares in the company?
      `I have requested a copy of the register or part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have requested a copy of the register or part of it?
      `I have paid $1 for every page or part of a page required to be copied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have paid $1 for every page or part of a page required to be copied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 93(5), must the company supply me with a copy of the register of debenture holders` IS
    `s 93(5) the company must supply the person with a copy of the register` `I am a registered holder of debentures of the company or a holder of shares in the company` `I have requested a copy of the register or part of it` `I have paid $1 for every page or part of a page required to be copied`

-- s 93(6). Layer 1 rule called: `s 93(6) the company must forward the copy of the trust deed to the holder`
@export Under section 93(6), must the company forward me a copy of the trust deed?
GIVEN `I am a holder of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a holder of the debentures?
      `I have requested a copy of the trust deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have requested a copy of the trust deed?
      `I have paid the sum the subsection allows the company to require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have paid the sum the subsection allows the company to require?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 93(6), must the company forward me a copy of the trust deed` IS
    `s 93(6) the company must forward the copy of the trust deed to the holder` `I am a holder of the debentures` `I have requested a copy of the trust deed` `I have paid the sum the subsection allows the company to require`

-- s 93(7). Layer 1 rule called: `s 93(7) the copy was forwarded within the time the subsection allows`
@export Under section 93(7), was the copy forwarded to me within the time the subsection allows?
GIVEN `the date on which I made my request` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you made your request?
      `the date on which the copy was forwarded to me` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the copy was forwarded to you?
      `the copy was forwarded within a reasonable time after my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the copy was forwarded within a reasonable time after your request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 93(7), was the copy forwarded to me within the time the subsection allows` IS
    `s 93(7) the copy was forwarded within the time the subsection allows` `the date on which I made my request` `the date on which the copy was forwarded to me` `the copy was forwarded within a reasonable time after my request`

-- s 93(9). Layer 1 rule called: `s 93(9) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`  FALSE
-- The person is the company: fixed at FALSE, because the seat is an individual.
@export Under section 93(9), am I guilty, as an officer in default, of the offence of the company's failure to comply with section 93?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 93` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company fails to comply with section 93?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 93(9), am I guilty, as an officer in default, of the offence of the company's failure to comply with section 93` IS
    `s 93(9) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the company fails to comply with section 93` FALSE `I am an officer of the company who is in default`

-- s 96(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 96(1) the company has power to reissue the redeemed debentures`
@export Under section 96(1), does the company have power to reissue debentures it has redeemed?
GIVEN `the company has redeemed debentures, whether before or after 29 December 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company has redeemed debentures, whether before or after 29 December 1967?
      `a provision to the contrary, express or implied, is contained in the constitution or in a contract entered into by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a provision to the contrary, express or implied, is contained in the constitution or in a contract entered into by the company?
      `the company has, by passing a resolution to that effect or by some other act, manifested its intention that the debentures are to be cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company has, by passing a resolution to that effect or by some other act, manifested its intention that the debentures are to be cancelled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 96(1), does the company have power to reissue debentures it has redeemed` IS
    `s 96(1) the company has power to reissue the redeemed debentures` `the company has redeemed debentures, whether before or after 29 December 1967` `a provision to the contrary, express or implied, is contained in the constitution or in a contract entered into by the company` `the company has, by passing a resolution to that effect or by some other act, manifested its intention that the debentures are to be cancelled`

-- s 100(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 100(1) the Court may order that the security be enforceable`
@export Under section 100(1), may the Court order that my security be enforceable?
GIVEN `the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on the happening of a contingency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on the happening of a contingency?
      `the application is made by the trustee for the holders of the debentures or, where there is no trustee, by the holder of any of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is made by the trustee for the holders of the debentures or, where there is no trustee, by the holder of any of the debentures?
      `at the time of the issue the assets which constituted or were intended to constitute the security were sufficient or likely to become sufficient to discharge the principal debt and any interest on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that at the time of the issue the assets which constituted or were intended to constitute the security were sufficient or likely to become sufficient to discharge the principal debt and any interest on it?
      `the sum the security, if realised in the present circumstances, would be likely to bring, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum the security, if realised in the present circumstances, would be likely to bring, in dollars?
      `the principal sum of moneys outstanding, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the principal sum of moneys outstanding, in dollars?
      `the assets covered by the security, fairly valued as a going concern, are worth less than the principal sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the assets covered by the security, fairly valued as a going concern, are worth less than the principal sum?
      `the borrowing corporation is not making sufficient profit to pay the interest due on the principal sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the borrowing corporation is not making sufficient profit to pay the interest due on the principal sum?
      `the debenture is offered to the public for subscription or purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the debenture is offered to the public for subscription or purchase?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 100(1), may the Court order that my security be enforceable` IS
    `s 100(1) the Court may order that the security be enforceable` `the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on the happening of a contingency` `the application is made by the trustee for the holders of the debentures or, where there is no trustee, by the holder of any of the debentures` `at the time of the issue the assets which constituted or were intended to constitute the security were sufficient or likely to become sufficient to discharge the principal debt and any interest on it` `the sum the security, if realised in the present circumstances, would be likely to bring, in dollars` `the principal sum of moneys outstanding, in dollars` `the assets covered by the security, fairly valued as a going concern, are worth less than the principal sum` `the borrowing corporation is not making sufficient profit to pay the interest due on the principal sum` `the debenture is offered to the public for subscription or purchase`

§ `Part 4, Division 7: title and transfers (ss 121 to 130AE)`

-- s 121. Layer 1 rule called: `s 121 the share or other interest of a member is movable property`
