      `the certificate is under the common seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate is under the common seal of the company?
      `the certificate is under the official seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate is under the official seal of the company?
      `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the name of the company and the authority under which the company is constituted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the name of the company and the authority under which the company is constituted?
      `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the address of the registered office of the company in Singapore or, where it is issued by a branch office, the address of that branch office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the address of the registered office of the company in Singapore or, where it is issued by a branch office, the address of that branch office?
      `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the class of the shares, whether they are fully or partly paid up and the amount, if any, unpaid on them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the class of the shares, whether they are fully or partly paid up and the amount, if any, unpaid on them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 123(2), is my share certificate as the subsection requires` IS
    `s 123(2) the share certificate is as the subsection requires` `the certificate relates to shares on a branch register` `the certificate is under the common seal of the company` `the certificate is under the official seal of the company` `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the name of the company and the authority under which the company is constituted` `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the address of the registered office of the company in Singapore or, where it is issued by a branch office, the address of that branch office` `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the class of the shares, whether they are fully or partly paid up and the amount, if any, unpaid on them`

-- s 123(4). Layer 1 rule called: `s 123(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`  FALSE
