-- s 129(3). Layer 1 rule called: `s 129(3) the private company is barred from refusing by virtue of a discretion in the constitution`
@export Under section 129(3), is the private company barred from refusing to lodge the notice of transfer by virtue of a discretion in its constitution?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the application relates to a share that has been transferred or transmitted to a person by act of parties or operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application relates to a share that has been transferred or transmitted to a person by act of parties or operation of law?
      `the date on which the application was made` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the application was made?
      `the date on which the written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal was served on the applicant` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal was served on the applicant?
      `a written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that discretion has been served on the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that discretion has been served on the applicant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 129(3), is the private company barred from refusing to lodge the notice of transfer by virtue of a discretion in its constitution` IS
    `s 129(3) the private company is barred from refusing by virtue of a discretion in the constitution` `the company is a private company` `the application relates to a share that has been transferred or transmitted to a person by act of parties or operation of law` `the date on which the application was made` `the date on which the written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal was served on the applicant` `a written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that discretion has been served on the applicant`

-- s 129(4). Layer 1 rule called: `s 129(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`  FALSE
-- The person is the company: fixed at FALSE, because the seat is an individual.
@export Under section 129(4), am I guilty, as an officer in default, of the offence of the company's default under section 129?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 129` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that default is made in complying with section 129?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are an officer of the company who is in default?
