      `the date on which the notice of the refusal was sent` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the notice of the refusal was sent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 130AB(1), did the public company send notice of its refusal within 30 days after the transfer was lodged` IS
    `s 130AB(1) the notice of the refusal was sent within 30 days` `the date on which the transfer was lodged with the company` `the date on which the notice of the refusal was sent`

-- s 130AB(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 130AB(2) the public company is barred from refusing registration by virtue of a discretion in the constitution`
@export Under section 130AB(2), is the public company barred from refusing registration by virtue of a discretion in its constitution?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the application is for a person to be registered as a member in respect of shares that have been transferred or transmitted to the person by act of parties or operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is for a person to be registered as a member in respect of shares that have been transferred or transmitted to the person by act of parties or operation of law?
      `the date on which the application was made` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the application was made?
      `the date on which the written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal was served on the applicant` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal was served on the applicant?
      `a written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that discretion has been served on the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that discretion has been served on the applicant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 130AB(2), is the public company barred from refusing registration by virtue of a discretion in its constitution` IS
    `s 130AB(2) the public company is barred from refusing registration by virtue of a discretion in the constitution` `the company is a public company` `the application is for a person to be registered as a member in respect of shares that have been transferred or transmitted to the person by act of parties or operation of law` `the date on which the application was made` `the date on which the written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal was served on the applicant` `a written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that discretion has been served on the applicant`

-- s 130AC(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 130AC(2) the company must accept the document as sufficient evidence of the grant`
@export Under section 130AC(2), must the company accept my document as sufficient evidence of the grant of probate or letters of administration?
GIVEN `my document has been produced to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your document has been produced to the company?
      `my document is by law sufficient evidence of probate of the will, or letters of administration of the estate, of a deceased person having been granted to some person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your document is by law sufficient evidence of probate of the will, or letters of administration of the estate, of a deceased person having been granted to some person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 130AC(2), must the company accept my document as sufficient evidence of the grant of probate or letters of administration` IS
    `s 130AC(2) the company must accept the document as sufficient evidence of the grant` `my document has been produced to the company` `my document is by law sufficient evidence of probate of the will, or letters of administration of the estate, of a deceased person having been granted to some person`

-- s 130AD(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 130AD(2) the company is under the same liability to the person as if the certification had been made fraudulently`
@export Under section 130AD(2), is the company under the same liability to me as if its certification had been made fraudulently?
GIVEN `I acted on the faith of a false certification by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you acted on the faith of a false certification by the company?
      `the certification was made negligently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certification was made negligently?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 130AD(2), is the company under the same liability to me as if its certification had been made fraudulently` IS
    `s 130AD(2) the company is under the same liability to the person as if the certification had been made fraudulently` `I acted on the faith of a false certification by the company` `the certification was made negligently`

-- s 130AD(4). Layer 1 rule called: `s 130AD(4) the company and its officers are liable in respect of the registration of the transfer of shares, debentures or other interests`
@export Under section 130AD(4), are the public company and its officers liable in respect of the registration of the transfer of shares, debentures or other interests?
GIVEN `the certification was made by a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certification was made by a public company?
      `the number of days to which the certification is limited` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of days to which the certification is limited?
      `the date of the certification` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the certification?
      `the number of days by which the company has extended the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of days by which the company has extended the period?
      `the date of the registration of the transfer` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the registration of the transfer?
      `the instrument of transfer has within that period been lodged with the company for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the instrument of transfer has within that period been lodged with the company for registration?
      `there has been fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there has been fraud?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 130AD(4), are the public company and its officers liable in respect of the registration of the transfer of shares, debentures or other interests` IS
    `s 130AD(4) the company and its officers are liable in respect of the registration of the transfer of shares, debentures or other interests` `the certification was made by a public company` `the number of days to which the certification is limited` `the date of the certification` `the number of days by which the company has extended the period` `the date of the registration of the transfer` `the instrument of transfer has within that period been lodged with the company for registration` `there has been fraud`

-- s 130AE(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 130AE(1) the public company completed the certificates in time after the transfer`
@export Under section 130AE(1), did the public company complete the certificates in time after my transfer was lodged?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the date on which the transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the transfer was lodged with the company?
      `the date on which the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 130AE(1), did the public company complete the certificates in time after my transfer was lodged` IS
    `s 130AE(1) the public company completed the certificates in time after the transfer` `the company is a public company` `the date on which the transfer was lodged with the company` `the date on which the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery`

-- s 130AE(3). Layer 1 rule called: `s 130AE(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`  FALSE
-- The person is the company: fixed at FALSE, because the seat is an individual.
@export Under section 130AE(3), am I guilty, as an officer in default, of the offence of the company's default under section 130AE?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 130AE` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that default is made in complying with section 130AE?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 130AE(3), am I guilty, as an officer in default, of the offence of the company's default under section 130AE` IS
    `s 130AE(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 130AE` FALSE `I am an officer of the company who is in default`

-- s 130AE(4). Layer 1 rule called: `s 130AE(4) the Court may make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default`  failed
@export Under section 130AE(4), may the Court, on my application, order the company to make good its default in issuing my certificates?
GIVEN `a notice requiring the company to make good a default in complying with section 130AE has been served on the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice requiring the company to make good a default in complying with section 130AE has been served on the company?
      `the date on which the notice was served on the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the notice was served on the company?
      `the company has made good the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company has made good the default?
      `the date on which the company made good the default, if it has` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the company made good the default, if it has?
      `the date of my application to the Court` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of your application to the Court?
      `I am the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 130AE(4), may the Court, on my application, order the company to make good its default in issuing my certificates` IS
    `s 130AE(4) the Court may make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default` `a notice requiring the company to make good a default in complying with section 130AE has been served on the company` failed `I am the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to me`
    WHERE
        failed MEANS `s 130AE(4) the company failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` `the date on which the notice was served on the company` `the company has made good the default` `the date on which the company made good the default, if it has` `the date of my application to the Court`

§ `Part 5, Division 1: registered office and name (ss 142 to 144)`

-- s 142(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 142(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`  FALSE
-- The person is the company: fixed at FALSE, because the seat is an individual.
@export Under section 142(2), am I guilty, as an officer in default, of the offence of the company's default under section 142(1)?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1) of section 142` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that default is made in complying with subsection (1) of section 142?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 142(2), am I guilty, as an officer in default, of the offence of the company's default under section 142(1)` IS
    `s 142(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with subsection (1) of section 142` FALSE `I am an officer of the company who is in default`

-- s 143(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 143(1) the notice of the change was lodged within 14 days after the change`
@export Under section 143(1), did the company lodge notice of the change of its registered office's particulars within 14 days?
GIVEN `the date on which the particulars changed` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the particulars changed?
      `the date on which the notice of the change was lodged` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the notice of the change was lodged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 143(1), did the company lodge notice of the change of its registered office's particulars within 14 days` IS
    `s 143(1) the notice of the change was lodged within 14 days after the change` `the date on which the particulars changed` `the date on which the notice of the change was lodged`

-- s 144(1). Layer 1 rule called: `s 144(1) the name of the company must appear on the item`
@export Under section 144(1), must the company's name appear on this item?
GIVEN `the item` IS A `s 144 item` @desc Which of these is the item: the company's seal, a business letter, a statement of account, an invoice, an official notice, a publication, a bill of exchange, a promissory note, an indorsement, a cheque, an order, a receipt, a letter of credit, another negotiable instrument, or some other thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 144(1), must the company's name appear on this item` IS
    `s 144(1) the name of the company must appear on the item` `the item`

-- s 144(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 144(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`
@export Under section 144(2), am I guilty of an offence for what I did on the company's behalf?
GIVEN `I am an officer of the company or a person acting on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are an officer of the company or a person acting on its behalf?
      `what I did` IS A `s 144(2) what the person did` @desc Which of these did you do: use or authorise the use of a seal without the company's name in legible romanised letters, issue or authorise the issue of a business letter, statement of account, invoice, official notice or publication without the name, sign or issue or authorise a negotiable instrument, indorsement, order, receipt or letter of credit without the name, or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 144(2), am I guilty of an offence for what I did on the company's behalf` IS
    `s 144(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `I am an officer of the company or a person acting on its behalf` `what I did`

-- s 144(2). Layer 1 rule called: `s 144(2) the person is liable to the holder of the instrument for the amount due on it`
@export Under section 144(2), am I liable to the holder of the instrument for the amount due on it?
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `s 144(2) the instrument` @desc Which kind of instrument is it: a bill of exchange, a promissory note, another negotiable instrument, an indorsement, an order, a cheque, a receipt or a letter of credit?
      `I signed, issued or authorised to be signed or issued the instrument on behalf of the company, and the company's name is not mentioned in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you signed, issued or authorised to be signed or issued the instrument on behalf of the company, and the company's name is not mentioned in it?
      `the amount due on the instrument has been paid by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amount due on the instrument has been paid by the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 144(2), am I liable to the holder of the instrument for the amount due on it` IS
    `s 144(2) the person is liable to the holder of the instrument for the amount due on it` `the instrument` `I signed, issued or authorised to be signed or issued the instrument on behalf of the company, and the company's name is not mentioned in it` `the amount due on the instrument has been paid by the company`


-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sgk (wave 2; merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026) -- THE SEAT LAYER, ranges sgk.
-- This is a rendering of the Act and not the official text; nothing here is endorsed by, or associated with, the Singapore Government or the Attorney-General's Chambers.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, the company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company incorporated under the Act,
-- or of a foreign company registered under it, or who deals with one: asking, on facts they can state, what Part 4 Division 8 (the registration of charges)
-- and Part 9 (investigations) require of them or let them do, what they can claim, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done.
-- There is never a seat for the Registrar, the Minister, the Authority or the Court: a power of theirs appears only as what it means to the individual.
-- Parts 8 and 8A of the text hold no provision in this edition (sections 217 to 227X are shown repealed), so they have no question.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, numbers, dates and the layer-1 modules' own choices), one per fact the individual can state,
-- each with an @desc worded as the individual would be asked. The records the layer-1 modules expect (the facts about a charge, a Maybe date) are built
-- inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the layer-1 function is then called; no rule is restated here.
-- A question that asks "am I guilty of" an offence passes FALSE for the fact `the person is the company`: the individual is never the company.
-- Where the offence function has a penalty (Penalty record), a second and third question project its highest fine and its longest imprisonment.
--
-- READING AN ANSWER: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text's own no, NOTHING is "the text does not say" (NOTES.md, Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING).
-- Every question name begins "Under section N," and asks, in the same direction, what its body answers (NOTES.md lists the direction check).
-- Questions are grouped under § headings in the text's order.


§ `Part 4 Division 8: the registration of charges`

§§ `Section 131: registration of a charge created by a company`

-- s 131(3): layer-1 function `s 131(3) the charge is one to which section 131 applies`.
@export Under section 131(3), is the charge one to which section 131 applies?
GIVEN `the charge was created by a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the charge created by a company?
      `the day the charge was created` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the charge created?
      `the charge secures an issue of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the charge secure an issue of debentures?
      `the charge is on uncalled share capital of a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on uncalled share capital of a company?
      `the charge is on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are owned by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are owned by the company?
      `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge created or evidenced by an instrument which, if an individual had signed it, would need to be registered as a bill of sale?
      `the charge is on land wherever situate or on an interest in land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on land, wherever it is, or on an interest in land?
      `the charge is for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land?
      `the charge is on book debts of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on book debts of the company?
      `the charge is on a negotiable instrument or on debentures issued by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on a negotiable instrument or on debentures issued by the Government?
      `the charge is a floating charge on the undertaking or property of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge a floating charge on the company's undertaking or property?
      `the charge is on calls made but not paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on calls made but not paid?
      `the charge is on a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on a ship or aircraft, or on a share in one?
      `the charge is on goodwill, a patent, a trade mark, a copyright or a registered design, or on a licence under or to use any of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on goodwill, a patent, a trade mark, a copyright or a registered design, or on a licence under or to use any of them?
      `the charge is capable of being registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the charge be registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009?
      `the charge was one to which section 131 applied under subsection (3) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the charge one to which section 131 applied under subsection (3) as it read immediately before 3 January 2016?
      `the charge is a shipowner's lien` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge a shipowner's lien?
      `on 1 October 2018 an order for the winding up of the company had been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 1 October 2018, had an order for the winding up of the company been made?
      `on 1 October 2018 a resolution had been passed for the voluntary winding up of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 1 October 2018, had a resolution been passed for the voluntary winding up of the company?
      `on 1 October 2018 a creditor of the company had acquired a proprietary right to or an interest in the subject matter of the lien` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 1 October 2018, had a creditor of the company acquired a proprietary right to, or an interest in, the subject matter of the lien?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(3), is the charge one to which section 131 applies` IS
    `s 131(3) the charge is one to which section 131 applies` `the charge facts`
    WHERE
        `the charge facts` MEANS `s 131(3) the facts about the charge` WITH
            `the charge was created by a company` IS `the charge was created by a company`
            `the day the charge was created` IS `the day the charge was created`
            `the charge secures an issue of debentures` IS `the charge secures an issue of debentures`
            `the charge is on uncalled share capital of a company` IS `the charge is on uncalled share capital of a company`
            `the charge is on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are owned by the company` IS `the charge is on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are owned by the company`
            `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale` IS `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale`
            `the charge is on land wherever situate or on an interest in land` IS `the charge is on land wherever situate or on an interest in land`
            `the charge is for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land` IS `the charge is for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land`
            `the charge is on book debts of the company` IS `the charge is on book debts of the company`
            `the charge is on a negotiable instrument or on debentures issued by the Government` IS `the charge is on a negotiable instrument or on debentures issued by the Government`
            `the charge is a floating charge on the undertaking or property of the company` IS `the charge is a floating charge on the undertaking or property of the company`
            `the charge is on calls made but not paid` IS `the charge is on calls made but not paid`
            `the charge is on a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship or aircraft` IS `the charge is on a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship or aircraft`
            `the charge is on goodwill, a patent, a trade mark, a copyright or a registered design, or on a licence under or to use any of them` IS `the charge is on goodwill, a patent, a trade mark, a copyright or a registered design, or on a licence under or to use any of them`
            `the charge is capable of being registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009` IS `the charge is capable of being registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009`
            `the charge was one to which section 131 applied under subsection (3) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS `the charge was one to which section 131 applied under subsection (3) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016`
            `the charge is a shipowner's lien` IS `the charge is a shipowner's lien`
            `on 1 October 2018 an order for the winding up of the company had been made` IS `on 1 October 2018 an order for the winding up of the company had been made`
            `on 1 October 2018 a resolution had been passed for the voluntary winding up of the company` IS `on 1 October 2018 a resolution had been passed for the voluntary winding up of the company`
            `on 1 October 2018 a creditor of the company had acquired a proprietary right to or an interest in the subject matter of the lien` IS `on 1 October 2018 a creditor of the company had acquired a proprietary right to or an interest in the subject matter of the lien`

-- s 131(1): layer-1 function `s 131(1) a statement of the charge must be lodged with the Registrar`.
@export Under section 131(1), must a statement of the charge be lodged with the Registrar?
GIVEN `the charge was created by a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the charge created by a company?
      `the day the charge was created` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the charge created?
      `the charge secures an issue of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the charge secure an issue of debentures?
      `the charge is on uncalled share capital of a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on uncalled share capital of a company?
      `the charge is on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are owned by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are owned by the company?
      `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge created or evidenced by an instrument which, if an individual had signed it, would need to be registered as a bill of sale?
      `the charge is on land wherever situate or on an interest in land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on land, wherever it is, or on an interest in land?
      `the charge is for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land?
      `the charge is on book debts of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on book debts of the company?
      `the charge is on a negotiable instrument or on debentures issued by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on a negotiable instrument or on debentures issued by the Government?
      `the charge is a floating charge on the undertaking or property of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge a floating charge on the company's undertaking or property?
      `the charge is on calls made but not paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on calls made but not paid?
      `the charge is on a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on a ship or aircraft, or on a share in one?
      `the charge is on goodwill, a patent, a trade mark, a copyright or a registered design, or on a licence under or to use any of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge on goodwill, a patent, a trade mark, a copyright or a registered design, or on a licence under or to use any of them?
      `the charge is capable of being registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the charge be registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009?
      `the charge was one to which section 131 applied under subsection (3) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the charge one to which section 131 applied under subsection (3) as it read immediately before 3 January 2016?
      `the charge is a shipowner's lien` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge a shipowner's lien?
      `on 1 October 2018 an order for the winding up of the company had been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 1 October 2018, had an order for the winding up of the company been made?
      `on 1 October 2018 a resolution had been passed for the voluntary winding up of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 1 October 2018, had a resolution been passed for the voluntary winding up of the company?
      `on 1 October 2018 a creditor of the company had acquired a proprietary right to or an interest in the subject matter of the lien` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 1 October 2018, had a creditor of the company acquired a proprietary right to, or an interest in, the subject matter of the lien?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(1), must a statement of the charge be lodged with the Registrar` IS
    `s 131(1) a statement of the charge must be lodged with the Registrar` `the charge facts`
    WHERE
        `the charge facts` MEANS `s 131(3) the facts about the charge` WITH
            `the charge was created by a company` IS `the charge was created by a company`
            `the day the charge was created` IS `the day the charge was created`
            `the charge secures an issue of debentures` IS `the charge secures an issue of debentures`
            `the charge is on uncalled share capital of a company` IS `the charge is on uncalled share capital of a company`
            `the charge is on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are owned by the company` IS `the charge is on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are owned by the company`
            `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale` IS `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale`
            `the charge is on land wherever situate or on an interest in land` IS `the charge is on land wherever situate or on an interest in land`
            `the charge is for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land` IS `the charge is for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land`
            `the charge is on book debts of the company` IS `the charge is on book debts of the company`
            `the charge is on a negotiable instrument or on debentures issued by the Government` IS `the charge is on a negotiable instrument or on debentures issued by the Government`
            `the charge is a floating charge on the undertaking or property of the company` IS `the charge is a floating charge on the undertaking or property of the company`
            `the charge is on calls made but not paid` IS `the charge is on calls made but not paid`
            `the charge is on a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship or aircraft` IS `the charge is on a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship or aircraft`
            `the charge is on goodwill, a patent, a trade mark, a copyright or a registered design, or on a licence under or to use any of them` IS `the charge is on goodwill, a patent, a trade mark, a copyright or a registered design, or on a licence under or to use any of them`
            `the charge is capable of being registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009` IS `the charge is capable of being registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009`
