GIVEN `the charge has become void under section 131` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the charge become void under section 131?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(2), does the money secured by the charge become immediately payable by force of this subsection` IS
    `s 131(2) the money secured by the charge becomes immediately payable by force of this subsection` `the charge has become void under section 131`

-- s 131(5): layer-1 function `s 131(5) the lodging of the statement is sufficient`.
@export Under section 131(5), is the lodging of the statement sufficient?
GIVEN `the debentures are a series giving by reference to an instrument a charge to the benefit of which the debenture holders of the series are entitled equally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the debentures a series giving, by reference to an instrument, a charge to the benefit of which the holders of the series are entitled equally?
      `the day the instrument containing the charge was executed, or the first debenture of the series if there is no such instrument` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the instrument containing the charge executed (or, if there is none, the first debenture of the series)?
      `the day the statement was lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the statement lodged?
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document executed or made in a place out of Singapore?
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many further days has the Registrar allowed for lodging (0 if none)?
      `the statement gives the total amount secured by the whole series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the total amount secured by the whole series?
      `the statement gives the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series and the date of the covering instrument (if any)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series, and the date of the covering instrument (if any)?
      `the statement gives a general description of the property charged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give a general description of the property charged?
      `the statement gives the names of the trustee (if any) for the debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the names of the trustee (if any) for the debenture holders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(5), is the lodging of the statement sufficient` IS
