-- s 131(6): layer-1 function `s 131(6) the particulars of the issue are lodged within 30 days after the issue`.
@export Under section 131(6), were the particulars of the issue lodged within 30 days after the issue?
GIVEN `the day of the issue` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the issue of debentures made?
      `the day the particulars were lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the particulars lodged?
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document executed or made in a place out of Singapore?
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many further days has the Registrar allowed for lodging (0 if none)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(6), were the particulars of the issue lodged within 30 days after the issue` IF
    `s 131(6) the particulars of the issue are lodged within 30 days after the issue` `the day of the issue` `the day the particulars were lodged` `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`

-- s 131(6): layer-1 function `s 131(6) the omission affects the validity of the debentures issued`.
@export Under section 131(6), does the omission to lodge the particulars of an issue affect the validity of the debentures issued?
GIVEN `the particulars of the date and amount of an issue were not lodged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the particulars of the date and amount of the issue not lodged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(6), does the omission to lodge the particulars of an issue affect the validity of the debentures issued` IS
    `s 131(6) the omission affects the validity of the debentures issued` `the particulars of the date and amount of an issue were not lodged`

-- s 131(10): layer-1 function `s 131(10) the subsequent charge is not operative and has no validity as respects the property comprised in the prior charge`.
@export Under section 131(10), is the subsequent charge not operative and without validity as respects the property comprised in the prior charge?
GIVEN `the subsequent charge requires registration under section 131` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the subsequent charge require registration under section 131?
      `the subsequent charge was created before the lapse of 30 days after the creation of a prior unregistered charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the subsequent charge created before 30 days had passed after the creation of a prior charge that has not been registered?
      `the subsequent charge comprises all or part of the property comprised in the prior charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the subsequent charge comprise all or part of the property comprised in the prior charge?
      `the subsequent charge is given as security for the same debt as the prior charge, or any part of that debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsequent charge given as security for the same debt as the prior charge, or any part of that debt?
      `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Court that the subsequent charge was given in good faith for the purpose of correcting some material error in the prior charge or under other proper circumstances and not for the purposes of avoiding or evading the provisions of section 131` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved to the satisfaction of the Court that the subsequent charge was given in good faith to correct a material error in the prior charge, or in other proper circumstances, and not to avoid or evade section 131?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(10), is the subsequent charge not operative and without validity as respects the property comprised in the prior charge` IS
    `s 131(10) the subsequent charge is not operative and has no validity as respects the property comprised in the prior charge` `the subsequent charge requires registration under section 131` `the subsequent charge was created before the lapse of 30 days after the creation of a prior unregistered charge` `the subsequent charge comprises all or part of the property comprised in the prior charge` `the subsequent charge is given as security for the same debt as the prior charge, or any part of that debt` `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Court that the subsequent charge was given in good faith for the purpose of correcting some material error in the prior charge or under other proper circumstances and not for the purposes of avoiding or evading the provisions of section 131`

§§ `Section 132: default, and who may lodge`

-- s 132(1): layer-1 function `s 132(1) the person may lodge the documents and particulars for registration`.
@export Under section 132(1), may I lodge the documents and particulars for registration?
GIVEN `the person is the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you lodging on behalf of the company concerned?
      `the person is a person interested in the documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person interested in the documents?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 132(1), may I lodge the documents and particulars for registration` IS
    `s 132(1) the person may lodge the documents and particulars for registration` `the person is the company concerned` `the person is a person interested in the documents`

-- s 132(1): layer-1 function `s 132(1) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 131`; the individual is never the company: the company flag is FALSE.
@export Under section 132(1), am I guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 131?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 131` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 131 (the charge's statement was not lodged as it requires)?
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) of the Companies Act uses the phrase?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 132(1), am I guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 131` IS
    `s 132(1) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 131` `default is made in complying with section 131` FALSE `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`

-- s 132(1): layer-1 function `s 132(1) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction`.
@export Under section 132(1), what is the most I can be fined for default in complying with section 131, in Singapore dollars?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 131` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 131 (the charge's statement was not lodged as it requires)?
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) of the Companies Act uses the phrase?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 132(1), what is the most I can be fined for default in complying with section 131, in Singapore dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `s 132(1) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `default is made in complying with section 131` FALSE `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`
    WHEN JUST `the sentence` THEN JUST (`the sentence`'s `penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 132(2): layer-1 function `s 132(2) the person is entitled to recover the fees from the company`.
@export Under section 132(2), am I entitled to recover the fees from the company?
GIVEN `the registration is effected by a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the registration effected by a person other than the company?
      `the fees were properly paid by that person on the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you properly pay the fees on the registration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 132(2), am I entitled to recover the fees from the company` IS
    `s 132(2) the person is entitled to recover the fees from the company` `the registration is effected by a person other than the company` `the fees were properly paid by that person on the registration`

-- s 132(2): layer-1 function `s 132(2) the amount the person may recover from the company`.
@export Under section 132(2), how much may I recover from the company, in Singapore dollars?
GIVEN `the registration is effected by a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the registration effected by a person other than the company?
      `the amount of the fees properly paid by the person on the registration, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you properly pay in fees on the registration, in Singapore dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 132(2), how much may I recover from the company, in Singapore dollars` IS
    `s 132(2) the amount the person may recover from the company` `the registration is effected by a person other than the company` `the amount of the fees properly paid by the person on the registration, in Singapore dollars`

§§ `Section 133: charges on property acquired, and on a foreign company's registration`

-- s 133(1): layer-1 function `s 133(1) the company must cause a statement of the prescribed particulars of the charge to be lodged with the Registrar`.
@export Under section 133(1), must the company cause a statement of the prescribed particulars of the charge to be lodged with the Registrar?
GIVEN `the company acquires property which is subject to a charge of a kind that would have required registration under Division 8 had the company created it after the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company acquire property that is subject to a charge of a kind that would have needed registration under Division 8 had the company created it after the acquisition?
      `a foreign company becomes registered in Singapore and has before its registration created a charge that would have required registration under Division 8 had it been created while the company was registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a foreign company become registered in Singapore after creating a charge that would have needed registration under Division 8 had it been created while registered in Singapore?
      `a foreign company becomes registered in Singapore and has before its registration acquired property subject to a charge that would have required registration under Division 8 had the property been acquired while the company was registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a foreign company become registered in Singapore after acquiring property subject to a charge that would have needed registration under Division 8 had it been acquired while registered in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 133(1), must the company cause a statement of the prescribed particulars of the charge to be lodged with the Registrar` IS
    `s 133(1) the company must cause a statement of the prescribed particulars of the charge to be lodged with the Registrar` `the company acquires property which is subject to a charge of a kind that would have required registration under Division 8 had the company created it after the acquisition` `a foreign company becomes registered in Singapore and has before its registration created a charge that would have required registration under Division 8 had it been created while the company was registered in Singapore` `a foreign company becomes registered in Singapore and has before its registration acquired property subject to a charge that would have required registration under Division 8 had the property been acquired while the company was registered in Singapore`

-- s 133(1): layer-1 function `s 133(1) the last day for lodging the statement`.
@export Under section 133(1), what is the last day for lodging the statement?
GIVEN `which case section 133(1) covers` IS A `s 133(1) paragraph` @desc Which is your case: a company acquires property subject to a charge, a foreign company becomes registered after creating a charge, or a foreign company becomes registered after acquiring property subject to a charge?
      `the day the acquisition is completed` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the acquisition completed?
      `the day the foreign company is registered in Singapore` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the foreign company registered in Singapore?
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document executed or made in a place out of Singapore?
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many further days has the Registrar allowed for lodging (0 if none)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 133(1), what is the last day for lodging the statement` IS
    `s 133(1) the last day for lodging the statement` `which case section 133(1) covers` `the day the acquisition is completed` `the day the foreign company is registered in Singapore` `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`

-- s 133(2): layer-1 function `s 133(2) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 133`; the individual is never the company: the company flag is FALSE.
@export Under section 133(2), am I guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 133?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 133` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 133?
      `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) of the Companies Act uses the phrase?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 133(2), am I guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 133` IS
    `s 133(2) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 133` `default is made in complying with section 133` FALSE `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`

-- s 133(2): layer-1 function `s 133(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction`.
@export Under section 133(2), what is the most I can be fined for default in complying with section 133, in Singapore dollars?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 133` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 133?
      `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) of the Companies Act uses the phrase?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 133(2), what is the most I can be fined for default in complying with section 133, in Singapore dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `s 133(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `default is made in complying with section 133` FALSE `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`
    WHEN JUST `the sentence` THEN JUST (`the sentence`'s `penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

