§§ `Section 137: extension of time and rectification`

-- s 137: layer-1 function `s 137 the person may apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification`.
@export Under section 137, may I apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification?
GIVEN `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company?
      `the person is a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person interested in the charge?
      `the charge was not registered within the time required, or a particular was omitted or mis-stated in the register of charges or in a statement of satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the charge not registered within the time required, or was a particular omitted or mis-stated in the register of charges or in a statement of satisfaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 137, may I apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification` IS
    `s 137 the person may apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification` `the person is the company` `the person is a person interested` `the charge was not registered within the time required, or a particular was omitted or mis-stated in the register of charges or in a statement of satisfaction`

-- s 137: layer-1 function `s 137 the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified`.
@export Under section 137, may the Court order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified?
GIVEN `an application is made by the company or a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company or a person interested applied to the Court?
      `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that the omission or mis-statement was accidental, or due to inadvertence or some other sufficient cause?
      `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that the omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders?
      `the Court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 137, may the Court order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` IS
    `s 137 the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` `an application is made by the company or a person interested` `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause` `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders` `the Court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief`

