      `the person exercises or purports to exercise a right to dispose of the shares or a right to be issued with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you exercise, or purport to exercise, a right to dispose of the shares or a right to be issued with them?
      `the person votes in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy, or appoints a proxy to vote in respect of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you vote in respect of the shares, as holder or proxy, or appoint a proxy to vote in respect of them?
      `the person is the holder of some of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of some of the shares?
      `the person fails to notify the fact of their being subject to the restrictions to a person whom the person does not know to be aware of that fact but does know to be entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to notify the fact that the shares are subject to the restrictions to a person you do not know to be aware of it but do know to be entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of the shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 245(3), what is the longest I can be imprisoned for dealing in shares subject to the restrictions, in months` IS
    CONSIDER `s 245(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions mentioned in subsection (1)` `the person has knowledge that the shares are subject to the restrictions` `the person exercises or purports to exercise a right to dispose of the shares or a right to be issued with them` `the person votes in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy, or appoints a proxy to vote in respect of them` `the person is the holder of some of the shares` `the person fails to notify the fact of their being subject to the restrictions to a person whom the person does not know to be aware of that fact but does know to be entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy`
    WHEN JUST `the sentence` THEN JUST (`the sentence`'s `penalty: the longest imprisonment, in months`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 245(4): layer-1 function `s 245(4) the officer is guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions`.
@export Under section 245(4), am I guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions?
GIVEN `shares in the company have been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have shares in the company been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed under section 245(1)?
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) of the Companies Act uses the phrase?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 245(4), am I guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions` IS
    `s 245(4) the officer is guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions` `shares in the company have been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1)` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`

-- s 245(4): layer-1 function `s 245(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction`.
@export Under section 245(4), what is the most I can be fined for issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions, in Singapore dollars?
GIVEN `shares in the company have been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have shares in the company been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed under section 245(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 245(4), what is the most I can be fined for issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions, in Singapore dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `s 245(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `shares in the company have been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1)`
    WHEN JUST `the sentence` THEN JUST (`the sentence`'s `penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 245(5): layer-1 function `s 245(5) the prosecution is barred for want of the consent of the Public Prosecutor`.
@export Under section 245(5), is the prosecution barred for want of the consent of the Public Prosecutor?
GIVEN `the prosecution is a prosecution under section 245` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a prosecution under section 245?
      `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Public Prosecutor consented to the prosecution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 245(5), is the prosecution barred for want of the consent of the Public Prosecutor` IS
    `s 245(5) the prosecution is barred for want of the consent of the Public Prosecutor` `the prosecution is a prosecution under section 245` `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the prosecution`

-- s 246: layer-1 function `s 246 the inspector has the powers and duties of an inspector appointed under section 231`.
@export Under section 246, does the inspector have the powers and duties of an inspector appointed under section 231?
GIVEN `the Minister has by notice declared that the inspector is to have the same powers and duties in Singapore as if the corporation were a declared company and the inspector had been appointed under section 231` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister by notice declared that the inspector is to have the same powers and duties in Singapore as if the corporation were a declared company and the inspector had been appointed under section 231?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 246, does the inspector have the powers and duties of an inspector appointed under section 231` IS
    `s 246 the inspector has the powers and duties of an inspector appointed under section 231` `the Minister has by notice declared that the inspector is to have the same powers and duties in Singapore as if the corporation were a declared company and the inspector had been appointed under section 231`


-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sgl (wave 2; merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: the Singapore Statutes Online
-- informal consolidation in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026, amendments up to Act 24 of 2025.
-- That text is a rendering, not the official text of the Act.
-- Part 5, Division 3 (meetings and resolutions), ss 173J to 189 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, the secretary or a member
-- (shareholder) of a company, or who deals with one: someone asking, on facts they can state,
-- what the Act requires or lets them do at and about meetings and resolutions, what rights
-- they have against the company or its directors, what the company must file or keep and by
-- when, and what follows if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to
-- companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
-- There is no seat for the Registrar, the Minister or the Court. Their powers appear only
-- as what they mean to this person: s 175(2) (an extension of the AGM period), s 175(4)(b)
-- (an order that a general meeting be called), s 182 (an order for a meeting), s 183(5)
-- (an order about the costs of an application) and the Minister's orders at ss 173J(7) and
-- 175(5) are asked as facts the person can state ("Has the Registrar extended the period?"),
-- never as questions about what the official may do of the official's own motion.
--
-- This layer re-asks what the layer-1 modules imported above already decide, phrased as the
-- individual would ask it. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question
-- calls one layer-1 function, or, where the text itself builds one rule on another (ss 183(1),
-- 184A(1), 184B(2), 184D(1), 189(1) and (2)), calls the layer-1 functions for each in turn.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices
-- (a kind of meeting, a kind of resolution, how the company's members' liability is limited),
-- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be
-- asked. A layer-1 input that is a MAYBE (the constitution's own figure, a day that may not
-- exist yet) is built in WHERE from a yes/no and a plain value, as IF b THEN JUST v ELSE NOTHING.
-- Some inputs are shared across questions under one name, so a form asks the fact once:
-- "I am a director of the company", "I am the secretary of the company", "I am a member of
-- the company", "the company is a private company", "the company is a public company",
-- "the liability of the company's members", "the number of directors of the company" and
-- "the date asked".
--
-- READING AN ANSWER. A question that answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN says JUST TRUE for yes, JUST FALSE
-- where the text itself says no or the facts given fail a condition the text makes a bar or a
-- duty, and NOTHING where the text does not answer on these facts (typically a "may" whose
-- "if" condition is not met). NOTES.md (### Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sgl)) says
-- which is which and lists the places where a lawyer would read the line differently.
--
-- JUDGMENTS. A judgment the text hands to someone else (the Court being satisfied, the Registrar
-- thinking there are special reasons, "a reasonable time", "without delay", "so far as
-- practicable") is asked as a plain yes/no fact the person states, never guessed.
--
-- DEPARTURES from the defaults ruled on 2026-10-18 (recorded, not fixed):
--   * The Act is mostly addressed to the company and to its officers, so many questions are
--     phrased "must the company ..." or "have the directors ...": the person asking is the
--     director, secretary or member who needs the answer, not the company. Where the text
--     names a person who "authorises or permits", "is in default" or "may require", the question
--     is put to the individual ("Am I guilty ...", "May I as a member require ...").
--   * Each offence has two questions: whether the person is guilty, and the most they may be
--     fined, in dollars. Only the highest fine is asked. No offence in these sections carries
--     imprisonment (every Penalty the layer-1 modules return here has 0 months). The Penalty
--     record's default-penalty flag (a person who is guilty may also be liable to a default
--     penalty, s 4(1)) is carried by layer 1 and not asked here; a reader who needs it should
--     read the layer-1 function. Where the text states no fine (s 181(2)), the answer is NOTHING.
--   * Every date is asked as a date, never "today": where a day depends on the present moment
--     the question asks "the date asked".
--   * One question, s 184A(6), has no input: the subsection answers the same whatever the facts.

§ `Section 173J: meetings held using technology`

@export Under section 173J(1), does section 173J apply to the meeting?
GIVEN `the kind of meeting` IS A `Kind of meeting` @desc What kind of meeting is it: an annual general meeting, an extraordinary general meeting, the statutory meeting, a meeting of a class of members, or a meeting of creditors?
      `the meeting is a general meeting of an amalgamating company mentioned in section 215C or 215D` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a general meeting of an amalgamating company mentioned in section 215C or 215D of the Companies Act?
      `the Court order for the meeting` IS A `s 173J(1) meeting ordered by the Court` @desc Was the meeting ordered by the Court, and if so under section 182 or under section 210 of the Companies Act?
      `the Court so directs that section 173J applies to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court directed that section 173J applies to the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 173J(1), does section 173J apply to the meeting` IS
    `s 173J(1) the section applies to the meeting` `the kind of meeting` `the meeting is a general meeting of an amalgamating company mentioned in section 215C or 215D` `the Court order for the meeting` `the Court so directs that section 173J applies to the meeting`

@export Under section 173J(2), may the meeting be held in the way I propose?
GIVEN `the way I propose to hold the meeting` IS A `s 173J(2) way of holding a meeting` @desc How do you propose to hold the meeting: at a physical place, at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology, or using virtual meeting technology only?
      `section 173J applies to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting one to which section 173J of the Companies Act applies?
      `subsection (5) excludes the application of paragraph (b) or (c) of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution exclude the holding of the meeting at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology, or using virtual meeting technology only?
      `the Minister has by order excluded the application of subsection (2)(c) to this class of companies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister by order excluded meetings held using virtual meeting technology only for this class of companies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 173J(2), may the meeting be held in the way I propose` IS
    `s 173J(2) the meeting may be held in the way` `the way I propose to hold the meeting` `section 173J applies to the meeting` `subsection (5) excludes the application of paragraph (b) or (c) of subsection (2)` `the Minister has by order excluded the application of subsection (2)(c) to this class of companies`

@export Under section 173J(3), may the participants in the meeting be at different places?
GIVEN `the way I propose to hold the meeting` IS A `s 173J(2) way of holding a meeting` @desc How do you propose to hold the meeting: at a physical place, at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology, or using virtual meeting technology only?
      `section 173J applies to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting one to which section 173J of the Companies Act applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 173J(3), may the participants in the meeting be at different places` IS
    `s 173J(3) the participants need not be together at the same place` `the way I propose to hold the meeting` `section 173J applies to the meeting`

@export Under section 173J(4), does the Act's reference to a thing at a meeting include its virtual form?
GIVEN `the thing the Act's reference names` IS A `s 173J(4) paragraph` @desc Which thing at the meeting does the Act's reference name: attending, being present, a member's vote, voting, the right to vote, voting on a show of hands, the right to be heard, the right to speak on a resolution, the right to speak, members being at liberty to discuss a matter, a representation read out or a declaration made, an auditor's report read, a document available for inspection, the register produced and kept open, the list of members kept open, a statement or document laid before the meeting, or a statement or document laid or caused to be laid?
      `the meeting is held wholly or partly using virtual meeting technology` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting held wholly or partly using virtual meeting technology?
      `subsection (5) excludes or modifies the paragraph, or subsection (7) excludes it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution, or an order of the Minister, exclude or modify the reference for this company?
      `the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology?
      `the means used is electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the means used electronic means, or any other means the company's constitution permits?
      `the person can be identified by a method that is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the person be identified by a method that is prescribed?
      `no method is prescribed and the person can be identified by a method the directors of the company have determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If no method is prescribed, can the person be identified by a method the directors have determined?
      `the means used is a means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company have determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the means used a means of synchronous communication that the directors have determined?
      `the document is made available during the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document made available during the meeting?
      `the document is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document made available on a website?
      `the document is made available by other means that the company has determined by ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document made available by other means the company has determined by ordinary resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 173J(4), does the Act's reference to a thing at a meeting include its virtual form` IS
    `s 173J(4) the reference includes the virtual form of what it names` `the thing the Act's reference names` `the meeting is held wholly or partly using virtual meeting technology` `subsection (5) excludes or modifies the paragraph, or subsection (7) excludes it` `the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` `the means used is electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution of the company` `the person can be identified by a method that is prescribed` `no method is prescribed and the person can be identified by a method the directors of the company have determined` `the means used is a means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company have determined` `the document is made available during the meeting` `the document is made available on a website` `the document is made available by other means that the company has determined by ordinary resolution`

@export Under section 173J(5), does the company's constitution exclude or modify section 173J?
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company incorporated?
      `the date the exclusion or modification took effect in the constitution` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the exclusion or modification take effect in the constitution?
      `the constitution excludes the application of paragraph (b) or (c) of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the constitution exclude the holding of a meeting at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology, or using virtual meeting technology only?
      `the constitution excludes or modifies the application of paragraphs (a) to (q) of subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the constitution exclude or modify the application of any of paragraphs (a) to (q) of subsection (4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 173J(5), does the company's constitution exclude or modify section 173J` IS
    `s 173J(5) the constitution excludes or modifies the section` `the date the company was incorporated` `the date the exclusion or modification took effect in the constitution` `the constitution excludes the application of paragraph (b) or (c) of subsection (2)` `the constitution excludes or modifies the application of paragraphs (a) to (q) of subsection (4)`

@export Under section 173J(6), does the reference to a member in subsection (4) include me as the member's proxy or representative?
GIVEN `the person is the member's proxy or the member's representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the member's proxy or the member's representative?
      `it is appropriate to read the reference to a member as including the proxy or the representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it appropriate to read the reference to a member as including the proxy or the representative?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 173J(6), does the reference to a member in subsection (4) include me as the member's proxy or representative` IS
    `s 173J(6) the reference to a member in subsection (4) includes the person` `the person is the member's proxy or the member's representative` `it is appropriate to read the reference to a member as including the proxy or the representative`

@export Under section 173J(8), does this Act prohibit the meeting of the board or a committee from being held in the way proposed?
GIVEN `the meeting is a meeting of the board of directors of the company, or of a committee consisting of one or more directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a meeting of the board of directors, or of a committee of one or more directors?
      `the meeting is held at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology, or using virtual meeting technology only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting held at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology, or using virtual meeting technology only?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 173J(8), does this Act prohibit the meeting of the board or a committee from being held in the way proposed` IS
    `s 173J(8) this Act prohibits the board or committee meeting from being held in the way` `the meeting is a meeting of the board of directors of the company, or of a committee consisting of one or more directors of the company` `the meeting is held at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology, or using virtual meeting technology only`

§ `Section 174: the statutory meeting`

@export Under section 174(1), must the company hold a statutory meeting?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 174(1), must the company hold a statutory meeting` IS
    `s 174(1) the company must hold a statutory meeting` `the company is a public company` `the company is a limited company` `the company has a share capital`

@export Under section 174(1), is the meeting the statutory meeting the section requires?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `the meeting is a general meeting of the members of the company called the statutory meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting a general meeting of the members of the company called the statutory meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 174(1), is the meeting the statutory meeting the section requires` IS
    `s 174(1) the meeting is the statutory meeting the section requires` `the company is a public company` `the company is a limited company` `the company has a share capital` `the meeting is a general meeting of the members of the company called the statutory meeting`

@export Under section 174(1), is the statutory meeting held in the period the subsection fixes?
GIVEN `the date the company is entitled to commence business` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company entitled to commence business?
      `the date the statutory meeting is held` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the statutory meeting held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 174(1), is the statutory meeting held in the period the subsection fixes` IS
    `s 174(1) the statutory meeting is held in the period the subsection fixes` `the date the company is entitled to commence business` `the date the statutory meeting is held`

@export Under section 174(1), how many days after the date the company is entitled to commence business is the last day for the statutory meeting?
GIVEN `the date the company is entitled to commence business` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company entitled to commence business?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 174(1), how many days after the date the company is entitled to commence business is the last day for the statutory meeting` IS
    `s 174(1) the number of days from the date to the last day for the statutory meeting` `the date the company is entitled to commence business`

@export Under section 174(2), do the directors forward the statutory report to every member in time?
GIVEN `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the statutory meeting to be held?
      `the date the directors forward the statutory report to every member` IS A DATE @desc On what date do the directors forward the statutory report to every member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 174(2), do the directors forward the statutory report to every member in time` IS
    `s 174(2) the directors forward the statutory report in time` `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` `the date the directors forward the statutory report to every member`

@export Under section 174(2), what is the latest day for the directors to forward the statutory report?
GIVEN `the date the statutory meeting is to be held` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the statutory meeting to be held?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 174(2), what is the latest day for the directors to forward the statutory report` IS
    `s 174(2) the latest day for the directors to forward the statutory report` `the date the statutory meeting is to be held`

@export Under section 174(3), is the statutory report certified by enough directors?
GIVEN `the number of directors who have certified the statutory report` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors have certified the statutory report?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 174(3), is the statutory report certified by enough directors` IS
    `s 174(3) the statutory report is certified by enough directors` `the number of directors who have certified the statutory report`

@export Under section 174(3), is the statutory report certified and does it state what the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the number of directors who have certified the statutory report` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors have certified the statutory report?
      `the report states the total number of shares allotted, distinguishing shares allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the total number of shares allotted, distinguishing shares allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash?
      `the report states, in the case of shares partly paid up, the extent to which they are so paid up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the case of shares partly paid up, does the report state the extent to which they are so paid up?
      `the report states, in either case, the consideration for which the shares have been allotted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the consideration for which the shares have been allotted?
      `the report states the total amount of cash received by the company in respect of all the shares allotted and so distinguished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the total amount of cash received by the company in respect of all the shares allotted?
      `the report contains an abstract of the receipts of the company and of the payments made thereout` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report contain an abstract of the receipts of the company and of the payments made out of them?
      `the date up to which the abstract of receipts and payments is made up` IS A DATE @desc Up to what date is the abstract of receipts and payments made up?
      `the date of the statutory report` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the statutory report?
      `the abstract exhibits under distinctive headings the receipts from shares and debentures and other sources, the payments made thereout and particulars concerning the balance remaining in hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the abstract show, under distinctive headings, the receipts from shares and debentures and other sources, the payments made out of them and particulars of the balance remaining in hand?
      `the report contains an account or estimate of the preliminary expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report contain an account or estimate of the preliminary expenses?
      `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the names, addresses and descriptions of the directors?
      `the company has trustees for holders of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have trustees for holders of debentures?
      `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the trustees for holders of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the names, addresses and descriptions of the trustees for holders of debentures?
      `the company has auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have auditors?
      `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the names, addresses and descriptions of the auditors?
      `the company has chief executive officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have chief executive officers?
      `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the chief executive officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the names, addresses and descriptions of the chief executive officers?
      `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the secretaries of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the names, addresses and descriptions of the secretaries of the company?
      `a contract the modification of which is to be submitted to the meeting for its approval exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a contract whose modification is to be submitted to the meeting for its approval?
      `the report states the particulars of the contract together with the particulars of the modification or proposed modification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the particulars of the contract together with the particulars of the modification or proposed modification?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 174(3), is the statutory report certified and does it state what the subsection requires` IS
    `s 174(3) the statutory report is certified and states what the subsection requires` `the number of directors who have certified the statutory report` a b c d e
    WHERE
        a MEANS `s 174(3)(a) the report states the shares allotted` `the report states the total number of shares allotted, distinguishing shares allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash` `the report states, in the case of shares partly paid up, the extent to which they are so paid up` `the report states, in either case, the consideration for which the shares have been allotted`
        b MEANS `s 174(3)(b) the report states the cash received` `the report states the total amount of cash received by the company in respect of all the shares allotted and so distinguished`
        abstractInTime MEANS `s 174(3)(c) the abstract is made up to a date within 7 days of the date of the report` `the date up to which the abstract of receipts and payments is made up` `the date of the statutory report` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        c MEANS `s 174(3)(c) the report states the abstract and the account` `the report contains an abstract of the receipts of the company and of the payments made thereout` abstractInTime `the abstract exhibits under distinctive headings the receipts from shares and debentures and other sources, the payments made thereout and particulars concerning the balance remaining in hand` `the report contains an account or estimate of the preliminary expenses`
        d MEANS `s 174(3)(d) the report states the names and addresses and descriptions` `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the directors` `the company has trustees for holders of debentures` `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the trustees for holders of debentures` `the company has auditors` `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the auditors` `the company has chief executive officers` `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the chief executive officers` `the report states the names and addresses and descriptions of the secretaries of the company`
        e MEANS `s 174(3)(e) the report states the particulars of the contract` `a contract the modification of which is to be submitted to the meeting for its approval exists` `the report states the particulars of the contract together with the particulars of the modification or proposed modification`

@export Under section 174(4), have the auditors examined and reported upon the statutory report?
GIVEN `the company has auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have auditors?
      `the auditors have examined the statutory report so far as it relates to the shares allotted, the cash received in respect of such shares and the receipts and payments on capital account, and reported upon it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the auditors examined the statutory report so far as it relates to the shares allotted, the cash received in respect of them and the receipts and payments on capital account, and reported upon it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
