§ `Sections 175 and 175A: the annual general meeting`

@export Under section 175(1), within how many months after the end of the financial year must the annual general meeting be held, allowing for the Minister's order under subsection (5)?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the company has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore?
      `the company has been removed from that official list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been removed from that official list?
      `the Minister has by order specified a number of months in substitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister by order specified a different number of months for the company?
      `the number of months the Minister has specified` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months has the Minister specified?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 175(1), within how many months after the end of the financial year must the annual general meeting be held, allowing for the Minister's order under subsection (5)` IS
    `s 175(1) and (5) the number of months within which the annual general meeting must be held` `the company is a public company` `the company has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` `the company has been removed from that official list` `months`
    WHERE
        months MEANS IF `the Minister has by order specified a number of months in substitution` THEN JUST `the number of months the Minister has specified` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 175(1), is the annual general meeting held in time?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the company has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore?
      `the company has been removed from that official list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been removed from that official list?
      `the Minister has by order specified a number of months in substitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister by order specified a different number of months for the company?
      `the number of months the Minister has specified` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months has the Minister specified?
      `the date the financial year ends` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the financial year end?
      `the Registrar has extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar extended the period for holding the annual general meeting?
      `the date to which the Registrar has extended the period` IS A DATE @desc To what date has the Registrar extended the period?
      `the date the annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the annual general meeting held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 175(1), is the annual general meeting held in time` IS
    `s 175(1) the annual general meeting is held in time` `the date the financial year ends` lastDay `the date the annual general meeting is held`
    WHERE
        months MEANS `s 175(1) and (5) the number of months within which the annual general meeting must be held` `the company is a public company` `the company has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` `the company has been removed from that official list` (IF `the Minister has by order specified a number of months in substitution` THEN JUST `the number of months the Minister has specified` ELSE NOTHING)
        lastDay MEANS `s 175(1) and (2) the last day for the annual general meeting` `the date the financial year ends` months (IF `the Registrar has extended the period` THEN JUST `the date to which the Registrar has extended the period` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 175(1), what is the last day for the annual general meeting, allowing for an extension under subsection (2)?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the company has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore?
      `the company has been removed from that official list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been removed from that official list?
      `the Minister has by order specified a number of months in substitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister by order specified a different number of months for the company?
      `the number of months the Minister has specified` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months has the Minister specified?
      `the date the financial year ends` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the financial year end?
      `the Registrar has extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar extended the period for holding the annual general meeting?
      `the date to which the Registrar has extended the period` IS A DATE @desc To what date has the Registrar extended the period?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 175(1), what is the last day for the annual general meeting, allowing for an extension under subsection (2)` IS
    `s 175(1) and (2) the last day for the annual general meeting` `the date the financial year ends` months (IF `the Registrar has extended the period` THEN JUST `the date to which the Registrar has extended the period` ELSE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        months MEANS `s 175(1) and (5) the number of months within which the annual general meeting must be held` `the company is a public company` `the company has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` `the company has been removed from that official list` (IF `the Minister has by order specified a number of months in substitution` THEN JUST `the number of months the Minister has specified` ELSE NOTHING)

