      `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 64 or 64A of the Companies Act make other provision on the matter?
      `the number of members physically present at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members are physically present at the meeting?
      `the number of members attending the meeting using virtual meeting technology` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members attend the meeting using virtual meeting technology?
      `section 173J(4)(b) applies to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 173J(4)(b) of the Companies Act apply to the meeting (so that a member attending by virtual meeting technology counts as present)?
      `the number of corporate members deemed to be personally present by section 179(4)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many corporate members are deemed to be personally present by section 179(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 179(1)(a), do the members personally present form a quorum` IS
    `s 179(1)(a) the members personally present form a quorum` `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` present
    WHERE
        present MEANS `s 179(1)(a) the number of members of the company personally present, counting those section 173J(4)(b) and section 179(4) add` `the number of members physically present at the meeting` `the number of members attending the meeting using virtual meeting technology` `section 173J(4)(b) applies to the meeting` `the number of corporate members deemed to be personally present by section 179(4)`

@export Under section 179(1)(b), may I be chairperson of the meeting?
GIVEN `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution make other provision on the matter?
      `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 64 or 64A of the Companies Act make other provision on the matter?
      `I have been elected by the members present at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been elected by the members present at the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 179(1)(b), may I be chairperson of the meeting` IS
    `s 179(1)(b) the member may be chairperson of the meeting` `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` `I have been elected by the members present at the meeting`

@export Under section 179(1)(c)(i), how many votes do I have on a show of hands?
GIVEN `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution make other provision on the matter?
      `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 64 or 64A of the Companies Act make other provision on the matter?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `I am personally present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you personally present at the meeting?
      `I am entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to vote at the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 179(1)(c)(i), how many votes do I have on a show of hands` IS
    `s 179(1)(c)(i) the number of votes the member has on a show of hands` `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` `the company has a share capital` `I am personally present` `I am entitled to vote`

@export Under section 179(1)(c)(ii), how many votes do I have on a poll?
GIVEN `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution make other provision on the matter?
      `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 64 or 64A of the Companies Act make other provision on the matter?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `the number of shares held by the member` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares do you hold in the company?
      `the number of units of stock held by the member which are or were originally equivalent to one share` IS A NUMBER @desc How many units of stock do you hold which are or were originally equivalent to one share?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 179(1)(c)(ii), how many votes do I have on a poll` IS
    `s 179(1)(c)(ii) the number of votes the member has on a poll` `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` `the company has a share capital` `the number of shares held by the member` `the number of units of stock held by the member which are or were originally equivalent to one share`

@export Under section 179(1)(d), how many votes does every member have?
GIVEN `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution make other provision on the matter?
      `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 64 or 64A of the Companies Act make other provision on the matter?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 179(1)(d), how many votes does every member have` IS
    `s 179(1)(d) the number of votes every member has` `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` `the company has a share capital`

@export Under section 179(2), am I free not to use all my votes or to cast the votes I use in different ways?
GIVEN `the vote is on a poll` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vote on a poll?
      `the number of votes the person is entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are you entitled to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 179(2), am I free not to use all my votes or to cast the votes I use in different ways` IS
    `s 179(2) the person need not use all the person's votes or cast all the votes the person uses in the same way` `the vote is on a poll` `the number of votes the person is entitled to`

@export Under section 179(3), may the corporation authorise a person to act as its representative?
GIVEN `the corporation is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a member of the company?
      `the corporation is a creditor, including a holder of debentures, of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a creditor, including a holder of debentures, of the company?
      `the corporation has authorised the person by resolution of its directors or other governing body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation authorised the person by resolution of its directors or other governing body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 179(3), may the corporation authorise a person to act as its representative` IS
    `s 179(3) the corporation may authorise the person to act as its representative` `the corporation is a member of the company` `the corporation is a creditor, including a holder of debentures, of the company` `the corporation has authorised the person by resolution of its directors or other governing body`

@export Under section 179(3), am I as the person so authorised entitled to exercise the corporation's powers?
GIVEN `I have been authorised under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been authorised by the corporation under section 179(3)?
      `I act in accordance with my authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you acting in accordance with your authority?
      `the corporation has revoked my authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation revoked your authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 179(3), am I as the person so authorised entitled to exercise the corporation's powers` IS
    `s 179(3) the person so authorised is entitled to exercise the corporation's powers` `I have been authorised under subsection (3)` `I act in accordance with my authority` `the corporation has revoked my authority`

@export Under section 179(4), is the corporation deemed to be personally present at the meeting?
GIVEN `the person present at the meeting is authorised to act as the representative of the corporation at the meeting by virtue of an authority given under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person present at the meeting authorised to act as the representative of the corporation by an authority given under section 179(3)?
      `the person is not otherwise entitled to be present at the meeting as a member or proxy or as a corporate representative of another member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person not otherwise entitled to be present at the meeting as a member, a proxy, or the corporate representative of another member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 179(4), is the corporation deemed to be personally present at the meeting` IS
    `s 179(4) the corporation is deemed to be personally present at the meeting` `the person present at the meeting is authorised to act as the representative of the corporation at the meeting by virtue of an authority given under subsection (3)` `the person is not otherwise entitled to be present at the meeting as a member or proxy or as a corporate representative of another member`

@export Under section 179(5), is the certificate prima facie evidence of the appointment or of the revocation of the appointment?
GIVEN `section 41(8) or (9) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 41(8) or (9) of the Companies Act apply?
      `the certificate is under the seal of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate under the seal of the corporation?
      `the certificate is of the appointment or of the revocation of the appointment of a representative under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate of the appointment, or of the revocation of the appointment, of a representative under section 179(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 179(5), is the certificate prima facie evidence of the appointment or of the revocation of the appointment` IS
    `s 179(5) the certificate is prima facie evidence of the appointment or of the revocation of the appointment` `section 41(8) or (9) applies` `the certificate is under the seal of the corporation` `the certificate is of the appointment or of the revocation of the appointment of a representative under subsection (3)`

@export Under section 179(6), is the act, matter, thing or resolution deemed to have been duly made, performed or passed?
GIVEN `a holding company is beneficially entitled to the whole of the issued shares of the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a holding company beneficially entitled to the whole of the issued shares of the subsidiary?
      `a minute is signed by a representative of the holding company authorised pursuant to subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a minute signed by a representative of the holding company authorised under section 179(3)?
      `the minute states that the act, matter, thing, or ordinary or special resolution required by this Act or by the constitution of the subsidiary to be made, performed or passed by or at a general meeting has been made, performed or passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the minute state that the act, matter, thing, or ordinary or special resolution required by the Act or the subsidiary's constitution to be made, performed or passed at a general meeting has been made, performed or passed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 179(6), is the act, matter, thing or resolution deemed to have been duly made, performed or passed` IS
    `s 179(6) the act, matter, thing or resolution is deemed to have been duly made, performed or passed` `a holding company is beneficially entitled to the whole of the issued shares of the subsidiary` `a minute is signed by a representative of the holding company authorised pursuant to subsection (3)` `the minute states that the act, matter, thing, or ordinary or special resolution required by this Act or by the constitution of the subsidiary to be made, performed or passed by or at a general meeting has been made, performed or passed`

@export Under section 179(7), has the company lodged a copy of the minute with the Registrar in time?
GIVEN `a notice, copy of a resolution or other document relating to the matter is required to be lodged by the company with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a notice, copy of a resolution or other document relating to the matter required to be lodged by the company with the Registrar?
      `a minute mentioned in subsection (6) is signed by the representative and relates to that matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a minute mentioned in section 179(6) signed by the representative, and does it relate to that matter?
      `the date the minute was signed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the minute signed?
      `the date the company lodged a copy of the minute with the Registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company lodge a copy of the minute with the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 179(7), has the company lodged a copy of the minute with the Registrar in time` IS
    `s 179(7) the company has lodged a copy of the minute with the Registrar in time` `a notice, copy of a resolution or other document relating to the matter is required to be lodged by the company with the Registrar` `a minute mentioned in subsection (6) is signed by the representative and relates to that matter` `the date the minute was signed` `the date the company lodged a copy of the minute with the Registrar`

@export Under section 179(7), how many days after the signing of the minute is the last day for lodging a copy with the Registrar?
GIVEN `the date the minute was signed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the minute signed?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 179(7), how many days after the signing of the minute is the last day for lodging a copy with the Registrar` IS
    `s 179(7) the number of days from the signing to the last day for lodging` `the date the minute was signed`

@export Under section 179(8), is the company a member for the purposes of the section?
GIVEN `the company holds shares in itself as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company hold shares in itself as treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 179(8), is the company a member for the purposes of the section` IS
    `s 179(8) the company is a member for the purposes of this section` `the company holds shares in itself as treasury shares`

§ `Section 180: a member's rights at meetings`

@export Under section 180(1), have I as a member the right to attend any general meeting and to speak on any resolution before the meeting?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member (shareholder) of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 180(1), have I as a member the right to attend any general meeting and to speak on any resolution before the meeting` IS
    `s 180(1) the member has the right to attend any general meeting and to speak on any resolution before the meeting` `I am a member of the company`

@export Under section 180(2), may the holder of the share vote on the resolution?
GIVEN `the liability of the company's members` IS A `Liability of members` @desc Is the liability of the company's members limited by shares, limited by guarantee, limited by both, or unlimited?
      `the share confers on the holder a right to vote on that resolution in accordance with section 64` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In accordance with section 64 of the Companies Act, does the share confer on the holder a right to vote on that resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 180(2), may the holder of the share vote on the resolution` IS
    `s 180(2) the holder of the share may vote on the resolution` `the liability of the company's members` `the share confers on the holder a right to vote on that resolution in accordance with section 64`

@export Under section 180(3), may the member vote on the resolution?
GIVEN `the liability of the company's members` IS A `Liability of members` @desc Is the liability of the company's members limited by shares, limited by guarantee, limited by both, or unlimited?
      `the right to vote on that resolution is conferred on the member under the constitution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the right to vote on that resolution conferred on the member under the company's constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 180(3), may the member vote on the resolution` IS
    `s 180(3) the member may vote on the resolution` `the liability of the company's members` `the right to vote on that resolution is conferred on the member under the constitution of the company`

@export Under section 180(4), does my preference share carry the right to at least one vote on a poll in respect of the share?
GIVEN `the date the share was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the share issued?
      `the share does not entitle the holder to the right to vote at a general meeting, except in the circumstances specified in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share not entitle the holder to the right to vote at a general meeting (except in the circumstances section 180(4) specifies)?
      `the share does not entitle the holder to any right to participate beyond a specified amount in any distribution, whether by way of dividend, or on redemption, in a winding up, or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share not entitle the holder to any right to participate beyond a specified amount in any distribution, whether by way of dividend, or on redemption, in a winding up, or otherwise?
      `the dividend or any part of it remains in arrears and unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the preferential dividend, or any part of it, remain in arrears and unpaid?
      `the due date of the dividend` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the dividend due?
      `the constitution provides a lesser period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the constitution provide a lesser period than 12 months after the due date?
      `the lesser period in months the constitution provides` IS A NUMBER @desc What lesser period, in months, does the constitution provide?
      `the constitution starts the period from a stated date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the constitution start the period from a stated date?
      `the date from which the constitution starts the period` IS A DATE @desc From what date does the constitution start the period?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 180(4), does my preference share carry the right to at least one vote on a poll in respect of the share` IS
    `s 180(4) the preference share carries the right to at least one vote on a poll in respect of the share` `the date the share was issued` pref `the dividend or any part of it remains in arrears and unpaid` `the due date of the dividend` lesser started `the date asked`
    WHERE
        pref MEANS `s 180(5)(a) the share is a preference share` `the share does not entitle the holder to the right to vote at a general meeting, except in the circumstances specified in subsection (4)` `the share does not entitle the holder to any right to participate beyond a specified amount in any distribution, whether by way of dividend, or on redemption, in a winding up, or otherwise` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        lesser MEANS IF `the constitution provides a lesser period` THEN JUST `the lesser period in months the constitution provides` ELSE NOTHING
        started MEANS IF `the constitution starts the period from a stated date` THEN JUST `the date from which the constitution starts the period` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 180(5)(a), is the share a preference share?
GIVEN `the share does not entitle the holder to the right to vote at a general meeting, except in the circumstances specified in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share not entitle the holder to the right to vote at a general meeting (except in the circumstances section 180(4) specifies)?
      `the share does not entitle the holder to any right to participate beyond a specified amount in any distribution, whether by way of dividend, or on redemption, in a winding up, or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share not entitle the holder to any right to participate beyond a specified amount in any distribution, whether by way of dividend, or on redemption, in a winding up, or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 180(5)(a), is the share a preference share` IS
    `s 180(5)(a) the share is a preference share` `the share does not entitle the holder to the right to vote at a general meeting, except in the circumstances specified in subsection (4)` `the share does not entitle the holder to any right to participate beyond a specified amount in any distribution, whether by way of dividend, or on redemption, in a winding up, or otherwise`

@export Under section 180(5)(b), on what date is the dividend deemed to be due?
GIVEN `the constitution appoints a date for the payment of the dividend for the year or other period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the constitution appoint a date for the payment of the dividend for the year or other period?
      `the date appointed in the constitution for the payment of the dividend` IS A DATE @desc What date does the constitution appoint for the payment of the dividend?
      `the last day of the year or other period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the year or other period?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 180(5)(b), on what date is the dividend deemed to be due` IS
    `s 180(5)(b) the date on which the dividend is deemed to be due` appointed `the last day of the year or other period`
    WHERE
        appointed MEANS IF `the constitution appoints a date for the payment of the dividend for the year or other period` THEN JUST `the date appointed in the constitution for the payment of the dividend` ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 181: proxies`

@export Under section 181(1), am I as a member entitled to appoint another person as my proxy?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member (shareholder) of the company?
      `I am entitled to attend and vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to attend and vote at the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(1), am I as a member entitled to appoint another person as my proxy` IS
    `s 181(1) the member is entitled to appoint another person as the member's proxy` `I am a member of the company` `I am entitled to attend and vote at the meeting`

@export Under section 181(1), has the proxy the same right as the member to speak at the meeting?
GIVEN `the person has been appointed as proxy to attend and vote instead of a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been appointed as proxy to attend and vote instead of a member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(1), has the proxy the same right as the member to speak at the meeting` IS
    `s 181(1) the proxy has the same right as the member to speak at the meeting` `the person has been appointed as proxy to attend and vote instead of a member`

@export Under section 181(1A)(a), is a proxy barred from voting on the question?
GIVEN `the constitution otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution otherwise provide?
      `the proxy was appointed under subsection (1C)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the proxy appointed under section 181(1C) (a member who is a relevant intermediary appointing more than 2 proxies)?
      `the question is decided on a poll` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question decided on a poll?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(1A)(a), is a proxy barred from voting on the question` IS
    `s 181(1A)(a) the proxy is barred from voting on the question` `the constitution otherwise provides` `the proxy was appointed under subsection (1C)` `the question is decided on a poll`

@export Under section 181(1A)(b), am I entitled to appoint that number of proxies?
GIVEN `the constitution otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution otherwise provide?
      `section 181(1C) applies to the member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 181(1C) apply to you (are you a relevant intermediary appointing proxies for different shares)?
      `the number of proxies the member proposes to appoint to attend and vote at the same meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many proxies do you propose to appoint to attend and vote at the same meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(1A)(b), am I entitled to appoint that number of proxies` IS
    `s 181(1A)(b) the member is entitled to appoint that number of proxies` `the constitution otherwise provides` `section 181(1C) applies to the member` `the number of proxies the member proposes to appoint to attend and vote at the same meeting`

@export Under section 181(1A)(c), are the appointments of my 2 proxies valid?
GIVEN `the constitution otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution otherwise provide?
      `the member appoints 2 proxies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appoint 2 proxies?
      `the member specifies the proportions of the member's holdings to be represented by each proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you specify the proportions of your holdings to be represented by each proxy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(1A)(c), are the appointments of my 2 proxies valid` IS
    `s 181(1A)(c) the appointments of the 2 proxies are valid` `the constitution otherwise provides` `the member appoints 2 proxies` `the member specifies the proportions of the member's holdings to be represented by each proxy`

@export Under section 181(1B), may I appoint a proxy by depositing an instrument of appointment by electronic means?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member (shareholder) of the company?
      `the instrument of appointment is deposited by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you deposit the instrument of appointment by electronic means?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(1B), may I appoint a proxy by depositing an instrument of appointment by electronic means` IS
    `s 181(1B) the member may appoint a proxy by depositing an instrument of appointment by electronic means` `I am a member of the company` `the instrument of appointment is deposited by electronic means`

@export Under section 181(1BA), has the company specified the electronic means in the notice of meeting?
GIVEN `the company has specified the electronic means in the notice of meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company specified, in the notice of meeting, the electronic means by which an instrument of appointment may be deposited?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(1BA), has the company specified the electronic means in the notice of meeting` IS
    `s 181(1BA) the company has specified the electronic means in the notice of meeting` `the company has specified the electronic means in the notice of meeting`

@export Under section 181(1C), may I appoint more than 2 proxies?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `I am a relevant intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a relevant intermediary (a bank or its wholly owned subsidiary providing nominee services, a holder of a capital markets services licence for custodial services, or the Central Provident Fund Board)?
      `each proxy is appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by the member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each proxy appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares you hold?
      `the number and class of those shares are specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the number and class of those shares specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(1C), may I appoint more than 2 proxies` IS
    `s 181(1C) the member may appoint more than 2 proxies` `the company has a share capital` `I am a relevant intermediary` `each proxy is appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by the member` `the number and class of those shares are specified`

@export Under section 181(1D), has a proxy appointed under subsection (1C) the right to vote on a show of hands?
GIVEN `the proxy was appointed under subsection (1C)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the proxy appointed under section 181(1C) (a member who is a relevant intermediary appointing more than 2 proxies)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(1D), has a proxy appointed under subsection (1C) the right to vote on a show of hands` IS
    `s 181(1D) the proxy has the right to vote on a show of hands` `the proxy was appointed under subsection (1C)`

@export Under section 181(2), does the notice contain the statement the subsection requires?
GIVEN `a statement as to the rights of the member to appoint a proxy or proxies to attend and vote instead of the member appears in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a statement of the member's right to appoint a proxy or proxies to attend and vote instead of the member appear in the notice?
      `the statement appears with reasonable prominence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement appear with reasonable prominence?
      `the notice states that a proxy need not also be a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state that a proxy need not also be a member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(2), does the notice contain the statement the subsection requires` IS
    `s 181(2) the notice contains the statement the subsection requires` `a statement as to the rights of the member to appoint a proxy or proxies to attend and vote instead of the member appears in the notice` `the statement appears with reasonable prominence` `the notice states that a proxy need not also be a member`

@export Under section 181(2), am I guilty of the offence this subsection creates?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (2) as respects the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is default made in complying with section 181(2) as respects the meeting?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(2), am I guilty of the offence this subsection creates` IS
    `s 181(2) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with subsection (2) as respects the meeting` `I am an officer of the company who is in default`

@export Under section 181(2), what is the most I may be fined, in dollars?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (2) as respects the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is default made in complying with section 181(2) as respects the meeting?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 181(2), what is the most I may be fined, in dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `s 181(2) the most the officer may be sentenced to on conviction` `default is made in complying with subsection (2) as respects the meeting` `I am an officer of the company who is in default`
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN JUST (`penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` OF penalty)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 181(3), am I guilty of the offence this subsection creates?
GIVEN `I authorise or permit an invitation to appoint as proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the invitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you authorise or permit an invitation to appoint as proxy a person, or one of a number of persons, specified in the invitation?
      `the invitation is issued at the company's expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the invitation issued at the company's expense?
      `the invitation is issued to some only of the members entitled to be sent a notice of the meeting and to vote at it by proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the invitation issued to some only of the members entitled to be sent a notice of the meeting and to vote at it by proxy?
      `subsection (4) gives me a defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 181(4) give you a defence?
