@export Under section 181(6), am I a relevant intermediary?
GIVEN `I am a bank or merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a bank or merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970?
      `I am a wholly owned subsidiary of such a banking corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a wholly owned subsidiary of such a banking corporation?
      `my business includes the provision of nominee services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business include the provision of nominee services?
      `I hold shares in the capacity of a provider of nominee services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares in the capacity of a provider of nominee services?
      `I hold a capital markets services licence to provide custodial services under the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a capital markets services licence to provide custodial services under the Securities and Futures Act 2001?
      `I hold shares in the capacity of a provider of custodial services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares in the capacity of a provider of custodial services?
      `I am the Central Provident Fund Board established by the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Central Provident Fund Board established by the Central Provident Fund Act 1953?
      `the shares were purchased under the subsidiary legislation made under that Act providing for the making of investments from the contributions and interest standing to the credit of members of the Central Provident Fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the shares purchased under the subsidiary legislation, made under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953, providing for the making of investments from the contributions and interest standing to the credit of members of the Central Provident Fund?
      `the Board holds those shares in the capacity of an intermediary pursuant to or in accordance with that subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Board hold those shares in the capacity of an intermediary pursuant to or in accordance with that subsidiary legislation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181(6), am I a relevant intermediary` IS
    `s 181(6) the member is a relevant intermediary` a b c
    WHERE
        a MEANS `s 181(6)(a) the member is a relevant intermediary because of its banking business` `I am a bank or merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` `I am a wholly owned subsidiary of such a banking corporation` `my business includes the provision of nominee services` `I hold shares in the capacity of a provider of nominee services`
        b MEANS `s 181(6)(b) the member is a relevant intermediary because of its custodial licence` `I hold a capital markets services licence to provide custodial services under the Securities and Futures Act 2001` `I hold shares in the capacity of a provider of custodial services`
        c MEANS `s 181(6)(c) the member is a relevant intermediary because it is the Central Provident Fund Board` `I am the Central Provident Fund Board established by the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` `the shares were purchased under the subsidiary legislation made under that Act providing for the making of investments from the contributions and interest standing to the credit of members of the Central Provident Fund` `the Board holds those shares in the capacity of an intermediary pursuant to or in accordance with that subsidiary legislation`

§ `Section 182: meetings ordered by the Court`

@export Under section 182, may the Court order a meeting to be called, held and conducted?
GIVEN `it is impracticable to call a meeting in any manner in which meetings may be called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it impracticable to call a meeting in any manner in which meetings may be called?
      `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner prescribed by the constitution or this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner the constitution or the Companies Act prescribes?
      `the Court acts of its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court acting of its own motion?
      `the applicant is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a director of the company?
      `the applicant is a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting?
      `the applicant is the personal representative of a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant the personal representative of a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 182, may the Court order a meeting to be called, held and conducted` IS
    `s 182 the Court may order a meeting to be called, held and conducted` `it is impracticable to call a meeting in any manner in which meetings may be called` `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner prescribed by the constitution or this Act` `the Court acts of its own motion` `the applicant is a director of the company` `the applicant is a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting` `the applicant is the personal representative of a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting`

@export Under section 182, may the Court direct that one member present in person or by proxy is deemed to constitute the meeting?
GIVEN `the Court has ordered a meeting under section 182` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered a meeting under section 182?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 182, may the Court direct that one member present in person or by proxy is deemed to constitute the meeting` IS
    `s 182 the Court may direct that one member present in person or by proxy is deemed to constitute the meeting` `the Court has ordered a meeting under section 182`

@export Under section 182, may the Court direct that the personal representative of a deceased member may exercise the member's powers at the meeting?
GIVEN `the Court has ordered a meeting under section 182` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered a meeting under section 182?
      `the member is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the member deceased?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 182, may the Court direct that the personal representative of a deceased member may exercise the member's powers at the meeting` IS
    `s 182 the Court may direct that the personal representative of the deceased member may exercise the member's powers at the meeting` `the Court has ordered a meeting under section 182` `the member is deceased`

