      `the directors have notified that person of the date when it was first received by a director in legible form or a permitted alternative form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors notified that person of the date when it was first received by a director in legible form or a permitted alternative form?
      `they did so without delay after it was first so received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they do so without delay after it was first so received?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183(4B), have the directors complied with the duty to notify the date of receipt` IS
    `s 183(4B) the directors have complied with the duty to notify the date of receipt` `the requisition under subsection (4A)(a) requests that the date of its receipt by the company be notified to a specified person` `the directors have notified that person of the date when it was first received by a director in legible form or a permitted alternative form` `they did so without delay after it was first so received`

@export Under section 183(5), is the company not bound to circulate the statement?
GIVEN `the company or a person who claims to be aggrieved has applied to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company, or a person who claims to be aggrieved, applied to the Court?
      `the Court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that the rights conferred by section 183 are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183(5), is the company not bound to circulate the statement` IS
    `s 183(5) the company is not bound to circulate the statement` `the company or a person who claims to be aggrieved has applied to the Court` `the Court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter`

@export Under section 183(5), may the Court order the requisitionists to pay the company's costs of the application in whole or in part?
GIVEN `the costs are those of an application under section 183` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the costs those of an application under section 183 of the Companies Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183(5), may the Court order the requisitionists to pay the company's costs of the application in whole or in part` IS
    `s 183(5) the Court may order the requisitionists to pay the company's costs of the application in whole or in part` `the costs are those of an application under section 183`

@export Under section 183(6), is the resolution business that may be dealt with at the annual general meeting?
GIVEN `notice of the resolution is given in accordance with section 183` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is notice of the resolution given in accordance with section 183 of the Companies Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183(6), is the resolution business that may be dealt with at the annual general meeting` IS
    `s 183(6) the resolution is business that may be dealt with at the annual general meeting` `notice of the resolution is given in accordance with section 183`

@export Under section 183(6), is notice deemed to have been given despite the accidental omission of members?
GIVEN `the notice was otherwise given in accordance with section 183` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice otherwise given in accordance with section 183?
      `one or more members were omitted from it by accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were one or more members omitted from it by accident?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183(6), is notice deemed to have been given despite the accidental omission of members` IS
    `s 183(6) notice is deemed to have been given despite the accidental omission` `the notice was otherwise given in accordance with section 183` `one or more members were omitted from it by accident`

@export Under section 183(7), am I guilty of the offence this subsection creates?
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with section 183` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a default in complying with section 183 of the Companies Act?
      `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company, or an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183(7), am I guilty of the offence this subsection creates` IS
    `s 183(7) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `there is a default in complying with section 183` `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default`

@export Under section 183(7), what is the most I may be fined, in dollars?
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with section 183` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a default in complying with section 183 of the Companies Act?
      `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company, or an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 183(7), what is the most I may be fined, in dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `s 183(7) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `there is a default in complying with section 183` `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default`
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN JUST (`penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` OF penalty)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 183(8), is the thing in legible form or a permitted alternative form?
GIVEN `the thing is legible before being sent or otherwise supplied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing legible before it is sent or otherwise supplied?
      `the thing does not change form during that process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the thing not change form during that process?
      `the form is currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company?
      `documents sent or supplied in that form can be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can documents sent or supplied in that form be received in legible form, or be made legible after receipt in non-legible form?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183(8), is the thing in legible form or a permitted alternative form` IS
    `s 183(8) the thing is in legible form or a permitted alternative form` `the thing is legible before being sent or otherwise supplied` `the thing does not change form during that process` `the form is currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company` `documents sent or supplied in that form can be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form`

§ `Section 184: special resolutions`

@export Under section 184(1), how many days' written notice does the subsection require?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 184(1), how many days' written notice does the subsection require` IS
    `s 184(1) the number of days' written notice the subsection requires` `the company is a private company`

@export Under section 184(2), may the resolution be proposed and passed as a special resolution on shorter notice?
GIVEN `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting who agreed to the shorter notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting agreed to the shorter notice?
      `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members have the right to attend and vote at the meeting?
      `the voting rights held by the members who agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do the members who agreed hold?
      `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(2), may the resolution be proposed and passed as a special resolution on shorter notice` IS
    `s 184(2) the resolution may be proposed and passed as a special resolution on shorter notice` `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting who agreed to the shorter notice` `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting` `the voting rights held by the members who agreed` `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting`

@export Under section 184(1), is the resolution a special resolution?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the number voting in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members voted in favour of the resolution (on a poll, how many votes were cast in favour)?
      `the number voting against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members voted against the resolution (on a poll, how many votes were cast against)?
      `the number of days of written notice given of the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days' written notice of the meeting was given?
      `the notice specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice specify the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution?
      `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting who agreed to the shorter notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting agreed to the shorter notice?
      `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members have the right to attend and vote at the meeting?
      `the voting rights held by the members who agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do the members who agreed hold?
      `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(1), is the resolution a special resolution` IS
    `s 184(1) the resolution is a special resolution` `the company is a private company` `the number voting in favour` `the number voting against` `the number of days of written notice given of the meeting` `the notice specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution` ans2
    WHERE
        ans2 MEANS `s 184(2) the resolution may be proposed and passed as a special resolution on shorter notice` `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting who agreed to the shorter notice` `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting` `the voting rights held by the members who agreed` `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting`

@export Under section 184(3), is the chairperson's declaration conclusive evidence that the resolution is carried?
GIVEN `the chairperson has declared that the resolution is carried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the chairperson declared that the resolution is carried?
      `a poll is demanded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a poll demanded?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(3), is the chairperson's declaration conclusive evidence that the resolution is carried` IS
    `s 184(3) the chairperson's declaration is conclusive evidence that the resolution is carried` `the chairperson has declared that the resolution is carried` `a poll is demanded`

@export Under section 184(4), is a poll deemed to be effectively demanded?
GIVEN `the number of members entitled to vote who demand a poll` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members entitled to vote demand a poll?
      `the number of them that are the company itself registered as a member` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are the company itself registered as a member?
      `the constitution specifies a number of members for a demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the constitution specify a number of members for a demand?
      `the number of members the constitution specifies for a demand` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the constitution specify for a demand?
      `the number of paid-up shares the members demanding hold` IS A NUMBER @desc How many paid-up shares do the members demanding hold?
      `the total number of paid-up shares of the company excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many paid-up shares does the company have, not counting treasury shares?
      `the voting rights the members demanding represent` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do the members demanding represent?
      `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(4), is a poll deemed to be effectively demanded` IS
    `s 184(4) a poll is deemed to be effectively demanded` `the number of members entitled to vote who demand a poll` `the number of them that are the company itself registered as a member` specified `the number of paid-up shares the members demanding hold` `the total number of paid-up shares of the company excluding treasury shares` `the voting rights the members demanding represent` `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting`
    WHERE
        specified MEANS IF `the constitution specifies a number of members for a demand` THEN JUST `the number of members the constitution specifies for a demand` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 184(4A), is the registered member a member for the purposes of subsection (4)?
GIVEN `the registered member is the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registered member the company itself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(4A), is the registered member a member for the purposes of subsection (4)` IS
    `s 184(4A) the registered member is a member for the purposes of subsection (4)` `the registered member is the company itself`

@export Under section 184(5), is the majority on the poll not less than three-fourths?
GIVEN `the number of votes cast for the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast for the resolution?
      `the number of votes cast against the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against the resolution?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(5), is the majority on the poll not less than three-fourths` IS
    `s 184(5) the majority on the poll is not less than three-fourths` `the number of votes cast for the resolution` `the number of votes cast against the resolution`

@export Under section 184(6), is notice of the meeting deemed to be duly given?
GIVEN `the notice is given in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice given in the manner the Companies Act or the constitution provides?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(6), is notice of the meeting deemed to be duly given` IS
    `s 184(6) notice of the meeting is deemed to be duly given` `the notice is given in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution`

@export Under section 184(6), is the meeting deemed to be duly held?
GIVEN `the notice is given in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice given in the manner the Companies Act or the constitution provides?
      `the meeting is held in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting held in the manner the Companies Act or the constitution provides?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(6), is the meeting deemed to be duly held` IS
    `s 184(6) the meeting is deemed to be duly held` `the notice is given in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution` `the meeting is held in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution`

@export Under section 184(7), is the extraordinary resolution treated as a special resolution for the purposes of this Act?
GIVEN `the date the extraordinary resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the extraordinary resolution passed?
      `it was duly and appropriately passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it duly and appropriately passed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(7), is the extraordinary resolution treated as a special resolution for the purposes of this Act` IS
    `s 184(7) the extraordinary resolution is treated as a special resolution for the purposes of this Act` `the date the extraordinary resolution was passed` `it was duly and appropriately passed`

@export Under section 184(8), may the matter be done by special resolution?
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company incorporated?
      `a matter is required or permitted to be done by extraordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a matter required or permitted to be done by extraordinary resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(8), may the matter be done by special resolution` IS
    `s 184(8) the matter may be done by special resolution` `the date the company was incorporated` `a matter is required or permitted to be done by extraordinary resolution`

§ `Sections 184A to 184G: resolutions passed by written means`

@export Under section 184A(1), may the company pass the resolution by written means?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's securities listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or on any securities exchange outside Singapore?
      `the resolution is one mentioned in section 175A(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one mentioned in section 175A(1)(a) of the Companies Act (a resolution of the kind that section dispenses from the meeting rule)?
      `special notice is required of the resolution by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Companies Act require special notice of the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(1), may the company pass the resolution by written means` IS
    `s 184A(1) the company may pass the resolution by written means` `the company is a private company` unlisted `the resolution is one mentioned in section 175A(1)(a)` `special notice is required of the resolution by this Act`
    WHERE
        unlisted MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 184A(9) the company is an unlisted public company` `the company is a public company` `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore`
                WHEN JUST isUnlisted THEN isUnlisted
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

@export Under section 184A(3), is the special resolution passed by written means?
GIVEN `the resolution indicates that it is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution indicate that it is a special resolution?
      `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do the members who have formally agreed to the resolution on that date represent?
      `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the total voting rights of all the members who, on that date, would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting?
      `the constitution requires a greater majority for the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution require a greater majority for the resolution than the one this section sets (75% for a special resolution, a majority for an ordinary one)?
      `the greater majority the constitution requires, as a percentage of the total voting rights` IS A NUMBER @desc What greater majority does the constitution require, as a percentage of the total voting rights? (Answer 0 if it requires no greater majority.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(3), is the special resolution passed by written means` IS
    `s 184A(3) the special resolution is passed by written means` `the resolution indicates that it is a special resolution` `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` greater
    WHERE
        greater MEANS IF `the constitution requires a greater majority for the resolution` THEN JUST `the greater majority the constitution requires, as a percentage of the total voting rights` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 184A(4), do the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do the members who have formally agreed to the resolution on that date represent?
      `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the total voting rights of all the members who, on that date, would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting?
      `the constitution requires a greater majority for the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution require a greater majority for the resolution than the one this section sets (75% for a special resolution, a majority for an ordinary one)?
      `the greater majority the constitution requires, as a percentage of the total voting rights` IS A NUMBER @desc What greater majority does the constitution require, as a percentage of the total voting rights? (Answer 0 if it requires no greater majority.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(4), do the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires` IS
    `s 184A(4) the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires` `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` greater
    WHERE
        greater MEANS IF `the constitution requires a greater majority for the resolution` THEN JUST `the greater majority the constitution requires, as a percentage of the total voting rights` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 184A(4), is the ordinary resolution passed by written means?
GIVEN `the resolution indicates that it is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution indicate that it is a special resolution?
      `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do the members who have formally agreed to the resolution on that date represent?
      `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the total voting rights of all the members who, on that date, would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting?
      `the constitution requires a greater majority for the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution require a greater majority for the resolution than the one this section sets (75% for a special resolution, a majority for an ordinary one)?
      `the greater majority the constitution requires, as a percentage of the total voting rights` IS A NUMBER @desc What greater majority does the constitution require, as a percentage of the total voting rights? (Answer 0 if it requires no greater majority.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(4), is the ordinary resolution passed by written means` IS
    `s 184A(4) the ordinary resolution is passed by written means` `the resolution indicates that it is a special resolution` `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` greater
    WHERE
        greater MEANS IF `the constitution requires a greater majority for the resolution` THEN JUST `the greater majority the constitution requires, as a percentage of the total voting rights` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 184A(4A), is the resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e) passed by written means?
GIVEN `the resolution indicates that it is a resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution indicate that it is a resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e) of the Companies Act?
      `all the members who on that date would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting have formally agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the members who, on that date, would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting formally agreed to it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(4A), is the resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e) passed by written means` IS
    `s 184A(4A) the resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e) is passed by written means` `the resolution indicates that it is a resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e)` `all the members who on that date would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting have formally agreed`

@export Under section 184A(5), is the resolution formally agreed by the member?
GIVEN `the company receives from the member, or the member's proxy if that is allowed, a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company receive from the member (or the member's proxy, if that is allowed) a document?
      `the document is given to the company in legible form or a permitted alternative form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document given to the company in legible form or a permitted alternative form?
      `the document indicates the member's agreement by signature, or by such other method as the constitution may provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document indicate the member's agreement by signature, or by such other method as the constitution may provide?
      `the document includes the text of the resolution or otherwise makes clear that it is that resolution that is being agreed to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document include the text of the resolution, or otherwise make clear that it is that resolution being agreed to?
      `the member, or the member's proxy, had a legible text of the resolution before giving the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the member (or the member's proxy) have a legible text of the resolution before giving the document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(5), is the resolution formally agreed by the member` IS
    `s 184A(5) the resolution is formally agreed by the member` `the company receives from the member, or the member's proxy if that is allowed, a document` `the document is given to the company in legible form or a permitted alternative form` `the document indicates the member's agreement by signature, or by such other method as the constitution may provide` `the document includes the text of the resolution or otherwise makes clear that it is that resolution that is being agreed to` `the member, or the member's proxy, had a legible text of the resolution before giving the document`

@export Under section 184A(6), do subsections (3), (4) and (4A) require the requisite number of members to formally agree to the resolution on a single day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(6), do subsections (3), (4) and (4A) require the requisite number of members to formally agree to the resolution on a single day` IS
    `s 184A(6) subsection (3), (4) or (4A) requires the requisite number of members to formally agree to the resolution on a single day`

@export Under section 184A(6A), is the thing in legible form or a permitted alternative form?
GIVEN `the thing is legible before being sent or otherwise supplied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing legible before it is sent or otherwise supplied?
      `the thing does not change form during that process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the thing not change form during that process?
      `the form is currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company?
      `documents sent or supplied in that form can be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can documents sent or supplied in that form be received in legible form, or be made legible after receipt in non-legible form?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(6A), is the thing in legible form or a permitted alternative form` IS
    `s 184A(6A) the thing is in legible form or a permitted alternative form` `the thing is legible before being sent or otherwise supplied` `the thing does not change form during that process` `the form is currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company` `documents sent or supplied in that form can be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form`

@export Under section 184A(7), does a reference to the passing or making of a resolution include its passing by written means?
GIVEN `the resolution is passed by written means in accordance with section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution passed by written means in accordance with section 184A of the Companies Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(7), does a reference to the passing or making of a resolution include its passing by written means` IS
    `s 184A(7) the reference to the passing or making of a resolution includes its passing by written means` `the resolution is passed by written means in accordance with section 184A`

@export Under section 184A(8), does a reference to the doing of a thing at a general meeting include the passing of a resolution authorising it by written means?
GIVEN `a resolution authorising the doing of the thing is passed by written means in accordance with section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a resolution authorising the doing of the thing passed by written means in accordance with section 184A of the Companies Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(8), does a reference to the doing of a thing at a general meeting include the passing of a resolution authorising it by written means` IS
    `s 184A(8) the reference to the doing of a thing at a general meeting includes the passing of a resolution authorising it by written means` `a resolution authorising the doing of the thing is passed by written means in accordance with section 184A`

@export Under section 184A(9), is the company an unlisted public company?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's securities listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or on any securities exchange outside Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184A(9), is the company an unlisted public company` IS
    `s 184A(9) the company is an unlisted public company` `the company is a public company` `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore`

@export Under section 184B(1), may the resolution be passed by written means?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's securities listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or on any securities exchange outside Singapore?
      `agreement to the resolution was first sought by the directors in accordance with section 184C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was agreement to the resolution first sought by the directors in accordance with section 184C of the Companies Act?
      `a requisition for the resolution was first given in accordance with section 183 and the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on members in accordance with that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a requisition for the resolution first given in accordance with section 183, and were the documents referred to in section 183(3A) served on members in accordance with that subsection?
      `the constitution prohibits the passing of resolutions by written means, either generally or for the purpose in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution prohibit the passing of resolutions by written means, either generally or for the purpose in question?
      `all conditions in the constitution relating to the passing of the resolution by written means are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all conditions in the constitution relating to the passing of the resolution by written means met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184B(1), may the resolution be passed by written means` IS
    `s 184B(1) the resolution may be passed by written means` (`s 184A(1) the company is a private company or an unlisted public company` `the company is a private company` `the company is a public company` `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore`) `agreement to the resolution was first sought by the directors in accordance with section 184C` `a requisition for the resolution was first given in accordance with section 183 and the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on members in accordance with that subsection` `the constitution prohibits the passing of resolutions by written means, either generally or for the purpose in question` `all conditions in the constitution relating to the passing of the resolution by written means are met`

@export Under section 184B(2), is the resolution invalid because it was passed in contravention of subsection (1)?
GIVEN `the resolution was passed by written means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed by written means?
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's securities listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or on any securities exchange outside Singapore?
      `agreement to the resolution was first sought by the directors in accordance with section 184C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was agreement to the resolution first sought by the directors in accordance with section 184C of the Companies Act?
      `a requisition for the resolution was first given in accordance with section 183 and the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on members in accordance with that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a requisition for the resolution first given in accordance with section 183, and were the documents referred to in section 183(3A) served on members in accordance with that subsection?
      `the constitution prohibits the passing of resolutions by written means, either generally or for the purpose in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution prohibit the passing of resolutions by written means, either generally or for the purpose in question?
      `all conditions in the constitution relating to the passing of the resolution by written means are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all conditions in the constitution relating to the passing of the resolution by written means met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184B(2), is the resolution invalid because it was passed in contravention of subsection (1)` IS
    `s 184B(2) the resolution is invalid because it was passed in contravention of subsection (1)` `the resolution was passed by written means` a1
    WHERE
        a1 MEANS `s 184B(1) the resolution may be passed by written means` (`s 184A(1) the company is a private company or an unlisted public company` `the company is a private company` `the company is a public company` `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore`) `agreement to the resolution was first sought by the directors in accordance with section 184C` `a requisition for the resolution was first given in accordance with section 183 and the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on members in accordance with that subsection` `the constitution prohibits the passing of resolutions by written means, either generally or for the purpose in question` `all conditions in the constitution relating to the passing of the resolution by written means are met`

@export Under section 184C(1), have the directors sent each member entitled to vote a copy of the text of the resolution?
GIVEN `the directors wish to seek agreement to a resolution and for it to be passed by written means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors wish to seek agreement to a resolution and for it to be passed by written means?
      `the directors have sent each member having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting a copy of the text of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors sent each member having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting a copy of the text of the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184C(1), have the directors sent each member entitled to vote a copy of the text of the resolution` IS
    `s 184C(1) the directors have sent each member entitled to vote a copy of the text of the resolution` `the directors wish to seek agreement to a resolution and for it to be passed by written means` `the directors have sent each member having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting a copy of the text of the resolution`

@export Under section 184C(2), have the directors complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay?
GIVEN `the directors complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors comply with section 184C(1) as respects every member at the same time?
      `the directors complied with subsection (1) without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors comply with section 184C(1) without delay?
      `it was practicable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it practicable to do so?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184C(2), have the directors complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay` IS
    `s 184C(2) the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay` `the directors complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time` `the directors complied with subsection (1) without delay` `it was practicable to do so`

@export Under section 184C(3), have the directors complied with subsections (1) and (2)?
GIVEN `the directors secure that the same paper document containing the text of the resolution is sent without delay to each member in turn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors secure that the same paper document containing the text of the resolution is sent without delay to each member in turn?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184C(3), have the directors complied with subsections (1) and (2)` IS
    `s 184C(3) the directors have complied with subsections (1) and (2)` `the directors secure that the same paper document containing the text of the resolution is sent without delay to each member in turn`

@export Under section 184C(4), is the validity of the resolution not affected by its being passed before the directors complied with subsection (1)?
GIVEN `the resolution is passed before the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution passed before the directors have complied with section 184C(1) as respects every member?
      `section 184D applies to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 184D apply to the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184C(4), is the validity of the resolution not affected by its being passed before the directors complied with subsection (1)` IS
    `s 184C(4) the validity of the resolution is not affected by its being passed before the directors complied with subsection (1)` `the resolution is passed before the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member` `section 184D applies to the resolution`

@export Under section 184D(1), may I, as a member, give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, as section 4(1) of the Companies Act uses the word?
      `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's securities listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or on any securities exchange outside Singapore?
      `the voting rights I and the other members who join in the notice represent` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do you and the other members who join in the notice represent?
      `the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting?
      `the day the text of the resolution was sent to them in accordance with section 184C or the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on them` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the text of the resolution sent to the members in accordance with section 184C, or the documents referred to in section 183(3A) served on them?
      `the day they gave notice to the company requiring a general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date did they give notice to the company requiring a general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184D(1), may I, as a member, give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution` IS
    `s 184D(1) the member or members may give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution` (`s 184A(1) the company is a private company or an unlisted public company` `the company is a private company` `the company is a public company` `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore`) `the voting rights I and the other members who join in the notice represent` `the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` `the day the text of the resolution was sent to them in accordance with section 184C or the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on them` `the day they gave notice to the company requiring a general meeting`

@export Under section 184D(2)(a), is the resolution invalid because notice was given under subsection (1)?
GIVEN `notice is given under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a member or have members given notice to the company under section 184D(1) requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184D(2)(a), is the resolution invalid because notice was given under subsection (1)` IS
    `s 184D(2)(a) the resolution is invalid because notice was given under subsection (1)` `notice is given under subsection (1)`

@export Under section 184D(2)(b), have the directors proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution?
GIVEN `notice is given under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a member or have members given notice to the company under section 184D(1) requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution?
      `the directors have proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184D(2)(b), have the directors proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution` IS
    `s 184D(2)(b) the directors have proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution` `notice is given under subsection (1)` `the directors have proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution`

@export Under section 184DA(1), what is the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of circulation?
GIVEN `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written resolution circulated to the members?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 184DA(1), what is the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of circulation` IS
    `s 184DA(1) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of circulation` `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members`

@export Under section 184DA(1), was the resolution passed before the end of the period?
GIVEN `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written resolution circulated to the members?
      `the resolution has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the resolution been passed?
      `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the resolution passed? (Give any date if it has not been passed.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184DA(1), was the resolution passed before the end of the period` IS
    `s 184DA(1) the resolution was passed before the end of the period` `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` passedOn
    WHERE
        passedOn MEANS IF `the resolution has been passed` THEN JUST `the day the resolution was passed` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 184DA(1), has the resolution lapsed?
GIVEN `the constitution provides another period for the resolution to be passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution provide another period within which the resolution must be passed?
      `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written resolution circulated to the members?
      `the resolution has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the resolution been passed?
      `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the resolution passed? (Give any date if it has not been passed.)
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184DA(1), has the resolution lapsed` IS
    `s 184DA(1) the resolution has lapsed` `the constitution provides another period for the resolution to be passed` `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` passedOn `the date asked`
    WHERE
        passedOn MEANS IF `the resolution has been passed` THEN JUST `the day the resolution was passed` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 184DA(2), is the agreement to the resolution ineffective?
GIVEN `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written resolution circulated to the members?
      `the day the agreement was indicated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the agreement to the resolution indicated?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184DA(2), is the agreement to the resolution ineffective` IS
    `s 184DA(2) the agreement to the resolution is ineffective` `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` `the day the agreement was indicated`

@export Under section 184E(1), how many days after the awareness is the last day for notifying members that the resolution has been passed?
GIVEN `the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company is aware that it has been passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was a director or the secretary of the company first aware that the resolution had been passed?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 184E(1), how many days after the awareness is the last day for notifying members that the resolution has been passed` IS
    `s 184E(1) the number of days from the awareness to the last day for notifying members` `the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company is aware that it has been passed`

@export Under section 184E(1), has the company notified every member that the resolution has been passed in time?
GIVEN `the resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company is passed by written means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one of a private company or an unlisted public company, passed by written means?
      `the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company is aware that it has been passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was a director or the secretary of the company first aware that the resolution had been passed?
      `the date the company had notified every member that it has been passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company notify every member that the resolution had been passed? (Ask only once it has.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184E(1), has the company notified every member that the resolution has been passed in time` IS
    `s 184E(1) the company has notified every member that the resolution has been passed in time` `the resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company is passed by written means` `the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company is aware that it has been passed` `the date the company had notified every member that it has been passed`

@export Under section 184E(2), is the resolution invalid because the company did not comply with section 184E?
GIVEN `the company did not comply with section 184E` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company not comply with section 184E (notifying every member that the resolution has been passed)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184E(2), is the resolution invalid because the company did not comply with section 184E` IS
    `s 184E(2) the resolution is invalid because the company did not comply with section 184E` `the company did not comply with section 184E`

@export Under section 184F(1), has the company caused the record of the resolution to be entered in a book?
GIVEN `the resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company is passed by written means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one of a private company or an unlisted public company, passed by written means?
      `the company has caused a record of the resolution and of each member's agreement to be entered in a book in the same way as minutes of proceedings of a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company caused a record of the resolution and of each member's agreement to be entered in a book in the same way as minutes of proceedings of a general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184F(1), has the company caused the record of the resolution to be entered in a book` IS
    `s 184F(1) the company has caused the record to be entered in a book` `the resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company is passed by written means` `the company has caused a record of the resolution and of each member's agreement to be entered in a book in the same way as minutes of proceedings of a general meeting`

@export Under section 184F(2), is the resolution invalid because the company did not comply with subsection (1)?
GIVEN `the company did not comply with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company not comply with section 184F(1) (entering the record in a book)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184F(2), is the resolution invalid because the company did not comply with subsection (1)` IS
    `s 184F(2) the resolution is invalid because the company did not comply with subsection (1)` `the company did not comply with subsection (1)`

@export Under section 184F(3), is the record evidence of the proceedings in passing the resolution?
GIVEN `the record purports to be signed by a director or the secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the record purport to be signed by a director or the secretary of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184F(3), is the record evidence of the proceedings in passing the resolution` IS
    `s 184F(3) the record is evidence of the proceedings in passing the resolution` `the record purports to be signed by a director or the secretary of the company`

@export Under section 184F(4), are the requirements of this Act with respect to the proceedings deemed to have been complied with?
GIVEN `a record is made in accordance with section 184F` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a record made in accordance with section 184F?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184F(4), are the requirements of this Act with respect to the proceedings deemed to have been complied with` IS
    `s 184F(4) the requirements of this Act with respect to the proceedings are deemed to have been complied with` `a record is made in accordance with section 184F` `the contrary is proved`

@export Under section 184F(5), does section 189 apply to the record as it applies to minutes of proceedings of a general meeting?
GIVEN `a record is made in accordance with section 184F` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a record made in accordance with section 184F?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184F(5), does section 189 apply to the record as it applies to minutes of proceedings of a general meeting` IS
    `s 184F(5) section 189 applies to the record as it applies to minutes of proceedings of a general meeting` `a record is made in accordance with section 184F`

@export Under section 184G(1), may the company pass the resolution by the member recording it and signing the record?
GIVEN `the company has only one member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have only one member?
      `the member records the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the member record the resolution?
      `the member signs the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the member sign the record?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184G(1), may the company pass the resolution by the member recording it and signing the record` IS
    `s 184G(1) the company may pass the resolution by the member recording it and signing the record` `the company has only one member` `the member records the resolution` `the member signs the record`

@export Under section 184G(2), is the requirement to lodge the information or document satisfied?
GIVEN `this Act requires information or a document relating to the resolution to be lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Companies Act require information or a document relating to the resolution to be lodged with the Registrar?
      `the information or document is lodged with the resolution that is passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information or document lodged with the resolution that is passed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184G(2), is the requirement to lodge the information or document satisfied` IS
    `s 184G(2) the requirement to lodge the information or document is satisfied` `this Act requires information or a document relating to the resolution to be lodged with the Registrar` `the information or document is lodged with the resolution that is passed`

§ `Sections 185 to 187: special notice, lodging copies, adjourned meetings`

@export Under section 185, is the resolution not effective because notice of the intention to move it was not given to the company in time?
GIVEN `special notice is required of the resolution by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Companies Act require special notice of the resolution?
      `the day notice of the intention to move the resolution was given to the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date was notice of the intention to move the resolution given to the company?
      `the day of the meeting at which it is moved` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting at which the resolution is moved?
      `a meeting was called after that notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a meeting called after that notice was given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 185, is the resolution not effective because notice of the intention to move it was not given to the company in time` IS
    `s 185 the resolution is not effective because notice of the intention to move it was not given to the company in time` `special notice is required of the resolution by this Act` `the day notice of the intention to move the resolution was given to the company` `the day of the meeting at which it is moved` `a meeting was called after that notice was given`

@export Under section 185, has the company given its members notice of the resolution as the section requires?
GIVEN `special notice is required of the resolution by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Companies Act require special notice of the resolution?
      `the company gave members notice at the same time and in the same manner as notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company give members notice at the same time and in the same manner as notice of the meeting?
      `it was not practicable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it not practicable to do so?
      `the company gave members notice in a manner allowed by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company give members notice in a manner the constitution allows?
      `the day the company gave members notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company give members notice?
      `the day of the meeting at which it is moved` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting at which the resolution is moved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 185, has the company given its members notice of the resolution as the section requires` IS
    `s 185 the company has given its members notice of the resolution as the section requires` `special notice is required of the resolution by this Act` `the company gave members notice at the same time and in the same manner as notice of the meeting` `it was not practicable to do so` `the company gave members notice in a manner allowed by the constitution` `the day the company gave members notice` `the day of the meeting at which it is moved`

@export Under section 186(1), must a copy of the resolution be lodged by the company with the Registrar?
GIVEN `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution a special resolution?
      `the resolution effectively binds a class of shareholders, whether agreed to by all the members of that class or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution effectively bind a class of shareholders, whether agreed to by all the members of that class or not?
      `this Act expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Companies Act expressly provide otherwise for this resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 186(1), must a copy of the resolution be lodged by the company with the Registrar` IS
    `s 186(1) a copy of the resolution must be lodged by the company with the Registrar` `the resolution is a special resolution` `the resolution effectively binds a class of shareholders, whether agreed to by all the members of that class or not` `this Act expressly provides otherwise`

@export Under section 186(1), was the copy lodged within 14 days after the passing or making of the resolution?
GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed or made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the resolution passed or made?
      `the day a copy was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what date was a copy lodged with the Registrar?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 186(1), was the copy lodged within 14 days after the passing or making of the resolution` IS
    `s 186(1) the copy was lodged within 14 days after the passing or making` `the day the resolution was passed or made` `the day a copy was lodged with the Registrar`

@export Under section 186(1), how many days after the passing or making is the last day for lodging the copy?
GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed or made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the resolution passed or made?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 186(1), how many days after the passing or making is the last day for lodging the copy` IS
    `s 186(1) the number of days from the passing or making to the last day for lodging` `the day the resolution was passed or made`

@export Under section 186(2), must the company forward a copy of the resolution to the member?
GIVEN `the constitution of the company has not been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company's constitution not been registered?
      `the resolution is one to which section 186 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one to which section 186 applies?
      `a member has requested a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a member requested a copy?
      `the sum the member has paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum, in dollars, has the member paid?
      `the company directs a sum less than $1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company directed a sum less than $1?
      `the sum the company directs, if it directs a sum less than $1` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum, in dollars, has the company directed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 186(2), must the company forward a copy of the resolution to the member` IS
    `s 186(2) the company must forward a copy of the resolution to the member` `the constitution of the company has not been registered` `the resolution is one to which section 186 applies` `a member has requested a copy` `the sum the member has paid` `directed`
    WHERE
        directed MEANS IF `the company directs a sum less than $1` THEN JUST `the sum the company directs, if it directs a sum less than $1` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 186(3), am I guilty of the offence this subsection creates?
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a default in complying with section 186(1)?
      `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company, or an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 186(3), am I guilty of the offence this subsection creates` IS
    `s 186(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `there is a default in complying with subsection (1)` `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default`

@export Under section 186(3), what is the most I may be fined, in dollars?
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a default in complying with section 186(1)?
      `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company, or an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 186(3), what is the most I may be fined, in dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `s 186(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` `there is a default in complying with subsection (1)` `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default`
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN JUST (`penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` OF penalty)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 186(4), am I guilty of the offence this subsection creates?
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a default in complying with section 186(2)?
      `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company, or an officer of the company who is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 186(4), am I guilty of the offence this subsection creates` IS
    `s 186(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `there is a default in complying with subsection (2)` `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default`

@export Under section 186(4), what is the most I may be fined, in dollars, for all the copies in respect of which default is made?
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a default in complying with section 186(2)?
      `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company, or an officer of the company who is in default?
      `the number of copies in respect of which default is made` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many copies is default made?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 186(4), what is the most I may be fined, in dollars, for all the copies in respect of which default is made` IS
    CONSIDER `s 186(4) the fine on conviction` `there is a default in complying with subsection (2)` `I am the company or an officer of the company who is in default` `the number of copies in respect of which default is made`
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN JUST (`penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` OF penalty)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 187, on what date is the resolution treated as having been passed?
GIVEN `the resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of a company, or of holders of any class of shares, or of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution passed at an adjourned meeting of the company, of holders of a class of shares, or of directors?
      `the date on which it was in fact passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it in fact passed?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 187, on what date is the resolution treated as having been passed` IS
    `s 187 the date the resolution is treated as having been passed` `the resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of a company, or of holders of any class of shares, or of directors` `the date on which it was in fact passed`

§ `Sections 188 and 189: minutes of proceedings`

@export Under section 188(1)(a), how many days after the meeting is the last day for entering the minutes in a book?
GIVEN `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the relevant meeting held?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 188(1)(a), how many days after the meeting is the last day for entering the minutes in a book` IS
    `s 188(1)(a) the number of days from the meeting to the last day for entering the minutes` `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held`

@export Under section 188(1)(a), has the company caused the minutes to be entered in a book within one month?
