      `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the relevant meeting held?
      `the date the minutes were entered in a book kept for that purpose` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the minutes entered in a book kept for that purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 188(1)(a), has the company caused the minutes to be entered in a book within one month` IS
    `s 188(1)(a) the company has caused the minutes to be entered in a book within one month` `the proceedings are those of a general meeting, or of a meeting of its directors or of its chief executive officers` `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held` `the date the minutes were entered in a book kept for that purpose`

@export Under section 188(1)(b), have the minutes been signed by the chairperson of the meeting or of the next succeeding meeting?
GIVEN `the minutes are signed by the chairperson of the meeting at which the proceedings were had` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the minutes signed by the chairperson of the meeting at which the proceedings were had?
      `the minutes are signed by the chairperson of the next succeeding meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the minutes signed by the chairperson of the next succeeding meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 188(1)(b), have the minutes been signed by the chairperson of the meeting or of the next succeeding meeting` IS
    `s 188(1)(b) the minutes have been signed by the chairperson of the meeting or of the next succeeding meeting` `the minutes are signed by the chairperson of the meeting at which the proceedings were had` `the minutes are signed by the chairperson of the next succeeding meeting`

@export Under section 188(2), are the minutes evidence of the proceedings to which they relate?
GIVEN `the minutes are entered in a book and purport to be signed as provided in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the minutes entered in a book and do they purport to be signed as section 188(1) provides?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 188(2), are the minutes evidence of the proceedings to which they relate` IS
    `s 188(2) the minutes are evidence of the proceedings to which they relate` `the minutes are entered in a book and purport to be signed as provided in subsection (1)` `the contrary is proved`

@export Under section 188(3)(a), is the meeting deemed to have been duly held and convened?
