      `the company fails to comply with section 191(1) or (2), with section 192 or with any requirements of this Act as to the production of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company fails to comply with section 191(1) or (2), with section 192 or with any requirements of this Act as to the production of the register?
      `the failure is by reason of any default of that other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the failure is by reason of any default of that other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 193, does the Court's power under section 399 extend to orders against that other person and that person's officers and employees` IS
    `s 193 the power of the Court under section 399 extends to orders against that other person and that person's officers and employees` `the register of members is kept at the office of some person other than the public company by virtue of section 191(1)(b)` `the company fails to comply with section 191(1) or (2), with section 192 or with any requirements of this Act as to the production of the register` `the failure is by reason of any default of that other person`

-- section 193: s 193 the most the other person may be sentenced to on conviction
@export Under section 193, what is the most that other person can be fined?
GIVEN `the offence the default falls under` IS A `s 193 offence the default falls under` @desc Which offence does the default fall under: the offence of section 191(3), the offence of section 192(4), or an offence for failing to comply with a requirement of the Act as to the production of the register?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 193, what is the most that other person can be fined` IS
    CONSIDER `s 193 the most the other person may be sentenced to on conviction` `the offence the default falls under`
        WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `Section 194: rectification of the register`

-- section 194(1): s 194(1) the person may apply to the Court for rectification of the register
@export Under section 194(1), may I apply to the Court to rectify my company's register?
