    `s 194(1) the person may apply to the Court for rectification of the register` `a ground in section 194(1)(a) or (b) is made out` `the applicant is the person aggrieved, a member or the public company`

-- section 194(1): s 194(1) the Court may order the public company to pay damages sustained by a party to the application
@export Under section 194(1), may the Court order my company to pay damages sustained by a party to the application?
GIVEN `an application for rectification of the register has been made under section 194(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an application for rectification of the register has been made under section 194(1)?
      `a party to the application has sustained damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a party to the application has sustained damages?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 194(1), may the Court order my company to pay damages sustained by a party to the application` IS
    `s 194(1) the Court may order the public company to pay damages sustained by a party to the application` `an application for rectification of the register has been made under section 194(1)` `a party to the application has sustained damages`

-- section 194(2): s 194(2) the Court may decide the question on the application
@export Under section 194(2), may the Court decide this question on the application?
GIVEN `an application for rectification of the register has been made under section 194(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an application for rectification of the register has been made under section 194(1)?
      `the question the Court is asked to decide` IS A `s 194(2) question` @desc What kind of question is the Court asked to decide on the application: a question about a party's title to have a name entered in or omitted from the register, a question necessary or expedient to be decided for the rectification of the register, or some other question?
