    `s 196E(a) the address in the electronic register is also kept as the contact address of the member` `the member is an individual` `the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024` `a notice of a change in the individual's contact address has been lodged under any ACRA administered Act on or after that date` `the date asked`

-- section 196E(b): s 196E(b) the contact address is made available for public access under section 12(2)(d) as the address of the member
@export Under section 196E(b), is the contact address made available for public access under section 12(2)(d) as the address of the member?
GIVEN `the member is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the member is an individual?
      `the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 196E(b), is the contact address made available for public access under section 12(2)(d) as the address of the member` IS
    `s 196E(b) the contact address is made available for public access under section 12(2)(d) as the address of the member` `the member is an individual` `the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024` `the date asked`


§ `Part 5 Division 5: the annual return and the financial year (sections 197 and 198)`

§§ `Section 197: the annual return`

-- section 197(1): s 197(1) the number of months after the end of the financial year within which the company must lodge its return
@export Under section 197(1), how many months after the end of my company's financial year does it have to lodge its return?
GIVEN `the company is a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a listed company (admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore and not removed from it)?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company has a share capital?
      `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 197(1), how many months after the end of my company's financial year does it have to lodge its return` IS
    `s 197(1) the number of months after the end of the financial year within which the company must lodge its return` `the company is a listed company` `the company has a share capital` `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore`

-- section 197(1): s 197(1) the last day for lodging the return
@export Under section 197(1), by what day must my company lodge its annual return?
GIVEN `the company is a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a listed company (admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore and not removed from it)?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company has a share capital?
      `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore?
      `the last day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the financial year?
      `the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 197(1), by what day must my company lodge its annual return` IS
    `s 197(1) the last day for lodging the return` `the company is a listed company` `the company has a share capital` `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` `the last day of the financial year` `the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)`

-- section 197(1): s 197(1) the return was lodged after the annual general meeting and within the time the subsection allows
@export Under section 197(1), was my company's return lodged after its annual general meeting and within the time the subsection allows?
GIVEN `the company is a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a listed company (admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore and not removed from it)?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company has a share capital?
      `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore?
      `the last day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the financial year?
      `the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)?
      `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc What is the day of the annual general meeting?
      `the day on which the return is lodged` IS A DATE @desc What is the day on which the return is lodged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(1), was my company's return lodged after its annual general meeting and within the time the subsection allows` IS
    `s 197(1) the return was lodged after the annual general meeting and within the time the subsection allows` `the company is a listed company` `the company has a share capital` `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` `the last day of the financial year` `the number of days by which the Registrar has extended the period under section 197(1B) (0 if the Registrar has not)` `the day of the annual general meeting` `the day on which the return is lodged`

-- section 197(1): s 197(1) the return is the return required to be lodged under section 197(1)
@export Under section 197(1), is this return the return required to be lodged under section 197(1)?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company has a share capital?
      `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore?
      `the return is lodged with the Registrar after the annual general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the return is lodged with the Registrar after the annual general meeting of your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(1), is this return the return required to be lodged under section 197(1)` IS
    `s 197(1) the return is the return required to be lodged under section 197(1)` `the company has a share capital` `the company keeps a branch register in a place outside Singapore` `the return is lodged with the Registrar after the annual general meeting of the company`

-- section 197(1B): s 197(1B) the Registrar may extend the period within which the company must lodge its return
@export Under section 197(1B), may the Registrar extend the period within which my company must lodge its return?
GIVEN `the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to extend the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to extend the period?
      `the company has applied to the Registrar for the extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company has applied to the Registrar for the extension?
      `the company is in a prescribed class of companies for which the extension is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company is in a prescribed class of companies for which the extension is made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(1B), may the Registrar extend the period within which my company must lodge its return` IS
    `s 197(1B) the Registrar may extend the period within which the company must lodge its return` `the Registrar thinks there are special reasons to extend the period` `the company has applied to the Registrar for the extension` `the company is in a prescribed class of companies for which the extension is made`

-- section 197(2): s 197(2) the return is in the form, has the contents and is accompanied by the documents that the subsection requires
@export Under section 197(2), is my company's return in the form, with the contents and the documents, that the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the return is in the form prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the return is in the form prescribed?
      `the return contains the particulars and information prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the return contains the particulars and information prescribed?
      `the return is accompanied by the documents prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the return is accompanied by the documents prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(2), is my company's return in the form, with the contents and the documents, that the subsection requires` IS
    `s 197(2) the return is in the form, has the contents and is accompanied by the documents that the subsection requires` `the return is in the form prescribed` `the return contains the particulars and information prescribed` `the return is accompanied by the documents prescribed`

-- section 197(4): s 197(4) the private company must lodge a notice of the date on which the annual general meeting was held
@export Under section 197(4), must my private company lodge a notice of the date on which its annual general meeting was held?
GIVEN `the private company is required under section 175A(4) to hold an annual general meeting for a financial year after it has lodged its annual return for that financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your private company is required under section 175A(4) to hold an annual general meeting for a financial year after it has lodged its annual return for that financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(4), must my private company lodge a notice of the date on which its annual general meeting was held` IS
    `s 197(4) the private company must lodge a notice of the date on which the annual general meeting was held` `the private company is required under section 175A(4) to hold an annual general meeting for a financial year after it has lodged its annual return for that financial year`

-- section 197(4): s 197(4) the last day for lodging the notice
@export Under section 197(4), by what day must my company lodge that notice?
GIVEN `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc What is the day of the annual general meeting?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 197(4), by what day must my company lodge that notice` IS
    `s 197(4) the last day for lodging the notice` `the day of the annual general meeting`

-- section 197(4): s 197(4) the notice was lodged within 14 days
@export Under section 197(4), did my company lodge that notice within 14 days?
GIVEN `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc What is the day of the annual general meeting?
      `the day on which the notice is lodged` IS A DATE @desc What is the day on which the notice is lodged?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(4), did my company lodge that notice within 14 days` IF
    `s 197(4) the notice was lodged within 14 days` `the day of the annual general meeting` `the day on which the notice is lodged`

-- section 197(6): s 197(6) the company is guilty of an offence
@export Under section 197(6), is my company guilty of an offence for failing to comply with section 197?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 197` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company fails to comply with section 197?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(6), is my company guilty of an offence for failing to comply with section 197` IS
    `s 197(6) the company is guilty of an offence` `the company fails to comply with section 197`

-- section 197(6): s 197(6) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence
@export Under section 197(6), am I, as an officer in default, guilty of an offence under section 197?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 197` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company fails to comply with section 197?
      `the officer of the company is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the officer of your company is in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(6), am I, as an officer in default, guilty of an offence under section 197` IS
    `s 197(6) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` `the company fails to comply with section 197` `the officer of the company is in default`

-- section 197(6): s 197(6) the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction
@export Under section 197(6), what is the most my company, or I as an officer in default, can be fined?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 197` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company fails to comply with section 197?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 197(6), what is the most my company, or I as an officer in default, can be fined` IS
    CONSIDER `s 197(6) the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` `the company fails to comply with section 197`
        WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `Section 198: the financial year of a company`

-- section 198(1): s 198(1) the company is incorporated on or after 31 August 2018
@export Under section 198(1), was my company incorporated on or after 31 August 2018?
GIVEN `the date of incorporation of the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of incorporation of your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(1), was my company incorporated on or after 31 August 2018` IS
    `s 198(1) the company is incorporated on or after 31 August 2018` `the date of incorporation of the company`

-- section 198(1)(a): s 198(1)(a) the last day of the company's first financial year
@export Under section 198(1)(a), on what day does my company's first financial year end?
GIVEN `the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)?
      `a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year?
      `the new last day specified by that notice` IS A DATE @desc If a notice under section 198(4) specified a new last day for the first financial year, what is that day (any date if none)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 198(1)(a), on what day does my company's first financial year end` IS
    `s 198(1)(a) the last day of the company's first financial year` `the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)` `a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year` `the new last day specified by that notice`

-- section 198(1)(a): s 198(1)(a) the period is the first financial year of the company
@export Under section 198(1)(a), is this period my company's first financial year?
GIVEN `the date of incorporation of the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of incorporation of your company?
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period begin?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period end?
      `the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)?
      `a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year?
      `the new last day specified by that notice` IS A DATE @desc If a notice under section 198(4) specified a new last day for the first financial year, what is that day (any date if none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(1)(a), is this period my company's first financial year` IS
    `s 198(1)(a) the period is the first financial year of the company` `the date of incorporation of the company` `the first day of the period` `the last day of the period` `the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)` `a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year` `the new last day specified by that notice`

-- section 198(1)(b): s 198(1)(b) the last day of a subsequent financial year
@export Under section 198(1)(b), on what day does this subsequent financial year of my company end?
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period begin?
      `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 198(1)(b), on what day does this subsequent financial year of my company end` IS
    `s 198(1)(b) the last day of a subsequent financial year` `the first day of the period` `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)`

-- section 198(1)(b): s 198(1)(b) the period is a subsequent financial year of the company
@export Under section 198(1)(b), is this period a subsequent financial year of my company?
GIVEN `the last day of the previous financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the previous financial year?
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period begin?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period end?
      `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(1)(b), is this period a subsequent financial year of my company` IS
    `s 198(1)(b) the period is a subsequent financial year of the company` `the last day of the previous financial year` `the first day of the period` `the last day of the period` `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)`

-- section 198(2): s 198(2) the first financial year is no longer than the subsection allows
@export Under section 198(2), is my company's first financial year no longer than the section allows?
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period begin?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period end?
      `the Registrar on the application of the company has approved a longer first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar on the application of your company has approved a longer first financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(2), is my company's first financial year no longer than the section allows` IS
    `s 198(2) the first financial year is no longer than the subsection allows` `the first day of the period` `the last day of the period` `the Registrar on the application of the company has approved a longer first financial year`

-- section 198(3): s 198(3) the company was incorporated before 31 August 2018
@export Under section 198(3), was my company incorporated before 31 August 2018?
GIVEN `the date of incorporation of the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of incorporation of your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(3), was my company incorporated before 31 August 2018` IS
    `s 198(3) the company was incorporated before 31 August 2018` `the date of incorporation of the company`

-- section 198(3)(a): s 198(3)(a) the last day of the company's first financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018
@export Under section 198(3)(a), on what day does my company's first financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018 end?
GIVEN `the company had, before 31 August 2018, lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification informing the Registrar of the end of its financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company had, before 31 August 2018, lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification informing the Registrar of the end of its financial year?
      `the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification?
      `the date of incorporation of the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of incorporation of your company?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 198(3)(a), on what day does my company's first financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018 end` IS
    `s 198(3)(a) the last day of the company's first financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018` `the company had, before 31 August 2018, lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification informing the Registrar of the end of its financial year` `the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification` `the date of incorporation of the company`

-- section 198(3)(a): s 198(3)(a) the period is the company's first financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018
@export Under section 198(3)(a), is this period my company's first financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018?
GIVEN `the company had, before 31 August 2018, lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification informing the Registrar of the end of its financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company had, before 31 August 2018, lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification informing the Registrar of the end of its financial year?
      `the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification?
      `the date of incorporation of the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of incorporation of your company?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period end?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(3)(a), is this period my company's first financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018` IS
    `s 198(3)(a) the period is the company's first financial year ending on or after 31 August 2018` `the company had, before 31 August 2018, lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification informing the Registrar of the end of its financial year` `the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification` `the date of incorporation of the company` `the last day of the period`

-- section 198(3)(b): s 198(3)(b) the period is a subsequent financial year of the company
@export Under section 198(3)(b), is this period a subsequent financial year of my company?
GIVEN `the last day of the previous financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the previous financial year?
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period begin?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period end?
      `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(3)(b), is this period a subsequent financial year of my company` IS
    `s 198(3)(b) the period is a subsequent financial year of the company` `the last day of the previous financial year` `the first day of the period` `the last day of the period` `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)`

-- section 198(4): s 198(4) the company may by notice specify a new date as the last day of its financial year
@export Under section 198(4), may my company by notice specify a new date as the last day of its financial year?
GIVEN `the notice is lodged with the Registrar in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is lodged with the Registrar in the prescribed form?
      `the notice results in a financial year being longer than 18 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice results in a financial year being longer than 18 months?
      `the day on which the notice is lodged` IS A DATE @desc What is the day on which the notice is lodged?
      `the last day of the earlier financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the earlier financial year?
      `the end of that earlier financial year was changed under section 198` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the end of that earlier financial year was changed under section 198?
      `the Registrar has approved the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar has approved the notice?
      `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 175 within which an annual general meeting of the company must be held after that financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 175 within which an annual general meeting of your company must be held after that financial year?
      `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 197 within which an annual return of the company must be lodged with the Registrar after that financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 197 within which an annual return of your company must be lodged with the Registrar after that financial year?
      `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 203 within which a copy of the financial statements and the documents mentioned in section 203(1) are required to be sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 203 within which a copy of the financial statements and the documents mentioned in section 203(1) are required to be sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(4), may my company by notice specify a new date as the last day of its financial year` IS
    `s 198(4) the company may by notice specify a new date as the last day of its financial year` `the notice is lodged with the Registrar in the prescribed form` `the Registrar's approval must be obtained for my notice` `the Registrar has approved the notice` `my notice is barred by subsection (6)`
    WHERE
        `the Registrar's approval must be obtained for my notice` MEANS
            `s 198(5) the Registrar's approval must be obtained for the notice` `the notice results in a financial year being longer than 18 months` `the day on which the notice is lodged` `the last day of the earlier financial year` `the end of that earlier financial year was changed under section 198` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `my notice is barred by subsection (6)` MEANS
            `s 198(6) the notice cannot specify the new date as the last day of the financial year` `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 175 within which an annual general meeting of the company must be held after that financial year` `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 197 within which an annual return of the company must be lodged with the Registrar after that financial year` `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 203 within which a copy of the financial statements and the documents mentioned in section 203(1) are required to be sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- section 198(5): s 198(5) the Registrar's approval must be obtained for the notice
@export Under section 198(5), must the Registrar's approval be obtained for my notice?
GIVEN `the notice results in a financial year being longer than 18 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice results in a financial year being longer than 18 months?
      `the day on which the notice is lodged` IS A DATE @desc What is the day on which the notice is lodged?
      `the last day of the earlier financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the earlier financial year?
      `the end of that earlier financial year was changed under section 198` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the end of that earlier financial year was changed under section 198?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(5), must the Registrar's approval be obtained for my notice` IS
    `s 198(5) the Registrar's approval must be obtained for the notice` `the notice results in a financial year being longer than 18 months` `the day on which the notice is lodged` `the last day of the earlier financial year` `the end of that earlier financial year was changed under section 198`

-- section 198(6): s 198(6) the notice cannot specify the new date as the last day of the financial year
@export Under section 198(6), is my notice barred from specifying the new date as the last day of the financial year?
GIVEN `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 175 within which an annual general meeting of the company must be held after that financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 175 within which an annual general meeting of your company must be held after that financial year?
      `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 197 within which an annual return of the company must be lodged with the Registrar after that financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 197 within which an annual return of your company must be lodged with the Registrar after that financial year?
      `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 203 within which a copy of the financial statements and the documents mentioned in section 203(1) are required to be sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 203 within which a copy of the financial statements and the documents mentioned in section 203(1) are required to be sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(6), is my notice barred from specifying the new date as the last day of the financial year` IS
    `s 198(6) the notice cannot specify the new date as the last day of the financial year` `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 175 within which an annual general meeting of the company must be held after that financial year` `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 197 within which an annual return of the company must be lodged with the Registrar after that financial year` `the notice is lodged after the expiry of the period under section 203 within which a copy of the financial statements and the documents mentioned in section 203(1) are required to be sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`

-- section 198: s 198 the period is a financial year of the company as section 198 determines
@export Under section 198, is this period a financial year of my company as section 198 determines?
GIVEN `the date of incorporation of the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of incorporation of your company?
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period begin?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period end?
      `the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)?
      `a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year?
      `the new last day specified by that notice` IS A DATE @desc If a notice under section 198(4) specified a new last day for the first financial year, what is that day (any date if none)?
      `the company had, before 31 August 2018, lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification informing the Registrar of the end of its financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company had, before 31 August 2018, lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification informing the Registrar of the end of its financial year?
      `the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification?
      `the last day of the previous financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the previous financial year?
      `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198, is this period a financial year of my company as section 198 determines` IS
    `s 198 the period is a financial year of the company as section 198 determines` `the date of incorporation of the company` `the first day of the period` `the last day of the period` `the last day of the first financial year as furnished under section 19(1)(b)` `a notice under section 198(4) has specified a new last day for the first financial year` `the new last day specified by that notice` `the company had, before 31 August 2018, lodged an annual return, or lodged a notification informing the Registrar of the end of its financial year` `the last day of the financial year as indicated in the last annual return or last such notification` `the last day of the previous financial year` `the number of months in the regular interval (12, or the other interval the Registrar allows)`


§ `Part 10 Division 4 Subdivision (5): striking off and restoring a company's name (sections 344 to 344H)`

§§ `Section 344: striking off by the Registrar`

-- section 344(1): s 344(1) the Registrar may send the company and its directors, secretaries and members a letter
@export Under section 344(1), may the Registrar send my company, its directors, secretaries and members a letter that its name may be struck off?
GIVEN `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the company is not carrying on business or is not in operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that your company is not carrying on business or is not in operation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(1), may the Registrar send my company, its directors, secretaries and members a letter that its name may be struck off` IS
    `s 344(1) the Registrar may send the company and its directors, secretaries and members a letter` `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the company is not carrying on business or is not in operation`

-- section 344(1): s 344(1) the last day for an answer showing cause to the contrary
@export Under section 344(1), by what day must an answer showing cause to the contrary be received?
GIVEN `the date of the letter` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the Registrar's letter dated?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 344(1), by what day must an answer showing cause to the contrary be received` IS
    `s 344(1) the last day for an answer showing cause to the contrary` `the date of the letter`

-- section 344(1): s 344(1) the answer was received within 30 days after the date of the letter
@export Under section 344(1), was my answer received within 30 days after the date of the letter?
GIVEN `the date of the letter` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the Registrar's letter dated?
      `the day on which an answer showing cause to the contrary is received` IS A DATE @desc What is the day on which an answer showing cause to the contrary is received?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(1), was my answer received within 30 days after the date of the letter` IF
    `s 344(1) the answer was received within 30 days after the date of the letter` `the date of the letter` `the day on which an answer showing cause to the contrary is received`

-- section 344(1A): s 344(1A) the Registrar may have regard to the circumstance in determining whether the company is not carrying on business
@export Under section 344(1A), may the Registrar have regard to this circumstance in deciding whether my company is not carrying on business?
GIVEN `the circumstance is one prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the circumstance you are asking about one that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(1A), may the Registrar have regard to this circumstance in deciding whether my company is not carrying on business` IS
    `s 344(1A) the Registrar may have regard to the circumstance in determining whether the company is not carrying on business` `the circumstance is one prescribed`

-- section 344(2): s 344(2) the Registrar may publish the notice that the name of the company will be struck off
@export Under section 344(2), may the Registrar publish the notice that my company's name will be struck off?
GIVEN `the Registrar has sent the letter mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar has sent the letter mentioned in subsection (1)?
      `the date of the letter` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the Registrar's letter dated?
      `an answer to the effect that the company is carrying on business or is in operation has been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an answer to the effect that your company is carrying on business or is in operation has been received?
      `the day on which that answer was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the answer received?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(2), may the Registrar publish the notice that my company's name will be struck off` IS
    `s 344(2) the Registrar may publish the notice that the name of the company will be struck off` `the Registrar has sent the letter mentioned in subsection (1)` `the date of the letter` `an answer to the effect that the company is carrying on business or is in operation has been received` `the day on which that answer was received`

-- section 344(2): s 344(2) the last day of the 60 days after the date of the notice
@export Under section 344(2), on what day do the 60 days after the date of the notice end?
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the Registrar's notice dated?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 344(2), on what day do the 60 days after the date of the notice end` IS
    `s 344(2) the last day of the 60 days after the date of the notice` `the date of the notice`

-- section 344(3): s 344(3) the Registrar may publish in the Gazette and send the notice to the same effect as the notice under subsection (2)
@export Under section 344(3), may the Registrar publish and send a notice that my company, which is being wound up, will be struck off?
GIVEN `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company is being wound up?
      `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that no liquidator is acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that no liquidator is acting?
      `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of the company are fully wound up and for a period of 6 months the liquidator has been in default in lodging any return required to be made by the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of your company are fully wound up and for a period of 6 months the liquidator has been in default in lodging any return required to be made by the liquidator?
      `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of the company have been fully wound up under Division 2 of Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 and there are no assets or the assets available are not sufficient to pay the costs of obtaining an order of the Court dissolving the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of your company have been fully wound up under Division 2 of Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 and there are no assets or the assets available are not sufficient to pay the costs of obtaining an order of the Court dissolving your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(3), may the Registrar publish and send a notice that my company, which is being wound up, will be struck off` IS
    `s 344(3) the Registrar may publish in the Gazette and send the notice to the same effect as the notice under subsection (2)` `the company is being wound up` `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that no liquidator is acting` `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of the company are fully wound up and for a period of 6 months the liquidator has been in default in lodging any return required to be made by the liquidator` `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of the company have been fully wound up under Division 2 of Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 and there are no assets or the assets available are not sufficient to pay the costs of obtaining an order of the Court dissolving the company`

-- section 344(4): s 344(4) the Registrar may strike the name of the company off the register
@export Under section 344(4), may the Registrar now strike my company's name off the register?
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the Registrar's notice dated?
      `cause to the contrary has been shown before the time mentioned in the notice expires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that cause to the contrary has been shown before the time mentioned in the notice expires?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(4), may the Registrar now strike my company's name off the register` IS
    `s 344(4) the Registrar may strike the name of the company off the register` `the date of the notice` `cause to the contrary has been shown before the time mentioned in the notice expires` `the date asked`

-- section 344(4): s 344(4) the Registrar must publish notice of the striking off in the Gazette
@export Under section 344(4), must the Registrar publish notice of the striking off in the Gazette?
GIVEN `the Registrar has struck the name of the company off the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar has struck the name of your company off the register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(4), must the Registrar publish notice of the striking off in the Gazette` IS
    `s 344(4) the Registrar must publish notice of the striking off in the Gazette` `the Registrar has struck the name of the company off the register`

-- section 344(4): s 344(4) the company is dissolved
@export Under section 344(4), is my company dissolved?
GIVEN `the Registrar has published in the Gazette the notice of the striking off of the name of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar has published in the Gazette the notice of the striking off of the name of your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(4), is my company dissolved` IS
    `s 344(4) the company is dissolved` `the Registrar has published in the Gazette the notice of the striking off of the name of the company`

-- section 344(4)(a): s 344(4)(a) the liability of the officer or member continues and may be enforced as if the company had not been dissolved
@export Under section 344(4)(a), does my liability as an officer or member continue and may it be enforced as if the company had not been dissolved?
GIVEN `the company has been dissolved under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company has been dissolved under subsection (4)?
      `the person is an officer or a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is an officer or a member of your company?
      `the person has a liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer or member you are asking about under a liability in respect of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(4)(a), does my liability as an officer or member continue and may it be enforced as if the company had not been dissolved` IS
    `s 344(4)(a) the liability of the officer or member continues and may be enforced as if the company had not been dissolved` `the company has been dissolved under subsection (4)` `the person is an officer or a member of the company` `the person has a liability`

-- section 344(4)(b): s 344(4)(b) the Court may wind up the company the name of which has been struck off the register
@export Under section 344(4)(b), may the Court still wind up a company the name of which has been struck off the register?
GIVEN `the name of the company has been struck off the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the name of your company has been struck off the register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(4)(b), may the Court still wind up a company the name of which has been struck off the register` IS
    `s 344(4)(b) the Court may wind up the company the name of which has been struck off the register` `the name of the company has been struck off the register`

-- section 344(5): s 344(5) the Court may order the name of the company to be restored to the register
@export Under section 344(5), may the Court order my company's name to be restored to the register?
GIVEN `the person feels aggrieved by the name of the company having been struck off the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person feels aggrieved by the name of your company having been struck off the register?
      `the day on which the person applies to the Court` IS A DATE @desc What is the day on which the person applies to the Court?
      `the day on which the name of the company was struck off the register` IS A DATE @desc What is the day on which the name of your company was struck off the register?
      `the Court is satisfied that the company was, at the time of the striking off, carrying on business or in operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is satisfied that your company was, at the time of the striking off, carrying on business or in operation?
      `the Court is satisfied that otherwise it is just that the name of the company be restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is satisfied that otherwise it is just that the name of your company be restored to the register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(5), may the Court order my company's name to be restored to the register` IS
    `s 344(5) the Court may order the name of the company to be restored to the register` `the person feels aggrieved by the name of the company having been struck off the register` `the day on which the person applies to the Court` `the day on which the name of the company was struck off the register` `the Court is satisfied that the company was, at the time of the striking off, carrying on business or in operation` `the Court is satisfied that otherwise it is just that the name of the company be restored to the register`

-- section 344(5): s 344(5) the company is deemed to have continued in existence as if its name had not been struck off
@export Under section 344(5), is my company deemed to have continued in existence as if its name had not been struck off?
GIVEN `the Court has ordered the name of the company to be restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has ordered the name of your company to be restored to the register?
      `a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(5), is my company deemed to have continued in existence as if its name had not been struck off` IS
    `s 344(5) the company is deemed to have continued in existence as if its name had not been struck off` `the Court has ordered the name of the company to be restored to the register` `a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar`

-- section 344(6): s 344(6) the notice may be addressed to the liquidator at the liquidator's last known place of business
@export Under section 344(6), may a notice to a liquidator be addressed to the liquidator at the liquidator's last known place of business?
GIVEN `the notice is to be sent to a liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is to be sent to a liquidator?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(6), may a notice to a liquidator be addressed to the liquidator at the liquidator's last known place of business` IS
    `s 344(6) the notice may be addressed to the liquidator at the liquidator's last known place of business` `the notice is to be sent to a liquidator`

-- section 344(6): s 344(6) the letter or notice may be addressed to the company at its registered office
@export Under section 344(6), may a letter or notice to my company be addressed to it at its registered office?
GIVEN `the company has a registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company has a registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(6), may a letter or notice to my company be addressed to it at its registered office` IS
    `s 344(6) the letter or notice may be addressed to the company at its registered office` `the company has a registered office`

-- section 344(6): s 344(6) the letter or notice may be addressed to the company in the care of some officer of the company
@export Under section 344(6), may a letter or notice to my company be addressed in the care of some officer of the company?
GIVEN `the company has a registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company has a registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(6), may a letter or notice to my company be addressed in the care of some officer of the company` IS
    `s 344(6) the letter or notice may be addressed to the company in the care of some officer of the company` `the company has a registered office`

-- section 344(6): s 344(6) the letter or notice may be sent to each of the persons who subscribed the constitution
@export Under section 344(6), may a letter or notice to my company be sent to each of the persons who subscribed its constitution?
GIVEN `the company has a registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company has a registered office?
      `there is an officer of the company whose name and address are known to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there is an officer of your company whose name and address are known to the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(6), may a letter or notice to my company be sent to each of the persons who subscribed its constitution` IS
    `s 344(6) the letter or notice may be sent to each of the persons who subscribed the constitution` `the company has a registered office` `there is an officer of the company whose name and address are known to the Registrar`

-- section 344(7)(a): s 344(7)(a) the Registrar must ensure that the particulars are sent to the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore and the Central Provident Fund Board
@export Under section 344(7)(a), must the Registrar ensure that particulars of my company are sent to the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore and the Central Provident Fund Board?
GIVEN `the company is one mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company is one mentioned in subsection (1)?
