DECIDE `Under section 344(7)(a), must the Registrar ensure that particulars of my company are sent to the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore and the Central Provident Fund Board` IS
    `s 344(7)(a) the Registrar must ensure that the particulars are sent to the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore and the Central Provident Fund Board` `the company is one mentioned in subsection (1)`

-- section 344(7)(b): s 344(7)(b) the Registrar must ensure that the substance of the notice is also published on the Authority's website
@export Under section 344(7)(b), must the Registrar ensure that the substance of this notice is also published on the Authority's website?
GIVEN `the notice is one to be published in the Gazette under subsection (2), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is one to be published in the Gazette under subsection (2), (3) or (4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344(7)(b), must the Registrar ensure that the substance of this notice is also published on the Authority's website` IS
    `s 344(7)(b) the Registrar must ensure that the substance of the notice is also published on the Authority's website` `the notice is one to be published in the Gazette under subsection (2), (3) or (4)`

§§ `Section 344A: striking off on application by the company`

-- section 344A(1): s 344A(1) the Registrar may strike the company's name off the register on the application of the company
@export Under section 344A(1), may the Registrar strike my company's name off the register on its application?
GIVEN `the company has applied to the Registrar to strike its name off the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that your company has applied to the Registrar to strike its name off the register?
      `the grounds prescribed are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the grounds that the regulations prescribe for the application satisfied?
      `the conditions prescribed (if any) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions (if any) that the regulations prescribe for the application satisfied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 344A(1), may the Registrar strike my company's name off the register on its application` IS
    `s 344A(1) the Registrar may strike the company's name off the register on the application of the company` `the company has applied to the Registrar to strike its name off the register` `the grounds prescribed are satisfied` `the conditions prescribed (if any) are satisfied`

