-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11A (ss 386AA to 386AP) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, the company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company incorporated under the Act,
-- or of a foreign company registered under it, or who deals with one: a person asked to say who controls the company, an officer of a company that must keep a register of
-- controllers, a director or shareholder who is a nominee, a person who has received a notice, or a person the Registrar has asked for something.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.
-- There is never a seat for the Registrar, the Minister, the Authority or the Court; their powers appear only as what they mean to the individual.)
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs, one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked, and calls the layer-1 function of the
-- same provision (named in the comment above the question); no rule is restated here. The layer-1 functions already take plain facts, so no record is built here, except one list:
-- section 386AC takes a list of the kinds of controller through which the person holds the interest, which the seat asks as one kind and wraps.
-- The same fact keeps the same name and the same @desc in every question.
--
-- READING A RESULT: a question's name asks the question its body answers, in the same direction. JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text's no, NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sgn)").
--
-- WHAT THE PERSON CANNOT STATE. The amounts, periods and forms the regulations prescribe (the prescribed period, time, frequency, form, manner and place), the dates that the 2024 Act's
-- commencement fixes (the appointed days) and the Schedules' lists are facts the person supplies; a later change in any of them changes the answers.

§ `Whether Part 11A applies, and who a registrable controller is (ss 386AA to 386AC)`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AA(1) this Part applies to the company or foreign company` (sgn-application.l4).
@export Under section 386AA(1), does Part 11A apply to the company or foreign company?
GIVEN `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a company incorporated under the Companies Act?
      `the company is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company set out in the Fourteenth Schedule of the Companies Act?
      `the company is a foreign company registered under Part 11` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a foreign company registered under Part 11 of the Companies Act?
      `the foreign company is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the foreign company set out in the Fifteenth Schedule of the Companies Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AA(1), does Part 11A apply to the company or foreign company` IS
    `s 386AA(1) this Part applies to the company or foreign company` `the body is a company` `the company is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule` `the company is a foreign company registered under Part 11` `the foreign company is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AA(1A) the provision applies to the person` (sgn-application.l4).
@export Under section 386AA(1A), does the provision apply to the person?
GIVEN `the provision of Part 11A the question is about` IS A `s 386AA(1A) provision` @desc Which provision of Part 11A is the question about?
      `the person is, or there are reasonable grounds to believe the person is, a registrable controller of the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a registrable controller of the company or foreign company, or are there reasonable grounds to believe so?
      `this Part applies to that company or foreign company under section 386AA(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 11A apply to that company or foreign company under section 386AA(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AA(1A), does the provision apply to the person` IS
    `s 386AA(1A) the provision applies to the person` `the provision of Part 11A the question is about` `the person is, or there are reasonable grounds to believe the person is, a registrable controller of the company or foreign company` `this Part applies to that company or foreign company under section 386AA(1)`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AB "controller" the person is a controller of the company or foreign company` (sgn-application.l4).
@export Under section 386AB, is the person a controller of the company or foreign company?
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
      `the person is a legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a legal entity (a body corporate, a foreign company, or another entity with legal personality)?
      `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning?
      `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AB, is the person a controller of the company or foreign company` IS
    `s 386AB "controller" the person is a controller of the company or foreign company` `the person is an individual` `the person is a legal entity` `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AC the controller is registrable` (sgn-application.l4).
@export Under section 386AC, is the person a registrable controller of the company or foreign company?
GIVEN `the person is a controller of the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a controller of the company or foreign company?
      `the person's interest or control is only through one or more other controllers of the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold the significant interest or control only through one or more other controllers of the company or foreign company?
      `the person is a controller of each of those other controllers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a controller of each of those other controllers?
      `the kind of those other controllers` IS A `s 386AC(c) kind of controller B` @desc Which kind of controller is each of those other controllers (section 386AC(c))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AC, is the person a registrable controller of the company or foreign company` IS
    `s 386AC the controller is registrable` `the person is a controller of the company or foreign company` `the person's interest or control is only through one or more other controllers of the company or foreign company` `the person is a controller of each of those other controllers` (IF `the person's interest or control is only through one or more other controllers of the company or foreign company` THEN (LIST `the kind of those other controllers`) ELSE EMPTY)

-- Layer 1: `s 386AB "member of the public" the person is a member of the public` (sgn-application.l4).
@export Under section 386AB, is the person a member of the public for the purposes of Part 11A?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company acting in the member's capacity as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the company, acting as a member?
      `the person is a member of the foreign company acting in the member's capacity as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the foreign company, acting as a member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AB, is the person a member of the public for the purposes of Part 11A` IS
    `s 386AB "member of the public" the person is a member of the public` `the person is a member of the company acting in the member's capacity as such` `the person is a member of the foreign company acting in the member's capacity as such`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AD(1) the evidence is evidence that the corporation had that state of mind` (sgn-evidence.l4).
@export Under section 386AD(1), is the evidence evidence that the corporation had that state of mind?
GIVEN `the proceeding is a proceeding for an offence under Part 11A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one for an offence under Part 11A?
      `it is necessary to prove the state of mind of the corporation in relation to a particular conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it necessary, in the proceeding, to prove the state of mind of the corporation in relation to a particular conduct?
      `the kind of person who engaged in the conduct` IS A `s 386AD kind of person who engaged in the conduct` @desc Was the person who engaged in the conduct an officer, an employee, an agent, or some other person?
      `the person engaged in that conduct within the scope of the person's actual or apparent authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person engage in that conduct within the scope of the person's actual or apparent authority?
      `the person had that state of mind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person have that state of mind?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AD(1), is the evidence evidence that the corporation had that state of mind` IS
    `s 386AD(1) the evidence is evidence that the corporation had that state of mind` `the proceeding is a proceeding for an offence under Part 11A` `it is necessary to prove the state of mind of the corporation in relation to a particular conduct` `the kind of person who engaged in the conduct` `the person engaged in that conduct within the scope of the person's actual or apparent authority` `the person had that state of mind`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AE(1) the information or document is subject to legal privilege` (sgn-evidence.l4).
@export Under section 386AE(1), is the information or document subject to legal privilege?
GIVEN `the kind of information or document` IS A `s 386AE(1) kind of information or document` @desc Which kind of communication, information or document is it (section 386AE(1)(a) to (e))?
      `it is made in connection with a lawyer giving legal advice to the client, or a legal counsel giving legal advice to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made in connection with a lawyer giving legal advice to the client, or a legal counsel giving legal advice to the employer?
      `it is made in connection with, and for the purposes of, legal proceedings (including anticipated or pending proceedings) in which the client or employer is or may be, or was or might have been, a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made in connection with, and for the purposes of, legal proceedings (including anticipated or pending proceedings) in which the client or employer is or may be, or was or might have been, a party?
      `it is made, prepared or held with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made, prepared or held with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AE(1), is the information or document subject to legal privilege` IS
    `s 386AE(1) the information or document is subject to legal privilege` `the kind of information or document` `it is made in connection with a lawyer giving legal advice to the client, or a legal counsel giving legal advice to the employer` `it is made in connection with, and for the purposes of, legal proceedings (including anticipated or pending proceedings) in which the client or employer is or may be, or was or might have been, a party` `it is made, prepared or held with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose`

§ `The register of controllers (ss 386AF and 386AFA)`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the day by which the company must have kept its register` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3), by what day must the company have kept its register of registrable controllers?
GIVEN `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company not a company to which Part 11A applied, and did it later become one?
      `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date did Part 11A apply (or apply again) to the company?
      `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company incorporated?
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 4 of the Companies and Limited Liability Partnerships (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2024 come into operation?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3), by what day must the company have kept its register of registrable controllers` IS
    `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the day by which the company must have kept its register` `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the company` `the date the company was incorporated` `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the company has kept its register in time` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3), has the company kept its register of registrable controllers in time?
GIVEN `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company not a company to which Part 11A applied, and did it later become one?
      `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date did Part 11A apply (or apply again) to the company?
      `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company incorporated?
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 4 of the Companies and Limited Liability Partnerships (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2024 come into operation?
      `the company has kept its register of registrable controllers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company kept its register of registrable controllers?
      `the day the company started to keep its register` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company start to keep its register (any date if it has not)?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3), has the company kept its register of registrable controllers in time` IS
    `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the company has kept its register in time` `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the company` `the date the company was incorporated` `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` `the company has kept its register of registrable controllers` `the day the company started to keep its register` `the date asked`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6), by what day must the foreign company have kept its register of registrable controllers?
GIVEN `the foreign company was not a foreign company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the foreign company not one to which Part 11A applied, and did it later become one?
      `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the foreign company` IS A DATE @desc On what date did Part 11A apply (or apply again) to the foreign company?
      `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11?
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 4 of the Companies and Limited Liability Partnerships (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2024 come into operation?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6), by what day must the foreign company have kept its register of registrable controllers` IS
    `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` `the foreign company was not a foreign company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the foreign company` `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AF(7) the register is as the subsection requires` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AF(7), is the register as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the register contains the prescribed particulars of the company's or foreign company's registrable individual controllers and registrable corporate controllers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the register contain the prescribed particulars of the registrable individual controllers and registrable corporate controllers?
      `section 386AFA(3) applies to the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company or foreign company know, or have reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller, or know that it has one but cannot identify it (section 386AFA(1))?
      `the register contains the note and prescribed particulars required under section 386AFA(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the register contain the note and the prescribed particulars that section 386AFA(3) requires?
      `a change to the prescribed particulars has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a change occurred to the particulars that the regulations require the register to hold?
      `the register has been updated for that change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the register been updated for that change?
      `the register is kept in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register kept in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AF(7), is the register as the subsection requires` IS
    `s 386AF(7) the register is as the subsection requires` `the register contains the prescribed particulars of the company's or foreign company's registrable individual controllers and registrable corporate controllers` `section 386AFA(3) applies to the company or foreign company` `the register contains the note and prescribed particulars required under section 386AFA(3)` `a change to the prescribed particulars has occurred` `the register has been updated for that change` `the register is kept in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AF(8) the company or foreign company has entered the particulars and updated the register in time and in the prescribed manner` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AF(8), has the company or foreign company entered the particulars and updated its register in time and in the prescribed manner?
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has entered the particulars or updated the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company or foreign company entered the particulars in its register and updated it?
      `the day the company or foreign company entered the particulars or updated the register` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company or foreign company enter the particulars or update the register (any date if it has not)?
      `the day from which the prescribed time runs` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the prescribed time for lodging begin to run?
      `the prescribed time, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the regulation prescribe for this?
      `the particulars were entered or the register was updated in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the particulars entered, or the register updated, in the prescribed manner?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AF(8), has the company or foreign company entered the particulars and updated its register in time and in the prescribed manner` IS
    `s 386AF(8) the company or foreign company has entered the particulars and updated the register in time and in the prescribed manner` `the company or foreign company has entered the particulars or updated the register` `the day the company or foreign company entered the particulars or updated the register` `the day from which the prescribed time runs` `the prescribed time, in days` `the particulars were entered or the register was updated in the prescribed manner` `the date asked`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AF(9) the company or foreign company has done what the subsection requires` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AF(9), has the company or foreign company done what the subsection requires about a controller's particulars?
GIVEN `the controller has confirmed the particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the controller confirmed the particulars to the company or foreign company?
      `the company or foreign company has entered or updated the particulars in its register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company or foreign company entered or updated the controller's particulars in its register?
      `the entry or update carries a note that the particulars have not been confirmed by the controller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the entry or update carry a note that the controller has not confirmed the particulars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AF(9), has the company or foreign company done what the subsection requires about a controller's particulars` IS
    `s 386AF(9) the company or foreign company has done what the subsection requires` `the controller has confirmed the particulars` `the company or foreign company has entered or updated the particulars in its register` `the entry or update carries a note that the particulars have not been confirmed by the controller`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AF(11) the company or foreign company is barred from disclosing the register to the person` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AF(11), is the company or foreign company barred from disclosing the register to the person?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the public?
      `the disclosure or inspection is a requirement or the exercise of a power under section 386AM` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure or inspection one that section 386AM requires or permits (a requirement or the exercise of a power of the Registrar or an officer of the Authority)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AF(11), is the company or foreign company barred from disclosing the register to the person` IS
    `s 386AF(11) the company or foreign company is barred from disclosing the register to the person` `the person is a member of the public` `the disclosure or inspection is a requirement or the exercise of a power under section 386AM`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AF(12) the company is guilty of the offence` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AF(12), is the company guilty of the offence?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to keep its register of registrable controllers by the time section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) or (3) (whichever applies) requires?
      `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with section 386AF(7), (8), (9) or (11) (what its register must hold, entering and updating it, entering a controller's particulars, or not disclosing it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AF(12), is the company guilty of the offence` IS
    `s 386AF(12) the company is guilty of the offence` `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AF(12) the officer of the company is guilty of the offence` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AF(12), is the officer of the company guilty of the offence?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to keep its register of registrable controllers by the time section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) or (3) (whichever applies) requires?
      `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with section 386AF(7), (8), (9) or (11) (what its register must hold, entering and updating it, entering a controller's particulars, or not disclosing it)?
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning (one who knowingly and wilfully commits, authorises or permits the default)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AF(12), is the officer of the company guilty of the offence` IS
    `s 386AF(12) the officer of the company is guilty of the offence` `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AF(12) the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AF(12), what is the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to keep its register of registrable controllers by the time section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) or (3) (whichever applies) requires?
      `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with section 386AF(7), (8), (9) or (11) (what its register must hold, entering and updating it, entering a controller's particulars, or not disclosing it)?
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the company itself?
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning (one who knowingly and wilfully commits, authorises or permits the default)?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 386AF(12), what is the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` IS
    `s 386AF(12) the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AFA(2) the person is taken to be a registrable controller of the company or foreign company for the purposes of this Part` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AFA(2), is the person taken to be a registrable controller of the company or foreign company?
GIVEN `this section applies to the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 386AFA apply to the company or foreign company (it knows it has no registrable controller, or has one it cannot identify)?
      `the person is a director with executive control of the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director with executive control of the company or foreign company?
      `the person is a chief executive officer of the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a chief executive officer of the company or foreign company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AFA(2), is the person taken to be a registrable controller of the company or foreign company` IS
    `s 386AFA(2) the person is taken to be a registrable controller of the company or foreign company for the purposes of this Part` `this section applies to the company or foreign company` `the person is a director with executive control of the company or foreign company` `the person is a chief executive officer of the company or foreign company`

-- Layer 1: `s 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company has entered the matters within the prescribed period` (sgn-register.l4).
@export Under section 386AFA(4), has the company or foreign company entered the matters within the prescribed period?
GIVEN `which of the two cases in section 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company is in` IS A `s 386AFA(4) case` @desc Is the company or foreign company in case (a) (it knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller) or case (b) (it has a registrable controller it has not been able to identify)?
      `the date on which the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company or foreign company know, or first have reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller?
      `the date on which the company or foreign company, having taken the reasonable steps required by section 386AG(1), forms the opinion that it is unable to identify the registrable controller` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company or foreign company, having taken the reasonable steps section 386AG(1) requires, form the opinion that it cannot identify its registrable controller?
      `the company or foreign company has entered the matters mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company or foreign company entered the note and the prescribed particulars in its register of controllers?
      `the day the company or foreign company entered the matters mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company or foreign company enter the note and the prescribed particulars (any date if it has not)?
      `the prescribed period, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the regulation prescribe for this?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386AFA(4), has the company or foreign company entered the matters within the prescribed period` IS
    `s 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company has entered the matters within the prescribed period` `which of the two cases in section 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company is in` `the date on which the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller` `the date on which the company or foreign company, having taken the reasonable steps required by section 386AG(1), forms the opinion that it is unable to identify the registrable controller` `the company or foreign company has entered the matters mentioned in subsection (3)` `the day the company or foreign company entered the matters mentioned in subsection (3)` `the prescribed period, in days` `the date asked`

§ `Notices, and the controller's own duties (ss 386AG to 386AK)`
-- These questions arise only where a notice has been or ought to have been given, or a controller's particulars have changed; the form can ask "Has this happened to you?" first.

-- Layer 1: `s 386AG(2) the company or foreign company must give a notice to the person` (sgn-notices.l4).
@export Under section 386AG(2), must the company or foreign company give a notice to the person?
GIVEN `the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the person is a registrable controller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company or foreign company know, or have reasonable grounds to believe, that the person is a registrable controller?
