§ `Part 12 Division 1: costs, solicitors and shareholders who cannot be found (ss 388 to 390)`

-- s 388(1) the court may require sufficient security to be given for the costs of the defendant  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 388(1), may the Court require sufficient security to be given for the costs of the defendant in an action by a corporation?
GIVEN `the corporation is claimant in an action or other legal proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation the claimant in the action or legal proceeding?
      `it appears by credible testimony that there is reason to believe that the corporation will be unable to pay the costs of the defendant if successful in the defendant's defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there credible testimony giving reason to believe the corporation could not pay the defendant's costs if the defendant succeeds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 388(1), may the Court require sufficient security to be given for the costs of the defendant in an action by a corporation` IS
    `s 388(1) the court may require sufficient security to be given for the costs of the defendant` `the corporation is claimant in an action or other legal proceeding` `it appears by credible testimony that there is reason to believe that the corporation will be unable to pay the costs of the defendant if successful in the defendant's defence`

-- s 388(1) the proceedings are stayed until the security is given  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 388(1), are the proceedings stayed until the security is given?
GIVEN `the court has required sufficient security to be given for the costs of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court required sufficient security for the defendant's costs?
      `the security has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the security been given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 388(1), are the proceedings stayed until the security is given` IS
    `s 388(1) the proceedings are stayed until the security is given` `the court has required sufficient security to be given for the costs of the defendant` `the security has been given`

-- s 388(2) the party must bear the costs of the proceeding  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 388(2), must the party bear the costs of a proceeding before a court under the Act?
GIVEN `the proceeding is a proceeding before a court under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one before a court under the Companies Act?
      `the court has directed, in its discretion, that the party bears the costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court directed, in its discretion, that the party bears the costs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 388(2), must the party bear the costs of a proceeding before a court under the Act` IS
    `s 388(2) the party must bear the costs of the proceeding` `the proceeding is a proceeding before a court under this Act` `the court has directed, in its discretion, that the party bears the costs`

-- s 389 the person may employ a solicitor at the person's own cost  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 389, may I employ a solicitor at my own cost when summoned for examination under Part 9?
GIVEN `the person has been summoned for examination under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been summoned for examination under Part 9 of the Companies Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 389, may I employ a solicitor at my own cost when summoned for examination under Part 9` IS
    `s 389 the person may employ a solicitor at the person's own cost` `the person has been summoned for examination under Part 9`

-- s 389 the solicitor is at liberty to put the question to the person  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 389, is my solicitor at liberty to put a question to me to let me explain or qualify my answers?
GIVEN `the person has been summoned for examination under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been summoned for examination under Part 9 of the Companies Act?
      `the inspector, Court or District Judge considers the question just for the purpose of enabling the person to explain or qualify any answers given by the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the inspector, the Court or the District Judge consider the question just, so that you can explain or qualify your answers?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 389, is my solicitor at liberty to put a question to me to let me explain or qualify my answers` IS
    `s 389 the solicitor is at liberty to put the question to the person` `the person has been summoned for examination under Part 9` `the inspector, Court or District Judge considers the question just for the purpose of enabling the person to explain or qualify any answers given by the person`

-- s 390(1) the company may cause the advertisement to be published  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 390(1), may the company publish an advertisement about a shareholder it cannot find?
GIVEN `the company is unable by the exercise of reasonable diligence to discover the whereabouts of a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company unable, with reasonable diligence, to find out where a shareholder is?
      `the number of years for which the company has been unable to discover the whereabouts of the shareholder` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years has the company been unable to find out where the shareholder is?
      `the advertisement is published in a newspaper circulating in the place shown in the register of members as the address of the shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the advertisement published in a newspaper circulating where the register of members shows the shareholder's address?
      `the advertisement states that the company after the expiration of one month from the date of the advertisement intends to transfer the shares to the Official Receiver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement say the company intends, after one month from its date, to transfer the shares to the Official Receiver?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 390(1), may the company publish an advertisement about a shareholder it cannot find` IS
    `s 390(1) the company may cause the advertisement to be published` `the company is unable by the exercise of reasonable diligence to discover the whereabouts of a shareholder` `the number of years for which the company has been unable to discover the whereabouts of the shareholder` `the advertisement is published in a newspaper circulating in the place shown in the register of members as the address of the shareholder` `the advertisement states that the company after the expiration of one month from the date of the advertisement intends to transfer the shares to the Official Receiver`

-- s 390(2) the company may transfer the shares held by the shareholder to the Official Receiver and execute the transfer for the owner  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 390(2), may the company transfer the shares of a shareholder it cannot find to the Official Receiver?
GIVEN `the date of the advertisement` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the advertisement published?
      `the day on which the company transfers the shares` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the company transfer the shares?
      `the whereabouts of the shareholder remain unknown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the shareholder's whereabouts remain unknown?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 390(2), may the company transfer the shares of a shareholder it cannot find to the Official Receiver` IS
    `s 390(2) the company may transfer the shares held by the shareholder to the Official Receiver and execute the transfer for the owner` `the date of the advertisement` `the day on which the company transfers the shares` `the whereabouts of the shareholder remain unknown`


§ `Part 12 Division 1: relief, irregularities and privilege (ss 391 to 394)`

-- s 391(1) the court may relieve the person either wholly or partly from the person's liability  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 391(1), may the Court relieve me wholly or partly from my liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust?
GIVEN `the person is a person to whom section 391 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer, auditor, expert or other person to whom section 391 applies?
      `the proceedings are proceedings for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust against the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings against you for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust?
      `it appears to the court that the person is or may be liable in respect of the negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Court that you are or may be liable for the negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust?
      `the person has acted honestly and reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act honestly and reasonably?
      `having regard to all the circumstances of the case including those connected with the person's appointment, the person ought fairly to be excused for the negligence, default or breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having regard to all the circumstances, including those of your appointment, ought you fairly to be excused?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 391(1), may the Court relieve me wholly or partly from my liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS
    `s 391(1) the court may relieve the person either wholly or partly from the person's liability` `the person is a person to whom section 391 applies` `the proceedings are proceedings for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust against the person` `it appears to the court that the person is or may be liable in respect of the negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` `the person has acted honestly and reasonably` `having regard to all the circumstances of the case including those connected with the person's appointment, the person ought fairly to be excused for the negligence, default or breach`

-- s 391(2) the person may apply to the Court for relief  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 391(2), may I apply to the Court for relief?
GIVEN `the person is a person to whom section 391 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer, auditor, expert or other person to whom section 391 applies?
      `the person has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against the person in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have reason to fear a claim against you for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 391(2), may I apply to the Court for relief` IS
    `s 391(2) the person may apply to the Court for relief` `the person is a person to whom section 391 applies` `the person has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against the person in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust`

-- s 392(2) the proceeding is not invalidated by reason of the procedural irregularity  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 392(2), is a proceeding not invalidated by reason of a procedural irregularity?
GIVEN `the proceeding under this Act is affected by a procedural irregularity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding under the Companies Act affected by a procedural irregularity?
      `the Court is of the opinion that the irregularity has caused or may cause substantial injustice that cannot be remedied by any order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court of the opinion that the irregularity has caused, or may cause, substantial injustice that no order could remedy?
      `the Court by order declares the proceeding to be invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court by order declared the proceeding invalid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 392(2), is a proceeding not invalidated by reason of a procedural irregularity` IS
    `s 392(2) the proceeding is not invalidated by reason of the procedural irregularity` `the proceeding under this Act is affected by a procedural irregularity` `the Court is of the opinion that the irregularity has caused or may cause substantial injustice that cannot be remedied by any order of the Court` `the Court by order declares the proceeding to be invalid`

-- s 392(2A) the meeting is not invalidated by reason of the technological disruption, malfunction or outage  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 392(2A), is a meeting not invalidated by reason of a technological disruption, malfunction or outage?
GIVEN `the meeting is a meeting to which section 173J(2)(b) or (c) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting one that section 173J(2)(b) or (c) applies to?
      `the meeting is affected by technological disruption, malfunction or outage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the meeting affected by a technological disruption, malfunction or outage?
      `the Court is of the opinion that the technological disruption, malfunction or outage has caused or may cause substantial injustice that cannot be remedied by any order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court of the opinion that the disruption, malfunction or outage has caused, or may cause, substantial injustice that no order could remedy?
      `the Court by order declares the meeting to be invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court by order declared the meeting invalid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 392(2A), is a meeting not invalidated by reason of a technological disruption, malfunction or outage` IS
    `s 392(2A) the meeting is not invalidated by reason of the technological disruption, malfunction or outage` `the meeting is a meeting to which section 173J(2)(b) or (c) applies` `the meeting is affected by technological disruption, malfunction or outage` `the Court is of the opinion that the technological disruption, malfunction or outage has caused or may cause substantial injustice that cannot be remedied by any order of the Court` `the Court by order declares the meeting to be invalid`

-- s 392(3) the meeting or its proceedings are not invalidated by reason only of the omission or non-receipt of notice  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 392(3), are a meeting and its proceedings not invalidated by reason only of the accidental omission of notice or its non-receipt?
GIVEN `the meeting is a meeting held for the purposes of this Act, a meeting notice of which is required to be given in accordance with this Act, or a proceeding at such a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a meeting held for the purposes of the Companies Act, a meeting the Act requires notice of, or a proceeding at one?
      `the invalidity would arise by reason only of the accidental omission to give notice of the meeting or the non-receipt by any person of notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the invalidity arise only because notice was accidentally left out, or someone did not receive it?
      `the Court has declared proceedings at the meeting to be void` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court declared the proceedings at the meeting void?
      `the Court made the declaration on the application of the person concerned, a person entitled to attend the meeting or the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court make that declaration on the application of the person concerned, a person entitled to attend, or the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 392(3), are a meeting and its proceedings not invalidated by reason only of the accidental omission of notice or its non-receipt` IS
    `s 392(3) the meeting or its proceedings are not invalidated by reason only of the omission or non-receipt of notice` `the meeting is a meeting held for the purposes of this Act, a meeting notice of which is required to be given in accordance with this Act, or a proceeding at such a meeting` `the invalidity would arise by reason only of the accidental omission to give notice of the meeting or the non-receipt by any person of notice of the meeting` `the Court has declared proceedings at the meeting to be void` `the Court made the declaration on the application of the person concerned, a person entitled to attend the meeting or the Registrar`

-- s 392(4) the Court may make the order on the application of an interested person  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 392(4), may the Court make an order curing a contravention or failure on the application of an interested person?
GIVEN `the kind of order sought under section 392` IS A `s 392(4) kind of order` @desc What kind of order is sought under section 392?
      `an interested person has applied for the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an interested person applied for the order?
      `the act, matter or thing, or the proceeding, is essentially of a procedural nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act, matter, thing or proceeding essentially procedural?
      `the person or persons concerned in or party to the contravention or failure acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person or persons concerned in the contravention or failure act honestly?
      `it is in the public interest that the order be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in the public interest that the order be made?
      `the person subject to the civil liability concerned acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person subject to the civil liability act honestly?
