GIVEN `the Court has power under section 409A to grant an injunction restraining a person from engaging in particular conduct, or requiring a person to do a particular act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Court have power under section 409A to grant an injunction restraining conduct or requiring an act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 409A(8), may the Court order a person to pay damages to any other person, in addition to or in substitution for the injunction` IS
    `s 409A(8) the Court may order the person to pay damages to any other person, in addition to or in substitution for the injunction` `the Court has power under section 409A to grant an injunction restraining a person from engaging in particular conduct, or requiring a person to do a particular act or thing`

-- s 409B(1) the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence  [sgo-penalties.l4]
@export Under section 409B(1), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence?
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence prescribed as a compoundable offence?
      `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you reasonably suspected of having committed the offence?
      `the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine prescribed for the offence, in Singapore dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 409B(1), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence` IS
    `s 409B(1) the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence` `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence` `the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence, in Singapore dollars`

-- s 409B(2) the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence that has ceased to be compoundable  [sgo-penalties.l4]
@export Under section 409B(2), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound an offence that has ceased to be compoundable?
GIVEN `the offence was compoundable under this Act at the time the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence compoundable under the Act when it was committed?
      `the offence has ceased to be so compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the offence since ceased to be compoundable?
      `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you reasonably suspected of having committed the offence?
      `the maximum fine that was prescribed for the offence at the time it was committed, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the maximum fine prescribed for the offence when it was committed, in Singapore dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 409B(2), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound an offence that has ceased to be compoundable` IS
    `s 409B(2) the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence that has ceased to be compoundable` `the offence was compoundable under this Act at the time the offence was committed` `the offence has ceased to be so compoundable` `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence` `the maximum fine that was prescribed for the offence at the time it was committed, in Singapore dollars`

-- s 409B(3) no further proceedings may be taken against the person in respect of the offence  [sgo-penalties.l4]
@export Under section 409B(3), may no further proceedings be taken against me in respect of the offence once I have paid the sum?
GIVEN `the person has paid the sum of money referred to in section 409B(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the sum of money referred to in section 409B(1) or (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 409B(3), may no further proceedings be taken against me in respect of the offence once I have paid the sum` IS
    `s 409B(3) no further proceedings may be taken against the person in respect of the offence` `the person has paid the sum of money referred to in section 409B(1) or (2)`

-- s 409C(1) the party may appeal to the Court against the act or decision  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 409C(1), may I appeal to the Court against the Registrar's act or decision?
GIVEN `the party is aggrieved by an act or a decision of the Registrar under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aggrieved by an act or decision of the Registrar under the Companies Act?
      `a provision in the nature of an appeal or a review is expressly provided in this Act in respect of the act or decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Companies Act expressly provide an appeal or review of the act or decision?
      `the act or decision is declared by this Act to be conclusive or final, or is embodied in a document declared by this Act to be conclusive evidence of an act, matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act declare the act or decision conclusive or final, or is it embodied in a document the Act declares conclusive evidence?
      `the date of the act or decision` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the act or decision made?
      `the date on which the appeal is brought` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the appeal brought?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 409C(1), may I appeal to the Court against the Registrar's act or decision` IS
    `s 409C(1) the party may appeal to the Court against the act or decision` `the party is aggrieved by an act or a decision of the Registrar under this Act` `a provision in the nature of an appeal or a review is expressly provided in this Act in respect of the act or decision` `the act or decision is declared by this Act to be conclusive or final, or is embodied in a document declared by this Act to be conclusive evidence of an act, matter or thing` `the date of the act or decision` `the date on which the appeal is brought`

-- s 409C(3) section 409C does not apply to the act or decision of the Registrar  [sgo-court.l4]
@export Under section 409C(3), does section 409C not apply to the act or decision of the Registrar?
GIVEN `a provision in the nature of an appeal or a review is expressly provided in this Act in respect of the act or decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Companies Act expressly provide an appeal or review of the act or decision?
      `the act or decision is declared by this Act to be conclusive or final, or is embodied in a document declared by this Act to be conclusive evidence of an act, matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act declare the act or decision conclusive or final, or is it embodied in a document the Act declares conclusive evidence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 409C(3), does section 409C not apply to the act or decision of the Registrar` IS
    `s 409C(3) section 409C does not apply to the act or decision of the Registrar` `a provision in the nature of an appeal or a review is expressly provided in this Act in respect of the act or decision` `the act or decision is declared by this Act to be conclusive or final, or is embodied in a document declared by this Act to be conclusive evidence of an act, matter or thing`
